  ('prov-4-18', 'alma-32-35', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma teaches that faith nurtured by the word of God grows into perfect knowledge and light, paralleling the progressive brightening of the just person''s path in Proverbs 4:18 as a metaphor for spiritual maturation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.314Z'),
  ('prov-8-24', 'gen-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:2 describes the primordial ''deep'' (tehom) and waters before creation was ordered, directly corresponding to the ''depths'' and ''fountains abounding with water'' in Proverbs 8:24 that did not yet exist when Wisdom was brought forth.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.314Z'),
  ('prov-8-26', 'gen-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Proverbs 8:26''s explicit statement that God had ''not yet made the earth, nor the fields'' directly alludes to the pre-creation state described in Genesis 1:1, anchoring Wisdom''s existence to the moment before the foundational creative act.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.314Z'),
  ('prov-8-27', 'gen-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The phrase ''upon the face of the depth'' (tehom) directly echoes Genesis 1:2''s ''darkness was upon the face of the deep,'' anchoring Wisdom''s presence to the specific moment of primordial creation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.314Z'),
  ('ps-102-25', 'gen-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The psalmist''s declaration that God laid the foundation of the earth and made the heavens directly alludes to the creation account of Genesis 1:1.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-14', 'gen-1-29', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:29 records God giving every herb and fruit-bearing tree to humanity for food, which the psalmist alludes to in describing God causing grass for cattle and herbs for the service of man to bring forth food from the earth.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-14', 'gen-1-30', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:30 specifically assigns green herbs as food for cattle and every beast, directly corresponding to the psalmist''s statement that God causes grass to grow for the cattle as part of His providential design.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-19', 'gen-1-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:14 records God appointing the lights in the heavens for seasons and signs, which the Psalmist directly echoes by stating He appointed the moon for seasons and the sun its course.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-20', 'gen-1-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s act of calling darkness ''night'' in Genesis 1:5 is presupposed in the Psalmist''s statement that God ''makest darkness, and it is night,'' attributing the nightly darkness directly to divine creative action.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-22', 'gen-1-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s establishment of day and night in Genesis 1 provides the foundational order that Psalm 104:22 illustrates through the behavior of creatures governed by the rising sun.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-25', 'gen-1-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:21 records God creating ''great whales and every living creature that moveth'' in the sea, which Psalm 104:25 alludes to in describing ''things creeping innumerable, both small and great beasts'' in the wide sea.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-30', 'gen-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:2 describes the Spirit of God moving over the face of the waters at creation, and Psalm 104:30 alludes to this same creative act — ''Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created'' — framing ongoing renewal as a continuation of original creation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-31', 'gen-1-31', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:31 records God seeing everything He had made and pronouncing it ''very good,'' which Psalm 104:31 alludes to when it says ''the Lord shall rejoice in his works,'' reflecting the same divine delight in creation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-104-6', 'gen-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe the primordial state of creation when waters covered everything, with the psalm''s ''the waters stood above the mountains'' elaborating the same formless, water-covered earth of Genesis 1:2.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.514Z'),
  ('ps-107-38', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s original blessing of ''be fruitful and multiply'' is directly echoed in the Psalm''s statement that God ''blesseth them so that they are multiplied greatly,'' presenting human multiplication as a continuation of the creation blessing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.729Z'),
  ('ps-115-15', '1-ne-3-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.961Z'),
  ('ps-115-16', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s grant of the earth to the children of men alludes to the dominion mandate in Genesis, where God gives humanity stewardship over the earth He created.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:11.961Z'),
  ('ps-12-6', '1-ne-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi''s emphasis on obtaining the brass plates so scripture would be preserved pure connects to the conviction of Ps 12:6 that God''s words, like silver refined seven times, are incorruptible and worth preserving at all cost.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.174Z'),
  ('ps-121-2', 'gen-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The phrase ''made heaven and earth'' directly echoes Genesis 1:1''s declaration of God as Creator, grounding the psalmist''s confidence in divine help on God''s power as maker of all things.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-124-8', 'gen-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The description of the Lord as the one ''who made heaven and earth'' directly alludes to the creation account of Genesis 1:1, establishing God''s sovereign authority as the foundation for His saving help.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-134-3', 'gen-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The description of the Lord as the one ''that made heaven and earth'' echoes the creation language of Genesis 1:1, grounding the blessing''s authority in the Creator''s sovereign power over all things.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-136-25', 'gen-1-29', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s original provision of food to ''every living thing'' at creation underlies the claim that He ''giveth food to all flesh,'' connecting creational providence to ongoing divine care.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-136-6', 'gen-1-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:9 records God gathering the waters so dry land appears, the precise cosmogonic act—earth separated above the waters—that Psalm 136:6 commemorates in its praise of the Creator.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-136-7', 'gen-1-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:16 records God making ''two great lights'' — the sun to rule the day and the moon to rule the night — which Psalm 136:7 directly commemorates as an act of enduring mercy.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-136-8', 'gen-1-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:16 specifically states the greater light ''to rule the day,'' and Psalm 136:8 repeats this exact function (''the sun to rule by day''), citing creation as evidence of God''s enduring mercy.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-136-9', 'gen-1-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:16 states God made ''the lesser light to rule the night: he made the stars also,'' which Psalm 136:9 recites verbatim in function (''the moon and stars to rule by night'') as ongoing proof of divine mercy.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.479Z'),
  ('ps-138-3', 'enos-1-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.708Z'),
  ('ps-139-14', 'gen-1-27', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Being ''fearfully and wonderfully made'' grounds in the Genesis declaration that humanity was made in the image of God, establishing the theological basis for the psalmist''s awe at the human body.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.708Z'),
  ('ps-145-16', 'gen-1-29', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s provision of every herb and fruit for food in Genesis 1:29 is the primordial act behind the ongoing reality this verse describes — God opening His hand to satisfy the desire of every living thing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.708Z'),
  ('ps-148-10', 'gen-1-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:24 categorizes God''s terrestrial creatures as cattle, creeping things, and beasts — the exact triad Psalm 148:10 summons to praise, grounding the call to worship in the original creation account.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.940Z'),
  ('ps-148-4', 'gen-1-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The phrase ''waters that be above the heavens'' directly alludes to the waters above the firmament described in the creation account, anchoring the praise call in the cosmology of Genesis.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.940Z'),
  ('ps-148-5', 'gen-1-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The clause ''he commanded, and they were created'' directly echoes the pattern of Genesis 1 where God speaks and creation immediately comes into existence (''And God said… and it was so'').","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.940Z'),
  ('ps-148-7', 'gen-1-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages reference ''great dragons'' (sea creatures/whales) as creations of God, with Psalm 148:7 calling them to praise the same Creator who made them in Genesis 1:21.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.940Z'),
  ('ps-17-1', 'alma-33-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s quotation of Zenos'' prayer emphasizes that God hears prayer offered with sincerity and a non-feigned heart, directly paralleling the psalmist''s assertion that his prayer ''goeth not out of feigned lips.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:02:12.940Z'),
