  ('alma-33-10', 'ps-31-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages affirm that God hears the afflicted person who is despised and cast off, and that enemies are delivered into God''s hands for destruction.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', '2-ne-2-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages affirm that there is no mercy unto mankind except through the merits and suffering of the Son of God, connecting the turning away of judgment to Christ''s atonement.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', 'alma-33-13', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma 33:11 contains Zenos''s prayer crediting the Son for God''s mercy, and Alma 33:13 directly identifies this phrase — ''thou hast turned away thy judgments because of thy Son'' — as Zenos''s words, confirming the quotation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"quotation"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', 'alma-36-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages link personal affliction with divine mercy mediated through Christ, with the speaker affirming that God''s deliverance in times of suffering is rooted in the Son.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', 'ex-34-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', 'mosiah-3-17', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages teach that salvation and mercy from God come specifically because of His Son, identifying Christ as the sole mediating cause of God''s merciful judgment toward mankind.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-11', 'ps-6-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages record a prayer of one in affliction who asserts that God has heard his weeping and supplication, resulting in the departure of enemies and the turning away of divine wrath.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-12', 'alma-33-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses frame Alma''s sermon around the authority of written scripture, with Alma directing the Zoramites to believe the words of the ancient prophets as a basis for faith in the Son.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-12', 'isa-7-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-12', 'jacob-7-10', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages use the rhetorical move of appealing to whether the audience has actually read the scriptures as the foundation for an argument about belief in Christ.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-12', 'john-5-39', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages urge the audience to search the scriptures, noting that those very scriptures testify of the Son of God and therefore form the evidentiary basis for belief in Him.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-13', 'alma-33-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma explicitly attributes the phrase ''thou hast turned away thy judgments because of thy Son'' to Zenos, identifying 33:11 as drawn from Zenos''s prayer and thereby anchoring both verses in that prophetic source.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"quotation"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-13', 'alma-34-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages rely on the testimony of Zenos and other ancient prophets to establish before the Zoramites that faith in and mercy through the Son of God is a doctrine taught in their own scriptures.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-14', 'jacob-7-10', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses pose the direct rhetorical question of whether the audience has read the scriptures, using that reading — or failure to read — as the test of whether disbelief in Christ is intellectually defensible.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-14', 'john-5-39', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-14', 'john-5-46', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages argue that if the audience truly believed the scriptures they claim to revere, they would necessarily believe in the Son of God, since the scriptures themselves testify of Him.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-14', 'mosiah-13-33', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages argue that all the prophets and scriptures from the beginning have testified of Christ, making disbelief in the Son of God a willful rejection of the entire scriptural witness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-15', '3-ne-10-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"3 Nephi 10:16 likewise appeals to the testimonies of the prophets Zenos and Zenock as witnesses of Christ''s suffering and redemption, reinforcing Alma''s point that multiple ancient voices spoke of the Son.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-15', 'alma-33-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma similarly introduces Zenos as a prophet who testified of prayer and worship, establishing the pattern of citing multiple ancient prophets as witnesses of Christ.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-15', 'hel-8-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Helaman 8:20 also names Zenock alongside other prophets as one who testified of Christ, confirming the same pairing of witnesses Alma references here.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
