  ('alma-33-16', 'jacob-6-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob similarly warns his people that God''s anger is kindled when they reject His mercies and the atonement offered through His Son, mirroring Zenock''s rebuke of an uncomprehending people.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-16', 'mosiah-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages ground God''s mercies toward humanity specifically in the atoning work of His Son, with the people''s failure to understand those mercies forming the central spiritual problem.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-17', 'alma-14-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages address the martyrdom of righteous witnesses whose blood testifies against the wicked, showing that rejecting prophetic testimony of Christ brings divine judgment.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-17', 'hel-8-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Helaman 8:19 explicitly states that Zenock was killed because of the plainness of his testimony of Christ, directly corroborating Alma''s account that Zenock was stoned to death for his words.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-17', 'mark-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-17', 'matt-23-37', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus laments that Jerusalem kills and stones the prophets sent to her, directly echoing the pattern Alma identifies wherein ancient prophets testifying of the Son were put to death by their own people.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-18', 'jacob-4-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob declares that all the prophets had hope in Christ and spoke of His atonement, supporting Alma''s broader claim that testimony of the Son of God was not limited to one or two prophetic voices.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-18', 'mark-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-18', 'mosiah-13-33', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Abinadi similarly argues that all the prophets since the world began have spoken concerning the coming of Christ, directly reinforcing Alma''s point that the Son was witnessed by many more than Zenos and Zenock.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', '1-ne-17-41', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi references the same episode of the brass serpent and laments that because the miracle was simple the people hardened their hearts and would not look, paralleling Alma''s contrast between those who did look and live and those who refused.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'deut-18-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'hel-8-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi (son of Helaman) likewise cites Moses raising the serpent as a type of Christ being lifted up, using the identical typological argument and the same phrase about looking and living.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'hosea-11-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'john-3-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus directly invokes the same Mosaic type, saying ''As Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of Man be lifted up,'' confirming the typological link Alma draws between the serpent and Christ''s crucifixion.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'num-21-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Numbers 21:8 records the actual event of Moses lifting up the brass serpent in the wilderness so that all who looked upon it would live, which Alma here identifies as a type of Christ.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-19', 'num-21-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-2', 'acts-17-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Paul''s declaration that God does not dwell in temples made with hands and cannot be confined to a location parallels Alma''s argument that worship is not dependent on access to a synagogue building.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-2', 'john-4-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages explicitly correct the false assumption that worship is geographically or institutionally restricted — Jesus tells the Samaritan woman that worship is not bound to a mountain or temple, just as Alma tells the Zoramites worship is not bound to a synagogue.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-2', 'john-5-39', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-20', '1-ne-17-41', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi recounts the same brass serpent episode, emphasizing that the people perished because the simpleness of the way caused them to harden their hearts and refuse to look.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-20', 'hel-8-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Helaman also references Moses lifting up the serpent in the wilderness as a type of Christ, connecting the act of looking in faith to salvation from spiritual death.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-20', 'john-12-40', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe people whose hardened hearts prevent them from seeing and being healed, connecting spiritual blindness to willful unbelief rather than ignorance.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-20', 'mark-3-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-20', 'num-21-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma references the brass serpent incident where Israelites died because they would not look at Moses''s serpent, directly paralleling the hardness of heart that prevented looking and caused perishing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-21', '2-ne-26-33', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages underscore that God''s invitation to be healed and saved is open to all, and the only barrier is the individual''s own slothfulness or hardness of heart in refusing to act.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-21', 'heb-3-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-21', 'jacob-6-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob similarly pleads with his people not to harden their hearts and reject the easiness of the way, using near-identical rhetorical appeal to shame willful unbelief.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-21', 'num-21-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The phrase ''cast about your eyes'' directly echoes the action required of Israelites who were to look upon the brazen serpent to be healed of snakebite, the foundational type Alma is invoking.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-22', '2-cor-11-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-22', '2-ne-9-22', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob teaches that Christ''s death and resurrection will bring all mankind before God for judgment, using the same sequence — atonement, resurrection, judgment — that Alma outlines here.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-22', 'alma-11-44', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses link the resurrection directly to the final judgment, affirming that all men will stand before God to be judged according to their works at the last day.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-22', 'john-3-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus identifies himself as the antitype of the lifted-up serpent, directly fulfilling the typology Alma is expounding — the Son of God who comes to redeem through suffering, death, and resurrection.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-22', 'mosiah-3-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages declare that the Son of God will come, suffer, die, and rise again to atone for sins and bring about resurrection, sharing nearly identical doctrinal content on Christ''s redemptive mission.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-23', 'alma-32-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s earlier parable of the seed, where a planted word begins to swell and grow into a tree of everlasting life, is directly recalled by the phrase ''plant this word in your hearts'' and ''become a tree springing up unto everlasting life.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-23', 'alma-36-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s personal testimony of the joy he felt through the Son of God after his conversion provides the experiential basis for his promise here that the joy of Christ will lighten the people''s burdens.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-23', 'matt-11-30', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Christ''s promise that his yoke is easy and his burden light is echoed in Alma''s benediction that God may grant the people''s burdens to be light through the joy of his Son.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-3', 'alma-34-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both Alma and Amulek cite the prophet Zenos by name as a scriptural authority, identifying him as a prophet of old whose testimony supports their gospel teachings to the Zoramites.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-3', 'jacob-5-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob also quotes Zenos extensively by name, confirming that Zenos was a recognized prophetic source on the brass plates whose words carried scriptural authority in Nephite tradition.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-4', '1-kgs-8-47', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-4', 'ps-55-17', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe crying out to God in isolated or afflicted circumstances — the wilderness and distress — and affirming that God hears such prayers, establishing the same pattern of solitary prayer met with divine response.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-5', 'ex-34-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-5', 'ps-34-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe a poor or humble man crying out to God in distress and being heard — Psalm 34:6 reads ''This poor man cried, and the Lord heard him,'' directly paralleling Zenos''s testimony of crying unto God and being heard.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-5', 'ps-55-17', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both describe crying unto God in prayer at multiple times and occasions, with confidence that God hears — Psalm 55:17 says ''Evening, and morning, and at noon, will I pray, and cry aloud: and he shall hear my voice,'' mirroring Zenos''s cry in the field.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-6', 'matt-6-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages connect prayer in one''s house or private space with being heard by God — Matthew 6:6 instructs entering one''s closet to pray to the Father ''in secret,'' and Zenos testifies of turning to his house and being heard in his prayer.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-8', '3-ne-13-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s citation of Zenos''s words ''to be heard of thee and not of men'' closely parallels Christ''s teaching in 3 Nephi 13:6 that prayers should not be ''as the hypocrites do...that they may be seen of men,'' indicating a shared doctrinal standard on authentic prayer.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"quotation"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-8', 'ex-34-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-8', 'matt-6-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages draw a sharp contrast between praying to be heard of men versus praying to be heard of God — Matthew 6:5 warns against hypocrites who ''pray standing in the synagogues...that they may be seen of men,'' exactly the contrast Zenos articulates.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-8', 'ps-65-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Psalm 65:2 declares ''O thou that hearest prayer, unto thee shall all flesh come,'' paralleling Zenos''s testimony that God is merciful to His children when they cry unto Him and that He will hear them.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-9', 'alma-33-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"These two consecutive verses create an intentional contrast: verse 8 highlights prayer heard ''not of men'' in private, while verse 9 affirms God also hears cries within congregations, together establishing that God''s mercy is not limited by the setting of prayer.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-33-9', 'ex-34-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z')
insert into lumen.edges (from_id, to_id, rel_type, collection_id, metadata, source, created_at) values
  ('alma-33-9', 'ps-22-22', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe praising or crying unto God in the midst of a congregation — Psalm 22:22 reads ''in the midst of the congregation will I praise thee,'' mirroring Zenos''s testimony of being heard by God even within public assemblies.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-2', 'alma-33-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Amulek picks up directly where Alma left off, referencing ''the things which have been spoken concerning the coming of Christ'' taught by ''us,'' grounding verse 2 in the preceding sermon as a continuous teaching unit.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-3', 'alma-32-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Amulek''s reference to Alma having ''exhorted you unto faith and to patience'' directly echoes Alma''s own definition of faith in 32:21, where faith is described as hoping for things not seen — showing Amulek building on Alma''s foundational exhortation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-3', 'alma-32-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma 32:6 describes the Zoramites coming to Alma because of their afflictions, and verse 3 directly references this same historical moment — ''as ye have desired of my beloved brother'' on account of ''your afflictions'' — linking Amulek''s opening to Alma''s preceding ministry.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-4', 'alma-32-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Amulek directly echoes Alma''s own words from 32:28, where Alma invites his hearers to ''plant'' the word like a seed in their hearts and ''try the experiment'' of its goodness — Amulek is recapping and affirming Alma''s seed-planting metaphor verbatim.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"quotation"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-4', 'alma-32-41', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s seed sermon culminates in the invitation to nourish the planted word ''with great diligence,'' and Amulek''s call to ''plant the word in your hearts'' in verse 4 closes the loop, establishing that Amulek''s sermon is the doctrinal payoff to Alma''s horticultural metaphor.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-5', 'alma-33-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma 33:2 records the same ''great question'' the Zoramites posed — how and where to worship — and Amulek in verse 5 reframes and sharpens that question specifically around whether the word (salvation) is in the Son of God, revealing the theological core behind their original inquiry.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-6', 'alma-33-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Amulek''s claim that Alma ''proved unto you, in many instances, that the word is in Christ unto salvation'' refers back to Alma''s citations of Zenos, Zenock, and Moses in Alma 33, which together constituted that multi-instance proof that Christ is the source of salvation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-34-7', 'alma-33-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma 33:3 is the immediate context where Alma quotes Zenos on prayer and redemption, which Amulek references here as the words his brother Alma has just cited.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-36-19', 'enos-1-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both Enos and Alma experience the immediate lifting of guilt the moment God responds to their cry for mercy — Enos hears ''thy sins are forgiven thee'' and his guilt is swept away, paralleling Alma''s instant relief when he calls upon Christ.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:19.153Z'),
  ('alma-37-19', 'enos-1-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos received a promise that the Nephite records would be preserved and brought to the Lamanites for their restoration to truth; Alma 37:19 identifies this very purpose as having been fulfilled in the Lamanite conversions, completing Enos''s prophetic hope.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:20.200Z'),
  ('alma-37-46', 'alma-33-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Earlier in the same discourse Alma uses the brass serpent as a type of Christ, emphasizing that because of the simplicity of the sign many perished—directly anticipating the warning here against slothfulness over the easiness of the way.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:20.200Z'),
  ('alma-37-8', 'enos-1-13', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos records his prayer for the preservation of the Nephite records so they might ''bring them unto salvation,'' expressing the same salvific purpose of scripture preservation that Alma articulates here.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:20.200Z'),
  ('alma-38-8', 'enos-1-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both Alma and Enos describe a prolonged period of anguish over their sins followed by crying unto the Lord and receiving a remission of sins and peace of soul, with the relief coming specifically in response to direct supplication.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:20.200Z'),
  ('alma-39-13', 'dc-4-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages use the identical tripartite phrase ''mind, might, and strength'' as the standard of wholehearted dedication required in serving God and repenting.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:20.200Z'),
  ('alma-45-11', 'enos-1-10', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos records the Lord''s warning that the Nephites would be destroyed if they fell into transgression, establishing the same conditional destruction pattern Alma now declares has become inevitable.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:21.384Z'),
  ('alma-46-20', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages invoke coming forth ''in the strength of the Lord'' as the operative phrase for covenant faithfulness that enables God''s people to accomplish what is required of them.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:23.125Z'),
  ('alma-46-40', 'gen-1-29', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages affirm that God provided plants from the earth for the benefit and healing of mankind, reflecting divine provision through natural creation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:23.125Z'),
  ('alma-48-19', 'dc-4-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages call those who serve God to engage with their whole heart in bringing souls to repentance through the word, mirroring the description of Helaman and his brethren baptizing ''all men whosoever would hearken.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:23.125Z'),
  ('alma-48-22', 'enos-1-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos similarly records that wars and contentions with the Lamanites never ceased throughout his lifetime, establishing early in the record the same pattern of unrelenting conflict that alma-48-22 confirms continued for many generations.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:23.125Z'),
  ('alma-54-19', '1-ne-3-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Laban threatens Nephi and Laman with death, paralleling Ammoron''s threatenings against Moroni and his people, with both passages showing that the Lord''s servants are not deterred by violent threats from those in power.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:23.888Z'),
  ('alma-58-11', 'enos-1-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe a direct divine communication that grants peace and assurance to the recipient, with God''s voice or Spirit speaking peace specifically in response to the individual''s or group''s faithful pleading.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.498Z'),
  ('alma-6-5', 'alma-32-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages address the universal privilege of hearing the word of God, with Alma''s concern that none be deprived of assembly echoed in his later open-air preaching to the poor and excluded.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.498Z'),
  ('alma-60-34', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages express that keeping God''s commandments is not optional when one has made a covenant to do so, with Moroni''s ''constrained by the covenant I have made'' echoing Nephi''s foundational principle that God prepares a way to fulfill commanded duties.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.498Z'),
  ('alma-61-13', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses reason from the character of God''s commands — He does not command subjection to evil enemies (Alma 61:13) just as He does not command without providing a way (1 Ne. 3:7) — grounding obedience in confidence that God''s directives align with His power to deliver.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.498Z'),
  ('alma-62-41', 'alma-32-13', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma''s teaching that those compelled to be humble by their circumstances can still be blessed connects directly to those in Alma 62:41 who were softened by affliction and humbled themselves, illustrating the same principle of compelled versus voluntary humility.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.981Z'),
  ('alma-8-10', 'enos-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe an individual wrestling before God in mighty prayer, using the specific word ''wrestle'' or its equivalent to convey intense, prolonged spiritual supplication on behalf of others.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.981Z'),
  ('alma-8-11', 'alma-32-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages show the Ammonihahites (or similarly hostile crowds) dismissing a missionary by attacking his institutional authority and labeling his teachings ''foolish traditions,'' using nearly identical rhetorical dismissal language about church and tradition.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:24.981Z'),
