  ('enos-1-13', '1-ne-13-40', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi prophesies that other books would come forth to make known the plain and precious truths to the Lamanites, directly anticipating the covenant Enos receives about preserving Nephite records for that purpose.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-13', '2-ne-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe the prophesied future bringing forth of records to the Lamanites as an instrument of their salvation, with Lehi''s prophecy naming the seer who would accomplish this work.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-13', 'dc-10-46', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The Lord tells Joseph Smith that the Book of Mormon record was preserved specifically to come forth to the Lamanites and convince them of the gospel, fulfilling the exact preservation covenant Enos describes here.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-13', 'dc-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages explicitly state that the Book of Mormon record is to be preserved and brought forth to the Lamanites so that they ''might be brought unto salvation'' and restored to knowledge of their fathers.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-13', 'lev-26-44', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-13', 'morm-5-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Mormon, like Enos, describes preserving the record specifically for the future benefit of the Lamanites, writing that it would ''come unto them'' that they might know the covenants of the Lord.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-14', 'alma-26-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Ammon''s rejoicing that thousands of Lamanites were converted to the Lord contrasts with Enos''s lament that ''our strugglings were vain in restoring them,'' marking the eventual partial fulfillment of Enos''s wrestle.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-14', 'ezra-4-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-14', 'jarom-1-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom uses strikingly similar language, describing the Lamanites seeking to destroy the Nephites and their records, confirming that the Lamanite hostility Enos describes was persistent across generations.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-14', 'morm-6-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Mormon''s act of hiding up all the records in the hill Cumorah directly responds to the centuries-long Lamanite threat Enos identifies here — the sworn destruction of Nephite records — showing the threat was real and the preservation miraculous.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-15', '3-ne-18-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus''s own words in 3 Nephi — ''whatsoever ye shall ask the Father in my name, which is right, believing that ye shall receive, behold it shall be given unto you'' — echo the exact promise Enos says he received, suggesting a consistent divine principle.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-15', 'ezra-4-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-15', 'mosiah-4-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages ground the confidence to ask God in knowledge of His power and willingness, with Enos citing God''s stated promise as the basis for his continued crying in faith.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-16', '2-ne-27-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi''s prophecy that the Lord will bring forth the sealed record ''in mine own due time'' uses identical language to the covenant God makes with Enos, tying both texts to the same divine promise of eventual restoration.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-16', 'alma-37-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma tells his son that the records have been preserved ''according to the purposes of God'' for the convincing of the Lamanites, directly describing the ongoing fulfillment of the covenant God made with Enos.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-16', 'dc-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The Lord''s covenant with Enos to bring the records forth to the Lamanites ''in his own due time'' is identified in D&C 3 as already having been decreed before the Book of Mormon came forth, showing the fulfillment of this specific covenantal promise.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-16', 'deut-4-23', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-17', 'gen-5-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-17', 'morm-9-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Moroni''s declaration that God is a God of covenants who changes not underpins the reason Enos knew his soul could rest — because God''s covenantal word is immutable and trustworthy.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-17', 'mosiah-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The rest Enos''s soul experiences after receiving God''s covenant reflects the peace that comes through yielding to God''s will, a principle King Benjamin identifies as central to becoming a saint through the atonement.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-18', '2-ne-3-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Lehi blesses his son Joseph by invoking the promises made to the fathers, reflecting the same principle Enos 1:18 states—that God honors the faithful petitions of ancestral figures like Lehi and Nephi for their posterity.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-18', 'enos-1-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The Lord''s response to Enos regarding the Nephite records mirrors His earlier response to Enos''s personal prayer, granting requests ''according to faith,'' establishing a consistent pattern of covenant fulfillment based on faith.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-18', 'jarom-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom records that God kept the promises made to the fathers (Lehi, Nephi, Enos) according to their faith, directly fulfilling the Lord''s statement to Enos that ''it shall be done unto them according to their faith.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"prophecy-fulfillment"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-18', 'mosiah-26-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The Lord tells Alma ''blessed art thou'' and grants his petition according to his faith, mirroring the pattern in Enos 1:18 where God honors both the individual''s faith and the faith of prior covenant-makers.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-19', '1-ne-1-18', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Lehi, like Enos, went among the people testifying of things he had heard and seen in his prophetic vision, establishing a recurring Nephite pattern of experiential testimony following divine encounter.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-19', 'alma-36-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma, after his conversion experience, immediately went about preaching what he had seen and heard, paralleling Enos''s pattern of going among the people to testify of his personal encounter with God.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-19', 'gen-5-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-19', 'mosiah-13-26', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Abinadi similarly describes his role as testifying of things he had seen and heard by the Spirit, using nearly identical language of personal witness combined with prophetic proclamation as Enos does in verse 19.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-2', 'alma-22-18', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos describes a ''wrestle before God'' before receiving remission of sins, and the Lamanite king similarly prostrates himself in desperate prayer crying ''I will give away all my sins to know thee''—both passages portray an anguished, whole-soul confrontation with God that precedes the granting of forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-2', 'mosiah-4-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos wrestles before God seeking remission of sins, and the people of King Benjamin similarly ''cry aloud with one voice'' begging for the atoning blood to cleanse them—both passages mark the same moment of penitent crisis that the narrative then records as met by divine forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-20', '2-ne-5-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi prophesied that the Lamanites would become ''an idle people, full of mischief and subtlety,'' and Enos 1:20 records the fulfillment of that description—wild, ferocious, bloodthirsty, feeding on raw meat—using strikingly similar language.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-20', 'alma-17-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The sons of Mosiah undertook missionary work among the Lamanites specifically because prior Nephite efforts (as described in Enos 1:20) had failed, making their mission a deliberate continuation of the labor Enos acknowledged was ''vain'' under previous methods.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-20', 'gen-25-27', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-20', 'jacob-7-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob similarly records that Lamanite hatred was ''fixed'' and their people wild, using the same language of ferocity and fixed enmity that Enos echoes, indicating a continuous generational pattern of conflict.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-20', 'mosiah-10-12', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Zeniff describes the Lamanites as wild, ferocious, and bloodthirsty people full of hatred toward the Nephites, using nearly identical characterizations to Enos 1:20, showing a persistent Nephite witness of Lamanite hostility rooted in ancestral grievances.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-21', '2-ne-5-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi records that after separating from the Lamanites his people tilled the land, raised grain, flocks, and herds—the same agricultural and pastoral activities Enos lists in verse 21, showing generational continuity in Nephite civilization.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-21', 'gen-12-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-21', 'jarom-1-8', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom describes Nephite prosperity in almost identical terms—tilling land, raising grain, cattle, and horses—directly continuing the description Enos gives in verse 21 and confirming the sustained material culture across generations.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-22', '2-ne-25-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi laments the difficulty of persuading the stiffnecked Nephite people to receive spiritual truth, sharing the same frustrated pastoral tone Enos expresses in verse 22 about a people ''hard to understand.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-22', 'ex-32-9', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-22', 'jarom-1-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom also describes the Nephites as a ''stiffnecked people'' requiring harsh preaching to keep them from destruction, using the exact same characterization Enos uses in verse 22 and showing that the spiritual hardness persisted across generations.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-23', '1-kgs-14-30', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-23', '2-ne-9-40', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob declares that ''the righteous fear not'' but that ''great plainness of speech'' is required to cut through hardness, paralleling Enos''s statement that only ''exceedingly great plainness of speech'' could restrain his people from ruin.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-23', 'hel-12-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Helaman 12:3 states that people will not remember God unless they are chastened, directly echoing Enos''s observation that nothing short of harsh preaching and reminders of death and judgment could keep his people from destruction.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-23', 'jacob-2-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob similarly describes the necessity of using ''plainness of speech'' and harsh rebukes to pierce the hearts of a stiff-necked people, reflecting the same preaching strategy Enos describes as the only means to prevent destruction.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-23', 'mosiah-4-30', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages emphasize the need to continually keep the people in remembrance of judgment and the power of God so they do not fall into destruction, treating constant spiritual vigilance as essential to survival.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-24', '1-kgs-14-30', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-24', 'jarom-1-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom records the same ongoing pattern of wars and contentions between Nephites and Lamanites during his generation, confirming the continuous conflict Enos witnessed and establishing it as a recurring historical thread in the small plates.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-25', 'jarom-1-13', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jarom similarly notes the passing of years from Lehi''s departure as a chronological marker, continuing the same temporal reckoning Enos uses here to anchor the narrative in historical time.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-25', 'judg-15-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-26', '1-cor-9-16', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-26', '2-ne-25-26', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both Nephi and Enos declare that they preach and prophesy of Christ according to truth, with Nephi explicitly saying ''we talk of Christ, we preach of Christ,'' mirroring Enos''s statement that he declared ''the word according to the truth which is in Christ.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-26', '2-tim-4-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Paul''s farewell declaration ''I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith'' closely parallels Enos''s closing testimony that he has declared the word in all his days and rejoiced in it, both being end-of-life affirmations of faithful ministry.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-27', '1-cor-15-53', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos''s expression ''when my mortal shall put on immortality'' echoes the specific Pauline phrase in 1 Corinthians 15:53, ''this mortal must put on immortality,'' signaling a shared doctrinal vocabulary about the resurrection.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-27', '2-ne-9-18', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jacob prophesies that the righteous ''shall have a perfect knowledge of their enjoyment, and their righteousness'' and will ''see his face with pleasure,'' language strikingly close to Enos''s anticipation of standing before the Redeemer and seeing ''his face with pleasure.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-27', 'alma-40-12', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma describes the state of the righteous after death as being ''received into a state of happiness, which is called paradise, a state of rest,'' directly paralleling Enos''s confident declaration that he goes ''to the place of my rest'' with his Redeemer.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-27', 'matt-25-34', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos directly quotes or closely echoes the language of Matthew 25:34 — ''Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you'' — in the words he anticipates hearing from his Redeemer: ''Come unto me, ye blessed, there is a place prepared for you.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"quotation"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-27', 'ps-65-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-3', '2-ne-4-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi similarly describes pondering his father Lehi''s words in his heart, establishing a pattern of children being shaped by parental teachings about eternal things.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-3', 'alma-36-17', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma the Younger likewise recalls his father''s words about Jesus Christ sinking into his memory during his own crisis of soul, mirroring Enos''s experience of a father''s teachings returning at a critical spiritual moment.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-4', 'alma-22-18', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"King Lamoni''s father similarly cries out with his whole soul in extended, desperate prayer for forgiveness and spiritual knowledge, using nearly identical language of crying mightily unto God.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-4', 'luke-18-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus''s parable instructs men to ''pray and not faint,'' and Enos''s all-day, all-night prayer is a literal embodiment of that persistent, unwearying supplication.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-4', 'mosiah-27-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The angel''s appearance to Alma the Younger is attributed to the ''prayers of his people'' offered with faith, paralleling Enos''s persistent vocal prayer that ''reached the heavens'' and received divine response.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-4', 'ps-138-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-4', 'ps-42-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The Psalmist''s declaration ''my soul thirsteth for God'' directly parallels Enos''s statement that ''my soul hungered,'' both using physical appetite as a metaphor for intense spiritual longing that drives urgent prayer.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-5', 'luke-14-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-5', 'luke-5-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-5', 'matt-9-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Jesus tells the man sick of palsy ''thy sins be forgiven thee,'' using the same direct divine declaration of forgiveness spoken personally to an individual, as the voice declares to Enos.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-6', 'alma-36-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma the Younger describes his guilt being ''swept away'' and replaced with joy upon receiving forgiveness, using language nearly identical to Enos''s ''my guilt was swept away,'' suggesting a shared spiritual vocabulary for the remission of sins.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-6', 'ether-3-12', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The brother of Jared''s confidence that ''thou art a God of truth and canst not lie'' is the same doctrinal premise Enos cites—''God could not lie''—as the logical foundation for accepting the divine promise of forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-6', 'gen-5-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-6', 'mosiah-4-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"King Benjamin''s people receive a remission of sins and their guilt is taken away through faith, directly paralleling Enos''s guilt being swept away upon receiving the divine declaration of forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-7', '2-ne-25-23', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Enos''s question ''how is it done?'' anticipates the doctrinal answer Nephi provides—that salvation comes by grace after all we can do—situating Enos''s inquiry within the broader Book of Mormon theology of the mechanism of forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-7', 'acts-9-6', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Paul on the road to Damascus responds to divine intervention with ''Lord, what wilt thou have me to do?''—a structurally identical moment of a newly forgiven person immediately asking a follow-up question of God about the means and implications of what has occurred.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-8', 'alma-22-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Like Enos, Aaron teaches that faith in Christ—specifically in his redemptive work—brings forgiveness and wholeness, using the same doctrinal structure of faith preceding the Savior''s physical manifestation.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-8', 'ether-12-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Moroni''s teaching that faith is not a perfect knowledge, yet produces miracles and divine responses, directly explains the mechanism by which Enos''s unwitnessed faith in Christ was counted as sufficient for forgiveness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-8', 'hel-5-41', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages center on faith in Christ as the operative power that grants spiritual wholeness and forgiveness, even before a direct encounter with the Savior in the flesh.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-8', 'mosiah-3-19', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses frame salvation as contingent on faith in Christ, whose mortal ministry is described as yet future, establishing that pre-mortal faith in the Atonement is efficacious.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', '1-sam-1-15', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', '1-sam-7-5', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', '2-ne-33-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi similarly records that he prays for his people with all diligence and that his heart is enlarged for their welfare, mirroring Enos''s move from personal forgiveness to intercessory concern for the Nephites.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', 'alma-31-26', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma likewise pours out his ''whole soul'' in intercessory prayer for a wayward people, using language nearly identical to Enos''s ''whole soul unto God,'' establishing a recurring Nephite idiom for intense intercession.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', 'jer-42-4', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', 'mosiah-27-14', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The angel''s appearance to Alma the Younger is explicitly credited to the prayers of his father and the church on his behalf, illustrating the same principle Enos acts on—that intercessory prayer for the welfare of brethren can produce divine intervention.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', 'mosiah-28-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both Enos and the sons of Mosiah, after receiving personal spiritual assurance, immediately experience a burning desire for the welfare of their brethren and pour out prayers on their behalf.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('enos-1-9', 'num-21-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.070Z'),
  ('eph-4-24', 'gen-1-27', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The ''new man'' is described as ''created after God in righteousness and true holiness,'' directly alluding to humanity''s original creation in God''s image (tselem) in Genesis 1:27, framing salvation as restoration of that original likeness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.245Z'),
  ('eph-4-6', 'alma-33-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.245Z'),
  ('eph-6-18', 'enos-1-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.245Z'),
  ('eph-6-4', 'enos-1-1', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.245Z'),
  ('ether-1-36', 'enos-1-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages depict a faithful man, having first secured a blessing for himself, then interceding before the Lord on behalf of friends and broader groups, with the Lord extending compassion in response to each successive petition.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.375Z'),
  ('ether-12-6', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi''s commitment to act before knowing how exemplifies the same principle Moroni articulates—that the witness comes only after the trial of faith, not before obedient action.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.528Z'),
  ('ether-12-6', 'alma-32-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma likewise defines faith as hope in things ''which are not seen, which are true,'' and both passages insist that the unseen nature of spiritual realities is no grounds for disputing their reality.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.528Z'),
  ('ether-2-22', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages show a faithful servant reporting obedience (''I have done even as thou hast commanded'') and then presenting a new problem to the Lord, illustrating the pattern of faithful action followed by continued divine dialogue.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.528Z'),
  ('ether-2-24', 'gen-1-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-2-3', 'gen-1-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The deliberate carrying of ''seeds of every kind'' echoes the creation mandate to bring forth vegetation after its kind, framing the Jaredite migration as a new-creation event repopulating an uninhabited land.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z')
insert into lumen.edges (from_id, to_id, rel_type, collection_id, metadata, source, created_at) values
  ('ether-3-15', 'gen-1-26', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-3-15', 'gen-1-27', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Christ''s statement that ''all men were created in the beginning after mine own image'' directly invokes Genesis 1:27''s declaration that God created man ''in his own image,'' but recontextualizes it by identifying the divine image as specifically that of the premortal Christ.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-3-16', 'gen-1-27', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"God''s declaration that He created man ''after the body of my spirit'' directly parallels Genesis''s declaration that God created man ''in his own image,'' both asserting a physical-spiritual correspondence between God and humanity.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-3-19', 'alma-32-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Alma defines faith as hope in things not seen, and Ether 3:19 marks the precise moment faith was superseded—''he had faith no longer, for he knew, nothing doubting''—directly illustrating the transition Alma''s definition implies.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-3-9', 'alma-32-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages define faith as the mechanism by which unseen divine realities are perceived, with Ether 3:9 providing the narrative demonstration of the principle Alma 32:21 articulates—that faith enables vision of what cannot otherwise be seen.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-6-10', 'gen-1-21', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-6-15', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The brother of Jared begetting sons and daughters in a newly inhabited promised land echoes the divine mandate to ''be fruitful and multiply and replenish the earth,'' fulfilling God''s foundational blessing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-6-18', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages describe a people spreading across the land, multiplying, and working the earth, echoing the divine mandate to ''be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-6-3', 'gen-1-3', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both describe God causing light to exist where there was darkness, with the Lord''s creative power over light operative in both the primordial deep and the dark interior of the Jaredite barges crossing the deep.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-8-26', '1-ne-3-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi cites preserving scripture so that people ''not dwindle in unbelief'' and be led to good, directly paralleling Moroni''s stated purpose that his record is commanded so ''evil may be done away'' and people ''be persuaded to do good continually.''","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-8-3', '1-ne-3-29', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages involve a son rising violently against his father figure in a struggle for power and authority, reflecting the theme of familial betrayal and its destructive consequences.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.647Z'),
  ('ether-9-18', 'gen-1-24', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The enumeration of cattle, oxen, cows, sheep, swine, and goats echoes the creation account''s listing of cattle and creeping things after their kind, framing Jaredite abundance as a fulfillment of God''s creative provision.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.828Z'),
  ('ex-1-7', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The language of ''fruitful,'' ''multiplied,'' and filling the land in Exodus 1:7 directly echoes God''s creation mandate in Genesis 1:28 (''Be fruitful, and multiply, and replenish the earth''), casting Israel''s growth as fulfillment of divine blessing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"allusion"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.828Z'),
  ('ex-12-28', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi''s declaration that God ''shall prepare a way'' for keeping commandments mirrors the obedient response of Israel in Exodus 12:28 — both passages affirm immediate, complete compliance with divine instruction as the defining mark of covenant faithfulness.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.828Z'),
  ('ex-14-15', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Nephi''s principle that God prepares a way when He commands parallels God''s rebuke to Moses—prayer alone is insufficient; Israel must act on the divine command to go forward.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.948Z'),
  ('ex-18-25', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both texts illustrate God''s pattern of raising up capable, chosen individuals to fulfill specific roles in governing or serving His people, reflecting the principle that the Lord prepares means through human instruments.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:30.948Z'),
  ('ex-20-11', 'alma-32-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"source":"bible-bom-curated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:31.160Z'),
  ('ex-3-10', '1-ne-3-7', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both passages affirm the principle that when God commands and sends a servant on a seemingly impossible mission, He prepares the way, reflecting the broader pattern of divine commissioning with divine enablement.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:31.969Z'),
