  ('gen-2-15', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses establish humanity''s mandate to exercise dominion and stewardship over the earth and its creatures, with Genesis 1:28 giving the broader command to ''replenish and subdue'' and Genesis 2:15 specifying that stewardship as dressing and keeping the garden.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
  ('gen-2-19', 'gen-1-20', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Genesis 1:20 records God''s creation of fowl and sea creatures in the creation account, while Genesis 2:19 revisits the formation of beasts and fowl in the Eden narrative, and the verbal echo of ''formed'' and ''fowl of the air'' links both accounts as complementary creation witnesses.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
  ('gen-2-20', 'gen-1-18', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"The search for a ''help meet'' in Gen 2:20 echoes God''s declaration that ''it is not good that the man should be alone'' (Gen 2:18), establishing the need for companionship that drives the narrative forward.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
  ('gen-2-20', 'gen-1-28', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Adam''s naming authority over all living creatures in Gen 2:20 enacts the dominion mandate given to humanity in Gen 1:28, where God grants rule over every living thing.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
  ('gen-2-5', 'gen-1-11', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses describe the creation of plants and herbs, but from different vantage points — Genesis 1:11 records God commanding vegetation to appear, while Genesis 2:5 specifies the pre-conditions (no rain, no man to till) before that vegetation was established on earth.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"parallel"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
  ('gen-2-6', 'gen-1-2', 'CROSS_REF', 'phase-b', '{"reason":"Both verses depict water as a primordial element present at or near the beginning of creation — the waters over which the Spirit moved in Genesis 1:2 and the mist rising from the earth in Genesis 2:6 both frame water as foundational to life''s emergence.","source":"ai-generated","to_label":"LM_Verse","from_label":"LM_Verse","relationship":"thematic"}'::jsonb, 'anthropic-batch', '2026-07-01T22:01:36.286Z'),
