  ('strongs', 'G9259', 'strongs', 'sumbolon σύμβολον', '''1'':6C ''2'':45C ''3'':57C ''4'':85C ''5'':109C ''6'':145C ''7'':161C ''adespota'':19C ''advanc'':54C ''aeschulus'':30C,43C ''alien'':118C ''aristophan'':119C,143C ''athen'':87C ''beacon'':28C ''beacon-fir'':27C ''bodi'':39C ''bone'':69C ''broke'':75C ''christian'':152C ''coin'':71C ''comicus'':120C,144C ''commerc'':174C ''commerci'':185C ''compar'':140C ''confess'':154C ''counter'':90C ''coven'':167C ''creed'':158C ''datestragica'':18C ''demosthen'':107C,175C,197C ''dicast'':99C ''distinct'':149C ''eccl'':147C ''end'':139C ''etc'':84C,177C ''euripid'':40C ''faith'':156C ''fee'':106C ''fire'':29C ''g9259'':1A ''given'':96C,116C,123C ''halv'':66C ''herdotus'':82C ''historicus'':83C ''hospital'':63C ''i.e'':64C ''infer'':14C ''iv'':142C ''join'':128C ''keep'':79C ''lat'':61C,91C,159C ''legal'':163C ''licenc'':113C ''lysia'':55C ''make'':183C ''mark'':36C,150C ''ml'':199C ''money'':52C ''often'':32C ''omen'':42C ''one'':13C,80C ''orat'':56C,108C,176C,198C ''pawn'':49C ''payment'':136C ''permit'':111C ''person'':74C,126C ''phrase'':164C ''picnic'':131C ''piec'':81C ''pledg'':47C ''plural'':34C,59C ''present'':101C,134C ''protect'':172C ''receiv'':104C ''resid'':115C ''sign'':8C ''state'':170C,189C ''sumbolon'':2A,3A ''symbol'':5B ''symbolum'':160C ''talli'':60C ''tessera'':62C,92C ''thing'':16C ''ticket'':89C,122C ''token'':10C,24C ''tragicus'':31C,44C ''treati'':186C,196C ''two'':73C,169C ''variant'':17C ''violat'':194C ''λαμπάδος'':20C ''ποιεῖσθαι'':179C ''πρὸς'':180C ''πόλιν'':181C ''ς'':191C ''συγχέειν'':192C ''συμβολή'':141C ''σύμβολα'':165C,178C ''σύμβολον'':22C ''τὰ'':190C ''τὸ'':21C'::tsvector, '{"lang":"greek","gloss":"a symbol","original":"σύμβολον","translit":"sumbolon","strongs_no":"G9259"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''ahead'':116 ''back'':54,78 ''base'':109 ''behind'':86 ''believ'':16 ''boot'':68,120 ''brought'':65 ''come'':143 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cross'':90 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''egypt'':85 ''exodus'':80 ''faith'':10,44 ''find'':9,105 ''friend'':52 ''god'':142 ''gonna'':73 ''good'':126 ''got'':132 ''halverson'':60 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''hike'':67,115,119 ''hope'':63 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':59 ''left'':84 ''lord'':14 ''m'':58 ''man'':5 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''mose'':137 ''mount'':111 ''navig'':97 ''need'':74 ''one'':38,133 ''order'':123 ''re'':72 ''red'':92 ''rod'':140 ''sea'':93 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''sin'':101 ''sinai'':112 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''stick'':128 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''think'':134 ''thou'':18 ''today'':69,103 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':56 ''us'':87 ''ve'':83,89,95,131 ''walk'':127 ''welcom'':53 ''wilder'':99 ''yes'':118'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, friends. Welcome back to Unshaken. I''m Jared Halverson, and I hope you brought your hiking boots today because we''re gonna need them. We are back in Exodus, and we''ve left Egypt behind us. We''ve crossed the Red Sea. We''ve been navigating our wilderness of sin, and today, we find ourselves at the base of Mount Sinai with some hiking ahead. So, yes, hiking boots are in order, and a good walking stick if you''ve got one. Thinking of you, Moses, and the rod of God.","seq_end":12,"t_end_s":62.59,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#294', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''absolut'':23 ''abus'':17 ''alreadi'':65 ''among'':18 ''approach'':91 ''aton'':103 ''birth'':20 ''came'':9 ''children'':6 ''construct'':106 ''creation'':101 ''damag'':77 ''deconstruct'':107 ''degre'':124 ''drug'':16 ''elsewher'':71 ''especi'':126 ''faith'':97 ''fall'':102 ''foster'':5,61 ''go'':119 ''handl'':42 ''hard'':13 ''help'':48,79 ''ill'':28 ''interest'':59 ''kid'':62,128 ''learn'':112 ''major'':26 ''mental'':27 ''need'':117 ''neglect'':24 ''pair'':35 ''parent'':21 ''rais'':60,66 ''realli'':11,12 ''reconstruct'':108 ''relearn'':87,114 ''said'':39,56 ''saint'':37 ''situat'':14 ''stage'':95 ''three'':4 ''tri'':73 ''undo'':75 ''unlearn'':81,113 ''way'':70,100 ''wife'':32 ''wrong'':69'::tsvector, '{"text":"And he has three foster children, and they came from really, really hard situations with drug abuse among their birth parents and absolute neglect and major mental illness. He and his wife are a pair of saints that said, We can handle all that, and we can help them. And so they are. And he said, It''s interesting raising foster kids that were already raised in the wrong way elsewhere, and trying to undo that damage to help them unlearn so that they can then relearn. That''s the approach. That''s the stages of faith, by the way, creation, fall, atonement. There''s construction, deconstruction, reconstruction, or there''s learn, unlearn, relearn. We all need to go through it to a degree, but especially his kids.","seq_end":309,"t_end_s":1202.78,"seq_start":294,"t_start_s":1151.97,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#466', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''18'':28 ''accomplish'':24 ''accord'':92 ''altogeth'':32 ''ascend'':48 ''descend'':39 ''dilig'':22 ''eye'':70 ''faith'':75 ''fire'':43,63 ''furnac'':54 ''goal'':17 ''god'':97 ''great'':60 ''like'':78 ''ll'':7 ''lord'':38 ''made'':91 ''mose'':19 ''mount'':29,58 ''peopl'':3 ''play'':11 ''purifi'':65 ''quak'':59,77 ''readi'':4 ''reduc'':82 ''requir'':73 ''rubbl'':84 ''said'':80 ''see'':8 ''seek'':21 ''sinai'':30 ''smoke'':35,46,51,66 ''standard'':95 ''therefor'':72 ''thereof'':47 ''thing'':85 ''truli'':89 ''upon'':40 ''veil'':68 ''vers'':27 ''well'':5 ''whole'':57'::tsvector, '{"text":"Are the people ready? Well, we''ll see how that plays out, but that is the goal and Moses is seeking diligently to accomplish it. In verse 18, Mount Sinai was altogether on a smoke because the Lord descended upon it in fire and the smoke thereof ascended as the smoke of a furnace and the whole mount quaked greatly. There''s fire to purify, smoke to veil our eyes and therefore require our faith. The quaking, like I said, to reduce to rubble things that have not truly been made according to the standards of God.","seq_end":476,"t_end_s":1808.005,"seq_start":466,"t_start_s":1770.695,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#678', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''anyth'':1,91 ''away'':98 ''book'':117 ''certain'':40,60 ''cheap'':5 ''couldn'':129 ''counten'':31 ''creat'':137 ''daughter'':20 ''depict'':127 ''disappoint'':122 ''els'':2 ''end'':95 ''engraven'':28 ''ever'':108 ''fact'':68 ''faith'':86 ''god'':12,57,82,105 ''graven'':65 ''heart'':143 ''homag'':46 ''honest'':90 ''imag'':27,38,50,66 ''imit'':6 ''invis'':81,104 ''justic'':132 ''lesser'':37,49 ''live'':11 ''mind'':141 ''movi'':111,125 ''need'':35,63,72 ''pay'':45 ''place'':85 ''probabl'':94 ''read'':115 ''realiti'':101 ''remind'':77 ''seen'':109 ''son'':16,22 ''take'':97 ''thing'':75 ''true'':9 ''understand'':24 ''ve'':114 ''visibl'':74,92 ''want'':43 ''well'':58 ''would'':93'::tsvector, '{"text":"Anything else is a cheap imitation of the true and living God. I am his son. You are his daughter or son. To understand that, his image engraven in our countenance, I don''t need any lesser image. I certainly don''t want to pay homage to some lesser image that''s out there. No other gods? Well, I certainly don''t need a graven image. In fact, I don''t need a visible thing to remind me of the invisible God. I will place faith in him because honestly, anything visible would probably end up taking away from the reality of the invisible God. Have you ever seen a movie that you''ve read the book for and you were disappointed because the movie''s depiction just couldn''t do justice to what you had created in your own mind and heart?","seq_end":687,"t_end_s":2710.605,"seq_start":678,"t_start_s":2662.74,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#1077', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''14'':76 ''adulteri'':84 ''angri'':43 ''back'':88 ''break'':72 ''command'':79 ''commit'':83 ''coven'':106 ''cross'':56,62 ''distanc'':50 ''draw'':46 ''enough'':34 ''even'':41 ''exist'':94 ''faith'':103 ''famili'':97 ''get'':42 ''import'':8 ''intimaci'':91 ''jesus'':22 ''kill'':4,38 ''law'':25 ''let'':44 ''life'':14 ''line'':48 ''ll'':60 ''make'':69 ''mount'':21 ''must'':93 ''never'':61 ''one'':58,64 ''rais'':27 ''safe'':49 ''say'':30 ''sermon'':18 ''seventh'':78 ''shalt'':2,81 ''take'':23 ''thou'':1,80 ''true'':101 ''understand'':10 ''valu'':12 ''vers'':75 ''within'':95'::tsvector, '{"text":"Thou shalt not kill. It''s so important to understand the value of life that in the Sermon on the Mount, Jesus takes that law and raises it and says, it''s not enough not just to kill. Don''t even get angry. Let''s draw a line, safe distance, that if you don''t cross this one, you''ll never cross that one because that''s a make it or break it. In verse 14, the seventh commandment, thou shalt not commit adultery. And that, again, back to the intimacy that must exist within the family and to be true and faithful to those covenants.","seq_end":1088,"t_end_s":4173.855,"seq_start":1077,"t_start_s":4131.94,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#1182', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''19'':21,104 ''b'':77 ''book'':62 ''c'':20,103 ''command'':108 ''covet'':114 ''d'':18,101 ''e'':76 ''earth'':71 ''excus'':24 ''faith'':37 ''farm'':56,89 ''freeli'':121 ''give'':51,86 ''go'':67 ''got'':58 ''granton'':78 ''great'':9 ''harri'':27 ''impart'':119 ''interest'':5 ''know'':2 ''last'':15 ''lord'':43,97 ''martin'':26 ''money'':81 ''mormon'':64 ''mortgag'':53 ''need'':45,79,91 ''oliv'':23 ''phrase'':98 ''point'':12 ''properti'':33,117 ''publish'':60 ''righteous'':73 ''sacrific'':40 ''say'':106 ''shalt'':112 ''struggl'':29 ''sweep'':69 ''thee'':109 ''thine'':115 ''thou'':111 ''vers'':10 ''way'':95 ''will'':49 ''year'':16 ''yes'':75'::tsvector, '{"text":"You know, it''s interesting, there''s a great verse, I pointed this out last year, in D and C 19 when Oliver excuse me, Martin Harris is struggling with his own property and his own faith and his sacrifice, And the Lord just needs him to be willing to give up mortgage of the farm. We got to publish the Book of Mormon. It''s going to sweep the earth with righteousness. But yes, E. B. Granton needs some money. So do it. Just give up your farm if need be. But the way the Lord phrases it in D and C 19, he says, I command thee that thou shalt not covet thine own property, but impart it freely.","seq_end":1191,"t_end_s":4589.865,"seq_start":1182,"t_start_s":4552.525,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#2757', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''amid'':113 ''bless'':49 ''brother'':14,80 ''cloud'':115 ''day'':103 ''elder'':79 ''faculti'':83 ''faith'':26,30,35,87 ''full'':57,85 ''get'':124 ''gift'':7 ''give'':70 ''god'':117 ''good'':13 ''happen'':40 ''hasn'':118 ''heal'':32,38 ''impati'':125 ''incred'':24,25 ''m'':9 ''man'':22 ''meet'':33 ''member'':84 ''miracl'':39,66 ''mose'':104 ''mountain'':108 ''name'':58 ''need'':47,92 ''oh'':45 ''older'':82 ''one'':3 ''paid'':88 ''pass'':18 ''past'':109 ''pleas'':69 ''prepar'':75,95 ''price'':90 ''remind'':98 ''seek'':68 ''sinc'':16 ''sit'':51 ''six'':102 ''spiritu'':6 ''spoken'':120 ''sure'':10,50 ''time'':73 ''veil'':111 ''vers'':97 ''wasn'':43 ''whatev'':89 ''yet'':121'::tsvector, '{"text":"That was one of the spiritual gifts, I''m sure, of this good brother who since has passed on, but a man of incredible, incredible faith. And when the faith to heal meets the faith to be healed, miracles happen. And it wasn''t, oh, you need a blessing? Sure. Sit down. And what''s your full name again? No. It was, that''s the miracle you seek? Please give me some time to prepare myself. And as elder brother, this older faculty member full of faith, paid whatever price he needed to to prepare. His verse reminds me of it. Six days Moses is on the mountain, past the veil, there amid the cloud, but God hasn''t spoken yet. Do you get impatient?","seq_end":2772,"t_end_s":10958.886,"seq_start":2757,"t_start_s":10909.14,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#3551', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''also'':12,26 ''ask'':97 ''author'':32,37 ''christ'':5 ''faith'':57,78,86 ''famous'':51 ''god'':10,17,34,96 ''grow'':40 ''joseph'':49 ''lamb'':8 ''lectur'':55 ''life'':81 ''love'':48 ''lowli'':22 ''meek'':20 ''natur'':91 ''necessari'':79 ''never'':70 ''outgrowth'':92 ''power'':27,39,73 ''produc'':76 ''quot'':52 ''ram'':15 ''religion'':60 ''requir'':64 ''sacrific'':46,66,95 ''salvat'':83 ''self'':45 ''strong'':29 ''suffici'':74 ''thing'':69 ''think'':3 ''unto'':80 ''us'':99'::tsvector, '{"text":"But to think of Christ as the lamb of God, but also as the ram of God. He is meek and lowly, but he''s also powerful and strong with the authority of God. And his authority, his power grows out of his own self sacrifice. I love Joseph''s famous quote from the Lectures on Faith that a religion that does not require the sacrifice of all things never has the power sufficient to produce the faith necessary unto life and salvation. No. That faith has to be a natural outgrowth of the sacrifice God asks of us.","seq_end":3559,"t_end_s":14177.745,"seq_start":3551,"t_start_s":14138.93,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#3560', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''add'':50 ''altar'':10 ''ash'':64 ''author'':19 ''basin'':70 ''beauti'':45 ''behalf'':31 ''brass'':87 ''earlier'':91 ''faith'':24 ''fire'':77 ''flesh'':73 ''give'':13,17 ''grant'':22 ''hook'':74 ''horn'':7 ''like'':88 ''made'':39 ''make'':58,85 ''other'':33 ''pan'':60,78 ''power'':15,46 ''receiv'':62 ''sacrific'':29,35,42 ''said'':90 ''shalt'':57,84 ''shovel'':67 ''symbol'':47 ''thereof'':82 ''think'':4 ''thou'':56,83 ''three'':55 ''ultim'':41 ''us'':14,18,23,44 ''vers'':54 ''vessel'':81 ''willing'':27 ''workplac'':95'::tsvector, '{"text":"And so to think of these horns on the altar and what gives us power, what gives us authority, what what grants us faith is our willingness to sacrifice on behalf of others and sacrifice for him who made the ultimate sacrifice for us. Beautiful, powerful symbolism here. To add to that in verse three, thou shalt make his pans to receive his ashes and his shovels and his basins and his flesh hooks and his fire pans. All the vessels thereof thou shalt make of brass. Like I said earlier, this is a workplace.","seq_end":3564,"t_end_s":14210.296,"seq_start":3560,"t_start_s":14178.226,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#4021', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''bear'':56,68 ''bless'':105 ''burden'':59 ''cours'':40,51,63,74 ''faith'':47 ''give'':101 ''glori'':91 ''go'':43,54,66,77 ''god'':80 ''guidanc'':82 ''heart'':72 ''high'':8 ''holi'':1,27 ''lord'':4,30 ''m'':34,42,53,65,76 ''mind'':16,23 ''never'':94 ''other'':61 ''ought'':18 ''perspect'':11 ''priest'':9 ''priesthood'':104 ''seek'':79 ''serv'':45 ''think'':35 ''thummim'':87 ''time'':26 ''upon'':70 ''urim'':85 ''ve'':98 ''well'':5 ''worthili'':49 ''yet'':99'::tsvector, '{"text":"Holiness to the Lord. Well, from the high priest''s perspective, what''s on my mind? What ought to be on my mind at all times? Holiness to the Lord. And if I''m thinking about that, then of course I''m going to serve him faithfully and worthily. Of course I''m going to bear up the burdens of others. Of course I''m going to bear them upon my heart. Of course I''m going to seek God''s guidance through that Urim and Thummim and to his glory. It''s never about me. I''ve yet to give myself a priesthood blessing.","seq_end":4032,"t_end_s":16106.955,"seq_start":4021,"t_start_s":16072.085,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#4621', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''aaron'':53,89 ''altar'':95 ''ark'':30 ''best'':56 ''built'':93 ''calf'':6 ''cherubim'':24 ''children'':66 ''come'':84 ''coven'':33 ''even'':9 ''faith'':77 ''five'':87 ''focus'':75 ''god'':13,16,39 ''golden'':5 ''interest'':78 ''isn'':7 ''lid'':27 ''mayb'':3 ''mean'':22,51 ''meant'':10 ''need'':68 ''pagan'':64 ''peopl'':61 ''possibl'':79 ''problem'':83 ''rather'':15 ''real'':82 ''ride'':18 ''saw'':90 ''sit'':43 ''someth'':69 ''tangibl'':72 ''throne'':37 ''upon'':19,45 ''utter'':63 ''vers'':86 ''visibl'':73 ''would'':42'::tsvector, '{"text":"And so maybe this golden calf isn''t even meant to be God, but rather God will ride upon it. I mean, the cherubim on the lid of the Ark of the Covenant, there''s the throne of God, and he would sit there upon it. So are they I mean, is Aaron doing the best he can? Are the people not utter pagans but children and needing something more, again, tangible, visible to focus their faith? Interesting possibilities here. The real problem comes in verse five. When Aaron saw it, he built an altar before it.","seq_end":4634,"t_end_s":18480.785,"seq_start":4621,"t_start_s":18438.291,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#4715', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''alon'':47 ''angri'':88 ''behold'':14 ''bow'':28 ''burn'':96 ''consum'':64 ''faith'':42 ''god'':33,40,48 ''great'':73 ''hot'':57 ''hous'':105 ''humil'':31 ''indign'':92 ''israel'':107 ''let'':45,98 ''look'':37 ''lord'':5 ''m'':85,87 ''make'':69 ''may'':55,63 ''mose'':8,51 ''nation'':74 ''neck'':19,22 ''nine'':3 ''oh'':83 ''peopl'':13,20 ''righteous'':91 ''said'':81 ''say'':6,49 ''seen'':11 ''start'':109 ''stiff'':18,24 ''thee'':71 ''therefor'':44 ''understand'':77 ''vers'':2 ''wax'':56 ''whole'':104 ''wipe'':101 ''won'':26 ''wrath'':54'::tsvector, '{"text":"In verse nine, the Lord says to Moses, I have seen this people. Behold, it is a stiff necked people. Their neck so stiff, they won''t bow down in humility before God, nor will they look up to God in faith. Now therefore, let me alone, God says to Moses, that my wrath may wax hot against them and that I may consume them, and I will make of thee a great nation. Now you understand what he just said there? Oh, I''m I''m angry. This is righteous indignation, and it is burning. So let me just wipe out the whole house of Israel and start over again with you.","seq_end":4724,"t_end_s":18836.88,"seq_start":4715,"t_start_s":18800.92,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#5203', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''11'':60 ''abl'':40,49 ''alway'':104 ''calf'':22 ''camp'':81 ''close'':107 ''cloud'':33 ''depart'':93 ''face'':66,68 ''faith'':26 ''friend'':75 ''get'':6 ''god'':13 ''golden'':21 ''israel'':15 ''joshua'':85,103 ''kudo'':100 ''ll'':38,47 ''lord'':62 ''man'':71,92 ''mose'':65,109 ''need'':19 ''nun'':89 ''peer'':28 ''possibl'':111 ''re'':3,9 ''righteous'':54 ''servant'':84 ''smoke'':35 ''son'':87 ''spake'':63 ''speak'':113 ''speaketh'':72 ''spoke'':112 ''start'':4 ''stay'':105 ''tabernacl'':98 ''talk'':42 ''true'':12 ''truth'':57 ''turn'':77 ''unto'':64,73,79 ''veil'':31 ''vers'':59 ''worship'':10,51 ''young'':91'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now you''re starting to get it. We''re worshiping the true God of Israel. You don''t need a golden calf. Just have the faith to peer through that veil, that cloud of smoke, and you''ll be able to talk with him yourself. You''ll be able to worship him in righteousness and in truth. In verse 11, the Lord spake unto Moses face to face as a man speaketh unto his friend. He turned again unto the camp, but his servant Joshua the son of Nun, a young man, departed not out of the tabernacle. Again, kudos to you, Joshua, always staying as close to Moses as possible.","seq_end":5210,"t_end_s":20800.76,"seq_start":5203,"t_start_s":20763.201,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#5363', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''11'':32 ''20'':3,98 ''3three'':97 ''beg'':23 ''canst'':7 ''exodus'':96 ''explain'':30 ''face'':11,37,40,42,106 ''fact'':46 ''faith'':59 ''father'':71 ''first'':54 ''friend'':44 ''god'':4,34,108 ''grove'':78 ''handl'':64 ''imposs'':94 ''joseph'':68 ''live'':20,110 ''ll'':80 ''man'':16 ''mose'':36 ''often'':81 ''oh'':85 ''one'':102 ''peopl'':47,56 ''question'':25 ''quot'':82 ''sacr'':77 ''saw'':35 ''say'':5,99 ''see'':9,17,69,104 ''shalt'':14 ''son'':74 ''spake'':39 ''spoke'':111 ''take'':51 ''thou'':6,13 ''thought'':66 ''vers'':2,31,84 ''vision'':55 ''want'':49'::tsvector, '{"text":"In verse 20, God says, thou canst not see my face, for thou shalt no man see me and live. Now that begs the question, then how do we explain verse 11? That God saw Moses face they spake face to face as friends. In fact, people who want to take down the first vision, people of other faiths that just can''t handle the thought of Joseph seeing the father and the son in the sacred grove, they''ll often quote that verse. Oh, no, no, no, you can''t. That''s impossible because Exodus 3three 20 says that no one can see the face of God and live.","seq_end":5369,"t_end_s":21407.432,"seq_start":5363,"t_start_s":21372.06,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#5380', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''ago'':68 ''also'':83 ''among'':96 ''anger'':78 ''believ'':29 ''canst'':53 ''clarifi'':8 ''destroy'':86 ''face'':57 ''faith'':25 ''fine'':71 ''friend'':22 ''go'':18 ''help'':20,38 ''joseph'':4,32 ''kindl'':80 ''know'':14 ''lest'':76 ''live'':104 ''lord'':45 ''man'':95 ''mine'':77 ''mose'':51 ''nine'':66 ''peopl'':90 ''realli'':46 ''right'':74 ''said'':47 ''say'':49 ''see'':55,98 ''shall'':93 ''situat'':64 ''smith'':5,33 ''specif'':65 ''thee'':82,87 ''thi'':89 ''thing'':11 ''thou'':52 ''time'':60,102 ''translat'':6,34 ''us'':40 ''vers'':67 ''whole'':10'::tsvector, '{"text":"There''s a Joseph Smith translation that clarifies the whole thing. Now I know that''s not going to help our friends of other faiths. They don''t believe in the Joseph Smith translation, but this is helpful for us. Here''s what the Lord really said. He says to Moses, thou canst not see my face at this time. So this is situation specific. Nine verses ago, it was fine, but not right now. Lest mine anger be kindled against thee also, and I destroy thee and thy people. For there shall no man among them see me at this time and live.","seq_end":5385,"t_end_s":21479.176,"seq_start":5380,"t_start_s":21448.984,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8#5844', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Exodus 19-34 - Moses at Mount Sinai', '''church'':90 ''coven'':32,36 ''daughter'':15,20 ''denomin'':94 ''differ'':95 ''faith'':79 ''fals'':6 ''forget'':93 ''get'':63 ''given'':56 ''god'':7 ''hang'':73 ''hold'':39 ''intermarri'':28 ''m'':67 ''mean'':34 ''member'':76 ''mingl'':13 ''mix'':11 ''nephi'':83 ''numer'':48 ''outsid'':29 ''pass'':44 ''pleas'':60 ''poster'':49 ''prefer'':81 ''re'':27 ''said'':84 ''say'':69 ''son'':18,23 ''start'':3,10 ''two'':89 ''worship'':4 ''wrong'':65'::tsvector, '{"text":"Then you start worshiping those false gods, then you start mixing and mingling their daughters with your sons, your daughters with their sons, and now we''re intermarrying outside of the covenant, which means the covenant can''t hold. It''s not being passed down to that numerous posterity? No. It''s it''s being given up on. Now please don''t get me wrong. I''m not saying we can''t hang out with members of other faiths. I prefer what Nephi said, that there''s only two churches out there. Forget denominational differences.","seq_end":5853,"t_end_s":23297.945,"seq_start":5844,"t_start_s":23259.5,"episode_id":"unshaken-25hrVBU3Vz8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''back'':56 ''believ'':16 ''come'':152 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''even'':74,84 ''exact'':97 ''faith'':10,44 ''far'':116 ''favorit'':99 ''find'':9 ''forgotten'':129 ''forsaken'':127 ''friend'':53 ''half'':91 ''halverson'':62 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''histor'':151 ''histori'':134,140 ''incred'':150 ''invit'':68 ''isn'':95 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':61 ''king'':94 ''know'':119 ''like'':78 ''lord'':14 ''m'':60,64 ''make'':108 ''man'':5 ''mani'':109 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''most'':135 ''old'':103,132 ''one'':38,80 ''part'':100,130 ''peopl'':88,123 ''say'':83,145 ''scriptur'':72 ''second'':90,93 ''section'':114 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''strong'':29 ''studi'':73 ''tale'':111 ''testament'':104,133 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''thrill'':65 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':58 ''veggi'':110 ''week'':77 ''welcom'':55 ''well'':141'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends, and welcome back to Unshaken. I''m Jared Halverson, I''m thrilled that you invite me over for scripture study even on a week like this one. And I say even because for most people, the second half of second Kings isn''t exactly their favorite part of the Old Testament. They don''t make many veggie tales of this section as far as I know. And for most people, it''s a forsaken or forgotten part of Old Testament history, mostly because it''s just history. Well, I don''t say just, but it''s incredibly historical.","seq_end":12,"t_end_s":67.005,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.72,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#836', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''bow'':91,99 ''call'':29 ''direct'':108 ''elsewher'':23 ''ever'':36 ''faith'':77 ''feel'':15 ''god'':75,84 ''hard'':21,45,64 ''harden'':1,10 ''heart'':11 ''humbl'':86 ''imag'':6 ''look'':72,81 ''love'':4 ''m'':13 ''mean'':51 ''neck'':3,22,32,39,61 ''oh'':48 ''re'':98 ''repent'':52,59 ''scriptur'':25 ''stiff'':31,41,68,105 ''submiss'':87 ''talk'':8 ''thing'':16,34 ''turn'':47,50 ''usual'':28 ''want'':95 ''won'':57,70,89 ''wonder'':55 ''world'':102 ''yeah'':53'::tsvector, '{"text":"Hardened their necks? Love that image. We talk about hardened hearts. I''m not feeling things, but how about a hard neck? Elsewhere in scripture, it''s usually called a stiff neck. Same thing. You ever had a neck so stiff that it was hard to turn? Oh, and turn means repent? Yeah. No wonder you won''t repent. Your neck is too hard. It''s too stiff. It won''t look up to God in faith nor will it look down before God in humble submission. You won''t bow before him. You want the you''re bowing before the world, not too stiff in that direction.","seq_end":843,"t_end_s":3565.745,"seq_start":836,"t_start_s":3529.605,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1059', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''12'':44 ''bear'':76 ''contrari'':100 ''david'':30 ''day'':11 ''easi'':69 ''faith'':21 ''find'':89 ''goldilock'':72,80 ''ground'':91 ''hard'':61 ''household'':19 ''interest'':5 ''israel'':28 ''jeroboam'':51,63 ''king'':43,84 ''kingdom'':26 ''like'':71 ''make'':58,66 ''middl'':90 ''nobodi'':97 ''one'':6,42,87 ''overzeal'':48 ''prove'':99 ''rehoboam'':46,55 ''rememb'':36 ''right'':96 ''saul'':29 ''schism'':16 ''see'':8 ''solomon'':31 ''sound'':70 ''split'':34 ''studi'':39 ''thing'':59,67 ''three'':75 ''two'':83 ''underzeal'':53 ''unit'':25 ''want'':56,64 ''well'':77 ''within'':17'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now that''s an interesting one to see in our day because there''s this schism within the household of faith. It was The United Kingdom Of Israel, Saul, David, Solomon, and then split. Why? Remember when we studied that in one Kings 12? Because Rehoboam was overzealous and because Jeroboam was underzealous. And Rehoboam wanted to make things too hard and Jeroboam wanted to make things too easy. Sound like Goldilocks and the three bears? Well, here''s Goldilocks and the Two Kings and no one''s finding middle ground where it''s just right. Nobody''s proving contraries.","seq_end":1069,"t_end_s":4405.885,"seq_start":1059,"t_start_s":4364.03,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1248', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''almighti'':49 ''assyria'':52 ''assyrian'':30 ''better'':107 ''beyond'':64 ''conquest'':31 ''demand'':57,66 ''distanc'':9 ''done'':95 ''even'':78 ''exorbit'':65 ''faith'':42 ''fall'':19 ''gold'':86 ''gonna'':18 ''happen'':26 ''heart'':103 ''hezekiah'':33,68,70,101 ''humbl'':38 ''kind'':22 ''king'':50,53 ''make'':55 ''next'':14 ''past'':98 ''pay'':76 ''place'':108 ''point'':81 ''re'':13 ''remov'':83 ''see'':4 ''seen'':93 ''sennacherib'':54 ''silver'':84 ''smoke'':6 ''templ'':89 ''thing'':24 ''think'':100 ''tri'':35 ''us'':47 ''ve'':92 ''well'':40 ''would'':44'::tsvector, '{"text":"and I can see the smoke in the distance, and and we''re next, and it''s gonna fall. The same kind of thing is happening here with the Assyrian conquest. But Hezekiah is trying to be humble as well as faithful. What would you have us do, almighty king of Assyria? King Sennacherib makes some demands, but they are so above and beyond, exorbitant demands of Hezekiah. But Hezekiah does all he can to pay them, even to the point of removing silver and gold from the temple. Now we''ve seen that done in the past. I think Hezekiah''s heart was in a better place.","seq_end":1260,"t_end_s":5223.66,"seq_start":1248,"t_start_s":5184.625,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1279', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''anti'':9,43 ''besieg'':89 ''certain'':64,68 ''choos'':72 ''come'':13 ''cut'':110 ''faith'':17 ''feel'':63 ''forc'':81,93 ''got'':119 ''great'':115 ''issu'':83 ''left'':35 ''like'':87 ''make'':61 ''matter'':15 ''mormon'':10 ''prove'':21,28 ''re'':34,109 ''religi'':44 ''rhetor'':37,45 ''right'':23 ''say'':52 ''starv'':100 ''studi'':42 ''surrend'':74,96 ''take'':5 ''tell'':105 ''term'':7 ''thing'':65,69,116 ''think'':67 ''time'':48 ''usual'':3 ''ve'':118 ''way'':58 ''wick'':124 ''world'':125 ''wrong'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s usually the take in terms of anti Mormonism. When it comes to matters of faith, I can''t prove it right, but you can''t prove it wrong, and so we''re left with rhetoric, which is why I study anti religious rhetoric all the time. What can I say to you in such a way that I make you feel certain things and think certain things where you choose to surrender on your own? I can''t force the issue. Again, it''s like being besieged. I can''t force you to surrender, but I can starve you out. I can tell you that you''re cut off from all the great things we''ve got out here in this wicked world.","seq_end":1282,"t_end_s":5335.27,"seq_start":1279,"t_start_s":5301.725,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1401', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''abl'':14,72 ''armi'':64 ''assyria'':52 ''call'':94 ''certain'':80 ''citi'':40 ''civil'':69 ''deceiv'':7 ''deliv'':16,36,44 ''excus'':92 ''faith'':55,95 ''flimsi'':91 ''got'':62 ''hand'':21,47 ''hezekiah'':6,24 ''hold'':87 ''king'':50 ''let'':5,23 ''lord'':30,33 ''make'':25 ''neither'':22 ''noth'':98 ''oh'':1 ''pleas'':84 ''say'':31 ''shall'':11,41 ''stand'':74 ''sure'':35 ''think'':59 ''trust'':27,101 ''us'':37 ''ve'':61 ''wish'':58 ''won'':81'::tsvector, '{"text":"Oh no, don''t let Hezekiah deceive you. For he shall not be able to deliver you out of his hand, neither let Hezekiah make you trust in the Lord saying, the Lord will surely deliver us and this city shall not be delivered into the hand of the king of Assyria? No, your faith is just wishful thinking. I''ve got an army here and no other civilization has been able to stand up against it. And you certainly won''t. So please do not hold on to these flimsy excuses you call faith. There''s nothing to it. Trust me.","seq_end":1409,"t_end_s":5871.9,"seq_start":1401,"t_start_s":5836.44,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1425', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''36'':29 ''advis'':59 ''answer'':37,49 ''armor'':119 ''assyrian'':93 ''children'':73 ''command'':46 ''common'':65 ''convert'':78 ''faith'':126 ''go'':89 ''god'':3,14,121 ''gonna'':18 ''held'':33 ''israel'':5,9,16 ''judah'':20 ''king'':44 ''live'':116 ''look'':110 ''m'':80 ''mano'':94,96 ''moment'':27 ''new'':77 ''peac'':35 ''peopl'':32 ''privat'':66 ''prophet'':103 ''realli'':11 ''safeti'':101 ''say'':48,82 ''shield'':124 ''spare'':8,19 ''stay'':98,114 ''take'':90 ''think'':12,23,56 ''throw'':83 ''troop'':62 ''underestim'':60 ''us'':112 ''vers'':28 ''wall'':71,87 ''watch'':106 ''watchtow'':109 ''within'':100 ''word'':41 ''yeah'':1 ''youth'':75'::tsvector, '{"text":"Yeah. The God of Israel did not spare Israel. You really think the God of Israel is gonna spare Judah? Don''t think it for a moment. Verse 36, but the people held their peace and answered him not a word, for the king''s commandment was saying, answer him not. That''s why I think that the advisers underestimated the troops. All those common privates up there on the wall, our children, our youth, our new converts. I''m not saying throw them out the wall and go take on the Assyrians, mano a mano. No. Stay here within safety with prophets on the watch on the watchtowers looking over us all. Stay here, live with the armor of God and the shield of faith.","seq_end":1440,"t_end_s":5988.835,"seq_start":1425,"t_start_s":5938.325,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1511', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''advis'':68 ''assyria'':24 ''blasphemi'':96 ''faith'':80 ''four'':3 ''god'':12,33,43,88 ''hath'':44 ''hear'':14 ''heard'':45 ''hope'':76 ''king'':22 ''least'':73 ''left'':56 ''lift'':47 ''live'':32 ''lord'':10,41 ''m'':75 ''master'':26 ''may'':7,70 ''mayb'':87 ''mention'':99 ''much'':79 ''muster'':84 ''overheard'':89 ''part'':65 ''prayer'':50 ''rabbuchadnezzar'':19 ''rebuk'':103 ''remnant'':53 ''reproach'':30 ''reprov'':36 ''right'':85 ''rob'':91 ''say'':5 ''sent'':28 ''shockett'':92 ''sort'':62 ''testimoni'':60 ''thi'':11,42,49 ''vers'':2 ''wherefor'':46 ''word'':17,38'::tsvector, '{"text":"In verse four, they say, it may be the Lord thy God will hear all the words of Rabbuchadnezzar, whom the king of Assyria, his master has sent to reproach the living God and will reprove the words which the Lord thy God hath heard. Wherefore, lift up thy prayer for the remnant that are left. This is a testimony of sorts on the part of these advisers. It may be, at least I''m hoping, as as much faith as I can muster right now, maybe God overheard what Rob Shockett was doing, that blasphemy I just mentioned, and he will rebuke them.","seq_end":1515,"t_end_s":6285.94,"seq_start":1511,"t_start_s":6256.1,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1843', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''19'':22 ''almost'':28 ''armi'':4 ''assyrian'':3 ''centuri'':94 ''chapter'':21 ''die'':67 ''end'':16,19 ''faith'':108 ''go'':99,105,110 ''god'':51 ''happen'':86 ''home'':63 ''isn'':52 ''judah'':87 ''kill'':71 ''king'':66 ''life'':47,102 ''like'':29,37,50,59 ''live'':45,100 ''mean'':11 ''move'':42 ''next'':77,81,93 ''okay'':60,76 ''plus'':95 ''ran'':9 ''re'':89 ''safe'':90 ''son'':74 ''stay'':107 ''still'':112 ''stori'':15 ''strong'':114 ''thing'':82 ''took'':6 ''trumpet'':54 ''underst'':25 ''victori'':56 ''wait'':30,31 ''way'':13 ''went'':62 ''yeah'':38'::tsvector, '{"text":"And the Assyrian army just took off and ran. I mean, the way the story ends at the end of chapter 19 is so understated. It''s almost like, wait, wait, is that it? It''s like, yeah, that''s it. Move on. Just live your life. It''s like God isn''t trumpeting his victories. It''s like, okay, they went home and the king died and he was killed by his sons and okay, next. What''s the next thing that has to happen? Judah, you''re safe for the next century plus. So how are going live your life? Are you going to stay faithful? Are going to still be strong?","seq_end":1850,"t_end_s":7682.61,"seq_start":1843,"t_start_s":7650.16,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1863', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''70'':85 ''aftermath'':124 ''amaz'':16 ''beauti'':58 ''blow'':134 ''book'':17 ''byu'':77 ''call'':34,49 ''came'':90 ''davi'':71,111 ''director'':62 ''dog'':149 ''elder'':19,79,105 ''eye'':37 ''faith'':10 ''famili'':148 ''first'':89 ''friend'':145 ''gave'':73 ''groberg'':22,82,106 ''h'':21 ''heaven'':54 ''hike'':139 ''john'':20 ''littl'':5 ''live'':3 ''ll'':8 ''longer'':6 ''man'':31,68 ''mind'':133 ''mission'':25,95,108,127 ''missionari'':120 ''mitch'':70,110 ''movi'':46,59,65,88,102 ''name'':69 ''promis'':12 ''rememb'':83 ''said'':129 ''side'':52 ''sister'':81 ''son'':142 ''stay'':9 ''stori'':96,114 ''storm'':40 ''talk'':75 ''tell'':93 ''told'':112 ''tonga'':27 ''turn'':43 ''young'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"Can I live a little longer? I''ll stay faithful, I promise. There''s an amazing book by Elder John H. Groberg about his mission in Tonga as a young man. It was called In the Eye of the Storm. It was turned into a movie that was called The Other Side of Heaven. It''s a beautiful movie. And the director of that movie was a man named Mitch Davis. He gave a talk at BYU with Elder and Sister Groberg, remember the ''70, when that movie first came out, to tell some mission stories and so on. And the movie is about Elder Groberg''s mission, but Mitch Davis told a story about his, not as a missionary, but in the aftermath of his mission. He said, and this is mind blowing, he was on a hike with his son and a friend and the family dog.","seq_end":1872,"t_end_s":7775.165,"seq_start":1863,"t_start_s":7727.105,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1917', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''amaz'':11 ''ask'':64 ''base'':70 ''better'':56,63 ''chang'':40,53,60,67 ''children'':78 ''concept'':87 ''death'':35 ''enough'':4 ''especi'':21 ''fact'':85 ''faith'':73 ''general'':91 ''generous'':13 ''god'':14,38,52,59,66 ''hezekiah'':8,29 ''isaiah'':26 ''king'':7,28 ''life'':19 ''mind'':42,55 ''passag'':80 ''prayer'':75,89 ''question'':47 ''said'':57 ''say'':82,93 ''sick'':33 ''sinc'':22 ''theolog'':46 ''told'':25 ''unto'':34 ''wait'':36 ''worth'':48 ''would'':81,92 ''wrestl'':49 ''yeah'':27 ''yes'':83,94'::tsvector, '{"text":"Will that be enough for you, King Hezekiah? It''s amazing how generous God is being here with life itself, especially since he just told Isaiah, yeah, King Hezekiah, this is a sickness unto death. Wait, did God just change his mind? This is a theological question worth wrestling with. Does God change his mind? Better said, does God change his will? Better asked, does God change his will based on the faith and prayers of his children? This passage would say yes. In fact, the concept of prayer in general would say yes.","seq_end":1925,"t_end_s":7980.775,"seq_start":1917,"t_start_s":7942.075,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#1972', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''10'':70 ''amaz'':85 ''ancestor'':41 ''around'':47 ''bought'':16 ''brought'':51 ''centuri'':20,54 ''d'':8 ''degre'':71 ''destroy'':34 ''done'':10 ''extra'':19,53,69,76 ''faith'':25 ''fifteen'':77 ''give'':66 ''guess'':59 ''happen'':96 ''hezekiah'':27,99 ''israel'':14 ''least'':61 ''life'':80 ''miracl'':86 ''moment'':102 ''peopl'':57 ''plus'':21 ''re'':30 ''realli'':82 ''righteous'':50 ''sundial'':74 ''thing'':93 ''turn'':44 ''way'':3 ''wicked'':38 ''year'':78'::tsvector, '{"text":"In a way, that''s what he''d just done for all of Israel. I bought you an extra century plus because of the faithfulness of Hezekiah. Now you''re about to be destroyed because of the wickedness of your ancestors and you turned it all around, and your righteousness brought an extra century for your people. I guess the least I can do is give you an extra 10 degrees on the sundial, an extra fifteen years of life. This really is an amazing miracle, but it''s not the only thing that''s happening on with Hezekiah at this moment.","seq_end":1979,"t_end_s":8186.26,"seq_start":1972,"t_start_s":8155.49,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#2053', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''absenc'':82 ''buri'':120 ''chronicl'':123 ''circumst'':99 ''dark'':23 ''decad'':69 ''doubt'':33 ''even'':1 ''everyth'':45 ''experi'':105 ''faith'':75 ''feel'':59 ''found'':126 ''go'':94 ''god'':3,60 ''grow'':101 ''hezekiah'':108 ''includ'':76 ''instead'':124 ''king'':107,129 ''know'':17,40,114 ''m'':35,43,52 ''mani'':71 ''mayb'':110 ''mother'':63 ''next'':90 ''night'':24 ''peopl'':72 ''second'':122,128 ''soul'':27 ''speak'':5 ''struggl'':36 ''suffer'':65 ''teresa'':64 ''time'':12,31 ''tri'':53 ''use'':48 ''vers'':91,96,116 ''well'':84 ''wrestl'':79'::tsvector, '{"text":"even when God is speaking to you. But there''s other times where I don''t know why. It''s just a dark night of the soul. It''s a time of doubt. I''m struggling. I don''t know why. I''m doing everything that I used to do. I''m trying, but I just don''t feel God with me. Mother Teresa suffered with that for decades and many people of any faith, including ours, have wrestled with this absence as well, and that''s why this next verse is my go to verse in these circumstances. It grows out of that experience from King Hezekiah, but maybe we don''t know this verse because it''s buried in second Chronicles instead of found in second Kings.","seq_end":2063,"t_end_s":8634.49,"seq_start":2053,"t_start_s":8591.195,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#2371', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''also'':50 ''began'':51 ''carpent'':4 ''child'':77 ''chronicl'':86 ''come'':24,42 ''eight'':64 ''faith'':30 ''give'':93 ''great'':34 ''hewer'':10 ''insight'':96 ''jehoiada'':49 ''jehoiash'':37 ''josiah'':39,62 ''keep'':83 ''lord'':67 ''mason'':7 ''materi'':19 ''money'':21 ''mover'':17 ''one'':46 ''paid'':2 ''parallel'':35,48 ''read'':84 ''reign'':53 ''restor'':70 ''seven'':61 ''start'':74 ''thing'':71 ''think'':78 ''us'':94 ''usual'':73 ''version'':87 ''want'':68 ''way'':92 ''wood'':12 ''young'':58 ''youth'':99'::tsvector, '{"text":"He paid the carpenters and the masons and the hewers of wood and the and the movers of materials. The money that was coming in, they did it all faithfully. There''s a great parallel between Jehoiash and Josiah when it comes to that. And one other parallel, Jehoiada also began to reign when he was very young. He was seven. Josiah was eight. When the Lord wants to restore things, he usually starts with a child. Think about that, but then keep reading. The Chronicles version of this, by the way, gives us an insight into that youth.","seq_end":2378,"t_end_s":10030.67,"seq_start":2371,"t_start_s":9996.301,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#2537', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''23'':72 ''best'':114 ''chapter'':71 ''consequ'':14 ''die'':20 ''elder'':94 ''faith'':8 ''fine'':43 ''gather'':91 ''get'':29 ''gonna'':40,68 ''good'':42 ''great'':144 ''hear'':82 ''hold'':86 ''hous'':110 ''humil'':6 ''influenc'':58 ''inhabit'':126 ''jerusalem'':98,128 ''josiah'':81 ''judah'':96,123 ''king'':52,75,80,105 ''leader'':48 ''ll'':19 ''lord'':113 ''m'':37,39,46,50,54 ''men'':121 ''need'':56 ''okay'':35 ''peac'':22 ''peopl'':59,140 ''place'':115 ''priest'':133 ''prophet'':136 ''prophetess'':89 ''righteous'':61 ''second'':74 ''sin'':16 ''small'':142 ''spare'':12 ''stori'':78 ''tell'':76 ''togeth'':99 ''two'':103 ''vers'':102 ''well'':63 ''went'':106 ''word'':84'::tsvector, '{"text":"And so because of your humility and faith, you will be spared the consequences of sin, and you''ll die in peace. So he did. But before we get there, what does he do? Okay. I''m I''m gonna be good. Fine. But I''m a leader. I''m the king. I''m I need to influence people to righteousness as well. So how am I gonna do that? Chapter 23 of second Kings tells his story. Once king Josiah hears the words of hold of the prophetess, he gathers all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem together. And in verse two, the king went up into the house of the Lord. Best place to do it. All the men of Judah, all the inhabitants of Jerusalem with him, and the priests, and the prophets, and all the people, both small and great.","seq_end":2541,"t_end_s":10754.029,"seq_start":2537,"t_start_s":10712.58,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#2542', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''boaz'':99 ''book'':27,50,61 ''call'':47,57 ''coven'':30,64 ''ear'':21 ''establish'':98 ''faith'':76 ''first'':43 ''found'':33 ''gather'':10 ''good'':80 ''hous'':13,36 ''israel'':7 ''joachim'':94 ''law'':53 ''lord'':16,39 ''mean'':95,100 ''next'':92 ''notic'':40 ''obedi'':71 ''one'':88 ''read'':18 ''relat'':75 ''saw'':44 ''stand'':91 ''strength'':83,104 ''support'':85 ''symbol'':81 ''transact'':70 ''wonder'':86 ''word'':24'::tsvector, '{"text":"And what''s he do once Israel has been gathered to the house of the Lord? He read in their ears all the words of the book of the covenant, which was found in the house of the Lord. Notice when he first saw it, they called it the book of the law. What''s he called it here? The book of the covenant. This is not about just transactional obedience. This is about relational faith, There''s a good symbol of strength, of support. Wonder which one he was standing next to. Joachim, meaning he will establish. Boaz, meaning in him is strength.","seq_end":2550,"t_end_s":10828.07,"seq_start":2542,"t_start_s":10754.795,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#2995', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''among'':24 ''beauti'':57 ''cri'':53 ''despis'':11 ''establish'':78 ''even'':27,50 ''faith'':26 ''feet'':63 ''first'':91 ''friend'':2 ''god'':41,72 ''half'':88 ''justif'':96 ''mean'':35 ''misus'':30 ''mock'':9 ''mountain'':60 ''peac'':68 ''prophet'':15,47 ''publish'':67 ''re'':75 ''reign'':97 ''reigneth'':73 ''repent'':55 ''sanctif'':93 ''sayeth'':70 ''second'':87 ''sometim'':29 ''thi'':71 ''think'':49 ''tri'':76 ''ultim'':43 ''upon'':58 ''use'':44 ''usual'':5 ''wanna'':81 ''wick'':7 ''word'':13 ''worri'':18 ''zion'':79'::tsvector, '{"text":"My friends, it''s usually the wicked who mock and despise the words of prophets, but I worry for you and me that among the faithful, even we sometimes misuse them. And what I mean by that is what''s God''s ultimate use for a prophet? I think even more than cry in repentance. How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of those who publish peace, who sayeth thy God reigneth. We''re trying to establish Zion. We wanna be on the on the second half, not the first, the sanctification, not the justification.","seq_end":3004,"t_end_s":12826.444,"seq_start":2995,"t_start_s":12790.165,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw#3014', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 14-25 - The Scattering of Israel', '''amaz'':65 ''better'':36 ''build'':104 ''challeng'':71 ''come'':108 ''debri'':87 ''faith'':4 ''foundat'':94 ''god'':97 ''grate'':40,50 ''hear'':76 ''helm'':56 ''hezekiah'':53 ''inspir'':47 ''learn'':74 ''let'':17,96 ''live'':90,101 ''lord'':78 ''m'':39,49 ''meant'':27 ''momentum'':106 ''nelson'':62 ''person'':81 ''place'':37 ''point'':33 ''prevail'':98 ''propheci'':12 ''prophet'':21 ''receiv'':80 ''revel'':16,82 ''right'':57 ''russel'':60 ''see'':67 ''seership'':14 ''spiritu'':105 ''strengthen'':92 ''sweep'':84 ''testifi'':44 ''testimoni'':8 ''unto'':109 ''us'':34,72 ''use'':19,30 ''way'':24'::tsvector, '{"text":"All of his faith, all of his testimony, all of his prophecy and seership and revelation. Let''s use the prophets in the way they were meant to be used as they point us to better places. I''m grateful for them. I testify of their inspiration. I''m grateful for a Hezekiah at the helm right now in Russell and Nelson. It''s amazing to see as he is challenging us to learn to hear the Lord and receive personal revelation and sweep out the debris from our lives and strengthen our foundations and let God prevail in our lives as we build spiritual momentum in coming unto him.","seq_end":3023,"t_end_s":12904.726,"seq_start":3014,"t_start_s":12860.311,"episode_id":"unshaken-4pSrikfJ5Yw"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''alway'':59 ''back'':52 ''basebal'':94 ''beat'':124 ''believ'':16 ''come'':147 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''doubl'':102 ''doublehead'':89 ''earth'':13 ''elijah'':118 ''elisha'':144 ''equal'':135 ''ever'':130 ''faith'':10,44 ''fan'':95 ''featur'':103 ''find'':9 ''follow'':146 ''gonna'':73 ''half'':86 ''hard'':122 ''help'':17 ''instal'':99 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':58 ''last'':81,109 ''left'':79 ''lord'':14 ''m'':57 ''man'':5 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''ministri'':142 ''movi'':108 ''one'':38 ''origin'':138 ''pick'':75 ''prefer'':106 ''prophet'':117 ''re'':72,92 ''saint'':55 ''scriptur'':68 ''second'':85,98 ''sequel'':132 ''shaken'':50,54 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''spend'':62 ''spent'':112 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''thrill'':60 ''time'':63,114 ''today'':70 ''unbelief'':20 ''week'':82,110 ''welcom'':51'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Welcome back in Shaken Saints. I''m Jared, always thrilled to spend time with you in the scriptures. And today, we''re gonna be picking up where we left off last week with the second half of our doubleheader, if you''re a baseball fan, or the second installment of our double feature, if you prefer the movies. Last week, we spent our time with the prophet Elijah, and it''s hard to beat him. But if there were ever a sequel that was equal to the original, it''s the ministry of Elisha that follows.","seq_end":14,"t_end_s":64.64,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#372', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''amaz'':78 ''baptism'':14 ''best'':3 ''case'':4,20 ''cautious'':53 ''chastiti'':49 ''church'':137 ''clear'':60 ''compassion'':55 ''doesn'':30,129 ''drop'':26,34 ''explain'':64 ''faith'':42 ''girlfriend'':36,106,128 ''go'':24 ''god'':70 ''happen'':115 ''hey'':6 ''interest'':133 ''join'':135 ''knew'':86 ''know'':126 ''law'':47 ''let'':124 ''littl'':41 ''marriag'':11 ''meant'':89 ''need'':99 ''oh'':38 ''re'':110 ''said'':93 ''scenario'':5,21 ''serious'':68,73 ''spoke'':120 ''take'':94 ''talk'':101 ''taught'':44 ''time'':97 ''took'':83 ''tri'':62 ''us'':27,122,125 ''want'':32 ''well'':2,37 ''whatev'':108,114 ''worst'':19 ''ye'':39'::tsvector, '{"text":"Because, well, best case scenario, hey, we can have a marriage before the baptism. We do that. Or worst case scenario, He''s going to drop us because he doesn''t want to drop his girlfriend. Well, Oh ye of little faith, we taught him the law of chastity. We did it cautiously and compassionately, but we did it clearly and tried to explain this is is serious to God. Is it serious to you? And what amazed me was how he took it. He knew what it meant. And we we said, take all the time you need, but talk it over with your girlfriend and whatever we''re here for you, whatever happens. And and when he spoke with us, he let us know, my girlfriend doesn''t have any interest in joining the church.","seq_end":386,"t_end_s":1693.675,"seq_start":372,"t_start_s":1643.365,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#616', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''anymor'':32,83,96 ''cloth'':76,84,102,107 ''crust'':40 ''done'':6 ''earlier'':23 ''faith'':48 ''get'':98 ''give'':65 ''go'':36 ''god'':69 ''gonna'':28,35 ''hard'':39 ''heart'':41 ''ident'':24 ''life'':15 ''liter'':1 ''m'':26,34 ''made'':9,18 ''make'':85 ''man'':87,93 ''need'':29,54 ''offer'':20 ''oh'':58 ''oxen'':59 ''plant'':45 ''plow'':31,37 ''previous'':14 ''put'':104 ''rid'':99 ''sacrific'':11,63 ''seed'':46 ''tri'':43 ''well'':88 ''within'':49'::tsvector, '{"text":"Literally, what has he just done? He''s made a sacrifice of his previous life. He''s made an offering of his earlier identity. I''m not gonna need this plow anymore. I''m gonna go plow up hard crusted hearts and try to plant seeds of faith within them. I don''t need this for that. Oh, oxen? No, this is sacrifice and giving them up to God. He''s doing it again. My clothing? That''s not who I am anymore. Clothes make the man, well that''s not the man I am anymore, so get rid of that clothing and put on this clothing.","seq_end":628,"t_end_s":2676.61,"seq_start":616,"t_start_s":2637.56,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#679', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''actual'':36 ''also'':15 ''answer'':108 ''ask'':66 ''d'':57,83 ''didn'':70 ''doubt'':38 ''elijah'':11,75,114,116 ''elisha'':26,33 ''faith'':47 ''felt'':60 ''god'':9 ''happen'':55 ''hither'':22,24 ''knew'':51,77,106 ''lord'':8,118 ''mantl'':62 ''much'':31 ''part'':21,97 ''question'':68,111 ''real'':101 ''relief'':35,41 ''said'':4 ''say'':72 ''see'':91,94,99 ''seen'':84 ''sens'':58 ''smitten'':17 ''sourc'':102 ''strength'':104 ''think'':43,49 ''total'':46 ''veil'':96 ''water'':19 ''way'':88 ''went'':27,81 ''whole'':87 ''work'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"And then he said, where is the Lord God of Elijah? And when he also had smitten the waters, they parted hither and hither, and Elisha went over. It worked much to Elisha''s relief. Actually, I doubt it was relief. I think it was total faith. I think he knew what had just happened. He''d sensed and felt the mantle. And when he asked the question, he didn''t say, where is Elijah? He knew where he had went. He''d seen it the whole way. And by seeing it and seeing that veil part and seeing the real source of strength, he knew the answer to his question. Not about Elijah, about Elijah''s Lord.","seq_end":686,"t_end_s":2888.015,"seq_start":679,"t_start_s":2852.655,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#990', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''alway'':22 ''bear'':62,75,85,104 ''bless'':12 ''call'':82,97 ''choos'':9,32,38 ''curs'':17 ''day'':79 ''deal'':51 ''death'':31 ''decid'':46 ''differ'':40 ''faith'':14 ''full'':102 ''god'':45 ''goe'':101 ''know'':67 ''let'':44 ''life'':29,33 ''ll'':43 ''mama'':84,103 ''obvious'':37 ''oh'':76 ''phrase'':93 ''re'':36 ''rememb'':88 ''set'':26 ''somebodi'':100 ''someth'':39 ''thing'':65 ''two'':61 ''use'':90 ''want'':49 ''well'':34 ''wick'':19 ''would'':81'::tsvector, '{"text":"and he can do with you as he chooses. He will bless the faithful. He will curse the wicked as he always has. I will set before you life and death, choose life. Well, you''re obviously choosing something different and I''ll let God decide how he wants to deal with it. And how does he do it? With two bears. Now the thing we know about them is that they were she bears. Oh, in our day, we would call them mama bears. And you remember the use of the phrase, what do we call it when somebody goes full mama bear on you?","seq_end":998,"t_end_s":4117.385,"seq_start":990,"t_start_s":4085.295,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1194', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''alway'':14 ''anxieti'':75,87 ''anyth'':57 ''assum'':45 ''attitud'':62 ''battl'':68 ''borrow'':77 ''combin'':70,100,106 ''even'':51 ''faith'':72,81 ''fall'':38 ''flip'':32 ''go'':66 ''god'':25,83 ''good'':99 ''great'':74 ''hope'':35 ''jacob'':78 ''lost'':115 ''meantim'':28 ''moabit'':109 ''never'':37 ''see'':9 ''side'':33 ''someday'':2 ''take'':65 ''trap'':42 ''trust'':24 ''truth'':12 ''victori'':48 ''wait'':19 ''wake'':6 ''win'':59 ''won'':50 ''word'':80 ''work'':92 ''world'':4'::tsvector, '{"text":"Just someday the world will wake up and see what the truth has always been. And so we wait for that, and we trust God in the meantime. And on the flip side, I hope we never fall into the same trap and just assume that the victory is won even if we don''t do anything to win it. The attitude that we take going into battle, this combination of faith and great anxiety, to borrow Jacob''s words, Faith that God has it, but anxiety that we have some work to do ourselves. That''s a good combination. And it''s not the combination that the Moabites had. That''s why they lost.","seq_end":1201,"t_end_s":4984.274,"seq_start":1194,"t_start_s":4946.8,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1265', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''anyth'':28 ''begin'':20 ''bishop'':73,89 ''church'':84 ''corn'':15 ''end'':32 ''faith'':49 ''famili'':65 ''friend'':61 ''gift'':57 ''got'':12 ''gotta'':37 ''help'':100 ''least'':4 ''like'':93 ''m'':76 ''mean'':53 ''miracl'':22 ''multipl'':24 ''multipli'':27 ''need'':78,82,99 ''okay'':95 ''say'':74,91 ''see'':26 ''seed'':14 ''show'':69 ''someth'':7,18,39 ''start'':9,41 ''still'':31 ''thing'':92 ''welfar'':85 ''well'':1 ''wise'':88 ''zero'':30,34'::tsvector, '{"text":"Well, but at least we have something to start with. We got some seed corn. We have something to begin, a miracle of multiplication. You see multiplying anything by zero still ends up zero, so you gotta have something to start. What do you have? Do you have faith? Do you have means? Do you have gifts? Do you have friends? Do you have family? Don''t just show up to the Bishop saying, I''m in need and so I need some church welfare. Because a wise Bishop will say things like this, Okay, what do you need help with?","seq_end":1272,"t_end_s":5302.88,"seq_start":1265,"t_start_s":5267.15,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1279', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''asid'':74 ''bring'':16 ''call'':96 ''empti'':30,115 ''end'':61 ''faith'':97 ''fill'':35,46 ''filler'':52 ''find'':121 ''full'':78,107 ''god'':90 ''gonna'':100 ''guess'':48 ''happen'':101 ''know'':89 ''m'':27 ''make'':83 ''mani'':114 ''master'':51 ''need'':33,44 ''neighbor'':20,125 ''noth'':11 ''nothing'':21 ''oil'':110 ''one'':106,116 ''possibl'':119 ''pot'':31 ''pour'':64 ''rub'':5 ''say'':58 ''sens'':85 ''set'':73 ''shalt'':63,72 ''special'':91 ''surround'':28,111 ''thou'':62,71 ''tri'':3 ''vessel'':69,108 ''wait'':79,80 ''want'':13 ''well'':23,36 ''yeah'':37'::tsvector, '{"text":"Are you trying to rub it in that I have nothing? You want me to bring in all my neighbors nothingness as well and now I''m surrounded by empty pots in need of filling? Well, yeah, that''s the They are in need of filling, and guess who the master filler is? That''s why he says at the end, thou shalt pour out into all those vessels, and thou shalt set aside that which is full. Wait. Wait. What? This makes no sense at all. I know. God specializes in that. It''s called faith. What''s gonna happen is you have this one full vessel of oil surrounded by as many empty ones as you possibly can find from all your neighbors.","seq_end":1289,"t_end_s":5378.71,"seq_start":1279,"t_start_s":5336.195,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1290', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''actual'':10 ''ask'':18 ''bacon'':78 ''better'':35 ''boy'':61 ''bring'':38,59 ''close'':79 ''come'':98 ''door'':81 ''empti'':28,107 ''even'':22 ''faith'':97 ''full'':104 ''gonna'':75 ''help'':20 ''humbl'':95 ''humil'':16,44 ''involv'':6,52 ''man'':93 ''meek'':96 ''miracl'':57,88 ''noth'':37 ''offer'':31 ''part'':69 ''particip'':54 ''peopl'':8 ''pour'':102 ''re'':84 ''save'':76 ''seen'':91 ''sinc'':72 ''start'':101 ''vessel'':29 ''want'':3,11,64 ''weak'':48'::tsvector, '{"text":"So I want you to involve other people. I actually want you to have the humility to ask for help. And even if all they have is empty vessels to offer, then that''s better than nothing, bring them. So there''s some humility, there''s some weakness, there''s some involvement, some participation in this miracle yourself. Bring your boys in, I want them to be a part of it since this is gonna save their bacon. Close the door because we''re not doing this miracle to be seen of man, but humbly, meekly, faithfully come and then start pouring the full into the empty.","seq_end":1294,"t_end_s":5408.9,"seq_start":1290,"t_start_s":5378.95,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1548', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''accid'':111 ''ass'':59 ''assum'':87 ''bed'':22 ''brought'':14 ''call'':39 ''come'':70,138 ''contact'':7 ''day'':115,146,150 ''didn'':119 ''door'':31 ''faith'':94 ''find'':102 ''get'':4 ''god'':68,88 ''goe'':36 ''happen'':112,121 ''husband'':42 ''intent'':132 ''know'':75 ''lay'':24 ''littl'':21 ''make'':134 ''man'':66 ''may'':62 ''men'':54 ''need'':153 ''one'':50,56 ''pray'':48 ''prophet'':18,104,118,137 ''quick'':106 ''run'':63 ''said'':44 ''send'':45 ''shut'':29 ''solut'':83 ''sourc'':9 ''spiritu'':11 ''strength'':12 ''sure'':135 ''thee'':49 ''today'':142 ''upon'':32 ''young'':53'::tsvector, '{"text":"How can I get them in contact with sources of spiritual strength? She brought him to the prophet''s own little bed and lays him there. She then shuts the door upon him and she goes out. She called into her husband and said, send me, I pray thee, one of the young men and one of the asses that I may run to the man of God and come again. I don''t know what to do here. I have no solution, but I am assuming God does. I have I have faith in that, and so I have to find his prophet as quickly as I can. This accident happened on a day that the prophet didn''t happen to be with me, and so I have to be intentional about making sure a prophet comes to be here today. This is a day more than any day that I need him.","seq_end":1557,"t_end_s":6464.14,"seq_start":1548,"t_start_s":6420.175,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1597', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''24'':123 ''abl'':139 ''absolut'':11 ''action'':19 ''anxieti'':101 ''ass'':128 ''bring'':35,45 ''child'':37,50 ''come'':141 ''concern'':72 ''confus'':62 ''devast'':14 ''didn'':130 ''doesn'':54 ''donkey'':106 ''drive'':155 ''even'':132 ''faith'':95,111 ''fli'':109 ''get'':56,102,105,163 ''give'':119 ''go'':83 ''gonna'':25,28,34,44,152 ''gotta'':108 ''great'':100 ''husband'':53 ''like'':147 ''ll'':88 ''loss'':12 ''love'':3 ''m'':24,33,43,69,116 ''may'':149 ''need'':112,153 ''okay'':30,66,86 ''peac'':71 ''prophet'':40,47 ''respons'':8 ''saddl'':126 ''servant'':104,136 ''shalom'':67 ''start'':166 ''thing'':26,74,157,165 ''total'':61 ''tragedi'':10 ''tri'':117 ''vers'':122 ''wait'':133 ''work'':89,113 ''yet'':16'::tsvector, '{"text":"And I love that that''s her response to tragedy, absolute loss and devastation, and yet it''s action and it''s I''m gonna things are gonna be okay, and I''m gonna bring this child to the prophet, and I''m gonna bring the prophet to the child, and my husband doesn''t get it, and he''s totally confused, and that''s okay. Shalom. I''m at peace concerning these things, and you can be too. It''s all going to be okay. It''ll work out. So there''s my faith. Now where''s my great anxiety? Get the servant, get donkey, we gotta fly. My faith needs works and I''m trying to give both. So verse 24, then she saddled an ass. So didn''t even wait for the servant to be able to come and do it. It''s like, he may he''s gonna need to drive the thing for me, but I can get this thing started.","seq_end":1605,"t_end_s":6674.865,"seq_start":1597,"t_start_s":6625.8,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#1757', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''accord'':21 ''apostl'':45 ''awak'':9 ''believ'':63,92 ''child'':6 ''come'':30 ''concern'':50 ''could'':65,71 ''couldn'':53 ''didn'':11,14,18,74 ''even'':60 ''faith'':88 ''go'':20 ''hand'':49 ''happen'':16 ''heal'':55 ''jame'':38 ''jesus'':27,80 ''john'':40 ''littl'':87 ''man'':57 ''mount'':33 ''need'':90 ''nine'':44 ''oh'':84 ''peter'':37 ''plan'':24 ''problem'':101 ''respons'':81 ''say'':4 ''son'':59 ''though'':61 ''thought'':68 ''told'':2 ''transfigur'':35 ''well'':77 ''work'':76 ''wring'':47 ''ye'':85'::tsvector, '{"text":"He told him saying, the child is not awake. It didn''t it didn''t happen. It didn''t go according to our plan. This is Jesus as he comes down the Mount Of Transfiguration with Peter, James, and John, and the other nine apostles are wringing their hands concerned that we couldn''t heal this man''s son even though we believed we could, and he thought that we could too. It didn''t work. Well, what''s Jesus'' response to them? Oh, ye of little faith. You need to believe more than you did. Is that the same problem here?","seq_end":1764,"t_end_s":7362.885,"seq_start":1757,"t_start_s":7328.595,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2009', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''amaz'':73 ''blank'':68 ''come'':92 ''condit'':69 ''didn'':25 ''divin'':10 ''eclips'':44 ''enemi'':106 ''even'':12,104 ''faith'':17 ''fill'':65 ''god'':4 ''good'':89 ''guy'':19,22 ''hap'':24 ''happen'':28 ''household'':15 ''keep'':80 ''know'':102 ''leprosi'':35 ''let'':40 ''man'':2 ''naaman'':86 ''one'':100 ''outsid'':13 ''peopl'':55 ''perspect'':84 ''proper'':83 ''purpos'':11 ''rais'':5 ''reduc'':57 ''seem'':107 ''sens'':109 ''someon'':41 ''strength'':48 ''thing'':81 ''think'':53 ''tragic'':51 ''two'':94 ''use'':8 ''vers'':93 ''weak'':43 ''would'':38 ''yeah'':20,31,32,70'::tsvector, '{"text":"The man that God raised up and used for divine purposes even outside the household of faith? That guy? Yeah. That guy. He hap didn''t he happen to have yeah. Yeah. He had leprosy. But why would you let someone''s weakness eclipse all of their strengths? It''s tragic to think of people being reduced down to their, but he was a fill in the blank condition. Yeah. She''s amazing, but she can we can we keep things in proper perspective? And Naaman was as good as they come. Verse two, he''s not the only one that knows it. Even his enemies seem to sense it.","seq_end":2021,"t_end_s":8321.19,"seq_start":2009,"t_start_s":8278.065,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2185', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''answer'':111 ''ask'':79 ''attend'':123 ''baptiz'':90 ''church'':120 ''come'':55 ''done'':9 ''end'':101 ''endur'':98 ''epic'':28 ''everyth'':23 ''exercis'':81 ''faith'':82 ''find'':70 ''go'':118 ''god'':57 ''herculean'':40,49 ''labor'':41,50 ''legend'':30 ''let'':2 ''level'':26 ''lift'':22 ''ll'':74 ''miracl'':53 ''myth'':32 ''often'':18 ''oh'':34 ''okay'':42 ''perform'':47 ''pray'':116 ''primari'':110 ''read'':112 ''realli'':58 ''repent'':84 ''scriptur'':114 ''serv'':122 ''simpl'':5,60 ''sin'':87 ''spirit'':96 ''spiritu'':105 ''strength'':106 ''templ'':125 ''think'':16 ''want'':20,104 ''wasn'':13 ''water'':92 ''way'':63 ''would'':7'::tsvector, '{"text":"Then let it be simple. You would have done it if it wasn''t. I think too often we want to lift everything to the level of epic and legend and myth and, oh, it has to be the Herculean labors. Okay? And if I can perform those Herculean labors, then the miracle will come where God really is. Simple is the way. But few there be there that find it. If you''ll just do as I ask, just exercise faith and repent of your sins and be baptized by water and by the spirit and endure to the end. Just you want spiritual strength? Then do the primary answers. Read your scriptures and pray and go to church and serve. Attend the temple.","seq_end":2195,"t_end_s":9066.585,"seq_start":2185,"t_start_s":9022.105,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2487', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''abl'':5 ''afford'':7 ''american'':22 ''among'':30 ''anyway'':121 ''architect'':116 ''build'':94,95,102,125 ''byu'':47 ''car'':11 ''civil'':51 ''d'':123 ''educ'':41 ''engin'':25,52,58 ''faith'':126 ''focus'':130 ''freshman'':44 ''geolog'':56 ''gift'':17 ''god'':106 ''help'':37 ''kind'':113 ''kingdom'':104 ''know'':111 ''let'':128 ''ll'':2,14 ''major'':49 ''mission'':78,85 ''much'':97 ''never'':3 ''one'':8 ''prerequisit'':66 ''program'':72 ''rather'':124 ''realiz'':87 ''rest'':69 ''societi'':23 ''take'':15,64 ''teach'':138 ''thank'':18,34 ''took'':55 ''tri'':62 ''want'':27,92,100,136 ''well'':42 ''went'':82 ''would'':118 ''year'':45'::tsvector, '{"text":"I''ll never be able to afford one of your cars but I''ll take your gift. Thank you. And the American Society of Engineers, I want to be among you. And so thank you for helping me with my education. Well, my freshman year at BYU, my major was civil engineering. And I took geology for engineers and I was trying to take some prerequisites for the rest of the program and so on before my mission. And then I went on my mission and realized that I don''t want to build buildings as much as I want to build the kingdom of God, and I don''t know what kind of an architect I would have been anyway. I''d rather build faith, so let''s focus on that, and I just want to teach.","seq_end":2494,"t_end_s":10368.851,"seq_start":2487,"t_start_s":10331.064,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2503', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''000'':45,78 ''3'':77 ''9'':44 ''american'':24,67 ''anoth'':43 ''appli'':57 ''becom'':18 ''bmw'':12,64,128 ''care'':30 ''civil'':102 ''conscienc'':41 ''construct'':33 ''doesn'':28 ''engin'':27,70,103 ''even'':121 ''faith'':34 ''fine'':5 ''freshman'':94 ''gave'':80 ''get'':91 ''give'':51 ''good'':7,40 ''help'':89 ''isn'':13 ''kind'':124 ''last'':114 ''letter'':62 ''longer'':56 ''love'':98,119 ''money'':54 ''oh'':11 ''pay'':15 ''purpos'':48 ''realiz'':10 ''seminari'':20 ''share'':126 ''societi'':25,68 ''studi'':101 ''take'':42 ''teacher'':21 ''thank'':73,86 ''three'':82 ''time'':100 ''two'':115 ''ve'':109 ''well'':1 ''whoever'':129 ''wrote'':60,134 ''year'':83,95,116'::tsvector, '{"text":"Well, that was all fine and good until I realized, oh, BMW isn''t paying me to become a seminary teacher. And the American Society of Engineers doesn''t care about me constructing faith. And I can''t in good conscience take another $9,000 when the purpose of them giving me that money no longer applies. So I wrote a letter to BMW and the American Society of Engineers and I thanked them for the $3,000 they gave me three years before. So thank you, that helped me get through my freshman year and I loved my time studying civil engineering but this is what I''ve been doing for the last two years and I love this even more. I kind of shared with BMW, whoever it was that I wrote to, that this is","seq_end":2511,"t_end_s":10459.891,"seq_start":2503,"t_start_s":10408.825,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2773', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''21'':82 ''along'':119 ''alreadi'':4 ''apostl'':70 ''behold'':40 ''bless'':95 ''c'':80 ''chariot'':48 ''come'':97 ''could'':65 ''d'':78 ''distanc'':75 ''elisha'':53,126 ''eye'':7,28,59 ''faith'':92,98 ''fire'':50 ''full'':44 ''get'':114 ''help'':15 ''hope'':128 ''hors'':46 ''ll'':86 ''lord'':25 ''man'':32 ''meantim'':111 ''mountain'':42 ''need'':12 ''obedi'':117 ''open'':26 ''patienc'':90,108 ''pleas'':14 ''prophet'':68,88 ''re'':105 ''round'':51 ''saw'':35 ''section'':81 ''see'':2,17,39,66,72,102,106 ''seer'':10,62 ''servant'':132 ''someday'':101 ''thing'':18 ''trust'':87 ''way'':20,121 ''young'':31'::tsvector, '{"text":"You see, I already have the eyes of a seer. He needs them. Please help him see things the way I do. And the Lord opened the eyes of the young man, and he saw. What did he see? Behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire round about Elisha. If we only had the eyes of a seer, if we could see what prophets and apostles can see from a distance, that''s D and C section 21, that if you''ll trust prophets with patience and faith, then the blessings will come. Faith that will someday see what they''re seeing and patience in the meantime until we get there. But obedience all along the way. And that''s what Elisha is hoping for for this servant.","seq_end":2786,"t_end_s":11658.77,"seq_start":2773,"t_start_s":11607.319,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2787', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''2001'':79 ''absolut'':123 ''apostl'':107 ''attack'':77,100 ''bednar'':68 ''board'':85 ''byu'':94 ''church'':84 ''concern'':113 ''could'':3 ''describ'':70 ''develop'':49 ''educ'':87 ''either'':62 ''elder'':67 ''eleven'':75 ''eye'':31,51 ''faith'':53 ''fear'':11,61,125 ''give'':28 ''go'':117 ''god'':42 ''idaho'':95 ''let'':26 ''meet'':88 ''nine'':74 ''noth'':57 ''pray'':40 ''presid'':92 ''proof'':35 ''prophet'':105 ''recogn'':110 ''right'':97 ''see'':5,33 ''short'':72 ''side'':22 ''sight'':45 ''spiritu'':44 ''think'':64 ''told'':14 ''us'':59 ''world'':121'::tsvector, '{"text":"If you could just see what''s out there. No fear. I just told you that there''s more on our side than theirs. Now let me give you the eyes to see the proof. And if we can pray for God''s spiritual sight, if we can develop the eye of faith, then there''s nothing for us to fear either. I think it was elder Bednar who described that shortly after nine eleven, the attacks in 2001. He was in the church board of education meeting because he was president of BYU Idaho. And right after the attacks, he''s there with prophets and apostles, and he recognized in them concern for what was going on in the world, but absolutely no fear.","seq_end":2796,"t_end_s":11701.706,"seq_start":2787,"t_start_s":11659.569,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#2987', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''absolut'':10 ''actual'':70 ''aren'':95 ''bless'':28 ''channel'':52 ''could'':32 ''dumbfound'':6 ''econom'':45 ''elisha'':51 ''enough'':39 ''even'':33,38,92 ''faith'':91,97 ''funni'':64 ''get'':101 ''go'':7,57 ''god'':21,81 ''gonna'':100 ''handl'':34,106 ''heaven'':17,61 ''imposs'':11 ''inner'':54 ''kind'':43 ''make'':41 ''malachi'':55,78 ''mean'':13 ''measur'':79 ''oh'':58 ''open'':22 ''overnight'':47 ''pictur'':50 ''pour'':26,85 ''re'':99 ''say'':67 ''see'':75 ''switch'':46 ''total'':5 ''will'':83 ''window'':15,19,63'::tsvector, '{"text":"But there he is totally dumbfounded going, that''s absolutely impossible. I mean, if windows if heaven had windows and God opened them up and poured out blessings more than we could even handle, that''s not even enough to make that kind of economic switch overnight. I can picture Elisha channeling his inner Malachi and going, oh, as if heaven had windows? Funny you should say that. It actually does. And you should see the the Malachi measure that God is willing to pour out to those that are faithful. Even those that aren''t faithful, you''re gonna get more than you can handle.","seq_end":2996,"t_end_s":12570.649,"seq_start":2987,"t_start_s":12534.83,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#3044', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''anti'':8,83 ''around'':137 ''battl'':132 ''choos'':128 ''claim'':43 ''clue'':59 ''creep'':38 ''destroy'':14 ''doubt'':23,37,106 ''faith'':16,67 ''fals'':51 ''feel'':122 ''get'':119,125 ''head'':109 ''hear'':30 ''heart'':112 ''instead'':18 ''ironi'':4 ''knowledg'':71 ''leav'':35,130 ''literatur'':10 ''make'':93,114 ''mean'':53 ''mind'':26 ''mormon'':9 ''much'':7 ''natur'':64 ''nervous'':120 ''nois'':32,75,94 ''peopl'':34,41 ''plant'':20,103 ''proof'':46 ''psycholog'':97 ''religi'':66,70,84 ''rhetor'':85,87 ''run'':139 ''scare'':126 ''seed'':21,104 ''start'':29 ''studi'':82 ''thing'':117,123 ''think'':116 ''tri'':101 ''turn'':136 ''use'':91 ''warfar'':98'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s the irony of so much anti Mormon literature. They can''t destroy your faith, so instead they plant seeds of doubt in the mind and you start hearing the noise of people leaving or doubts creeping up or people that claim to have proof that it''s all false, which means they don''t have a clue as to what the nature of religious faith is and religious knowledge. It''s just noises out there. That''s why I studied anti religious rhetoric because rhetoric is what is used to make noises. It''s psychological warfare. It''s trying to plant seeds of doubt in the head or the heart to make you think things and get nervous or feel things and get scared and choose to leave the battle yourself and just turn around and run.","seq_end":3055,"t_end_s":12855.105,"seq_start":3044,"t_start_s":12806.739,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8#3708', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 2 Kings 1-13 - Passing the Mantle', '''along'':120 ''altar'':57 ''armor'':17 ''away'':86 ''burn'':113 ''come'':41,44 ''context'':8 ''crown'':79,88 ''defend'':37 ''earth'':91 ''everi'':90 ''faith'':35 ''fals'':93,96,99,102 ''god'':19,76,94,118 ''guard'':48 ''hous'':74 ''king'':103 ''kingdom'':51 ''lesser'':105 ''light'':106,110 ''love'':2 ''make'':58 ''preserv'':69 ''priest'':100 ''process'':84 ''proper'':60 ''prophet'':97 ''readi'':22 ''sacrific'':61 ''sanctiti'':71 ''shield'':12,33 ''spear'':10 ''spirit'':30 ''stand'':47,54,64 ''sword'':27 ''take'':85 ''templ'':67,116 ''think'':3 ''togeth'':45 ''true'':109 ''usurp'':92'::tsvector, '{"text":"I love thinking of this in that context, that spears and shields do we have the armor of God at the ready? Do we have the sword of the spirit and the shield of faith to defend him when he comes? Will we come together and stand guard at his kingdom? Will we stand by the altar making the proper sacrifices? Will we stand at the temple to preserve the sanctity of the house of God? Will we crown him, and in the process, take away the crown from every earthly usurper? False gods and false prophets and false priests and false kings and lesser lights when a true light has been burning in the temple of God all along.","seq_end":3718,"t_end_s":15830.865,"seq_start":3708,"t_start_s":15785.141,"episode_id":"unshaken-6lXWLIOUKC8"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''add'':151 ''back'':58 ''battl'':64 ''bear'':72 ''believ'':16 ''better'':99 ''book'':157 ''boyd'':135 ''channel'':132 ''cold'':66 ''come'':160 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''day'':90,92,94 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''ever'':115 ''faith'':10,44 ''feel'':98 ''film'':89,107 ''find'':9 ''friend'':53 ''go'':126 ''gravelli'':147 ''gravita'':154 ''halverson'':55 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''hope'':79,96,143 ''inner'':134 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':54 ''joshua'':159 ''k'':136 ''kimbal'':141 ''know'':111 ''land'':121 ''littl'':146 ''ll'':114,129 ''lord'':14 ''m'':77 ''make'':81,116 ''man'':5 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''one'':38 ''packer'':137 ''pleas'':71 ''postpon'':88 ''promis'':120 ''raspi'':148 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''sound'':149 ''spencer'':139 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''time'':127 ''today'':84 ''tri'':130 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':60 ''ve'':62,86 ''voic'':75 ''w'':140 ''week'':68 ''welcom'':57'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello my friends, Jared Halverson here. Welcome back to Unshaken. I''ve been battling a cold all week and so please bear with my voice. I''m just hoping to make it through today. I''ve been postponing filming day after day after day in hopes of feeling better. And by now, if I don''t film, I don''t know if I''ll ever make it into the promised land. And so it''s go time. I''ll try to channel my inner Boyd K. Packer and Spencer W. Kimball in hopes that a little gravelly raspy sound will add to the gravitas of the book of Joshua.","seq_end":11,"t_end_s":66.33,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#91', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''abl'':82 ''actual'':13 ''amaz'':33 ''anoth'':76 ''anyth'':49 ''christ'':11 ''compar'':50 ''die'':67,69 ''faith'':98 ''feel'':25 ''fill'':6,29,84 ''generat'':70 ''grandpar'':43 ''group'':18 ''hear'':35 ''imagin'':3 ''jesus'':10 ''left'':92 ''legaci'':96 ''must'':28 ''one'':77 ''parent'':40 ''peopl'':89 ''pioneer'':57 ''seminari'':20 ''shoe'':8,23,86 ''student'':21 ''talk'':15,37,54,60 ''tri'':4 ''us'':93 ''ve'':59 ''wonder'':65,66,68'::tsvector, '{"text":"Can you imagine trying to fill the shoes of Jesus Christ? I actually once talked to a group of seminary students about shoes they feel that they must fill. And it was amazing to hear them talk about their parents and their grandparents, and how will I be anything compared to them. Them talking about the pioneers. We''ve talked about this with the wonder, wonder, die, wonder, die generations. And will we just be another one? Or will we be able to fill the shoes of those people who have left us such a legacy of faith?","seq_end":97,"t_end_s":478.56,"seq_start":91,"t_start_s":446.19,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#400', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''accord'':104 ''along'':69 ''amaz'':67 ''ask'':66 ''book'':79 ''canaan'':32 ''conquer'':36 ''counsel'':68 ''cross'':28 ''day'':95 ''depart'':85 ''eight'':61 ''emot'':12 ''faith'':5 ''feel'':15 ''fill'':3 ''glad'':64 ''jordan'':23 ''joshua'':77 ''know'':18 ''law'':82 ''lesser'':11 ''line'':72 ''lord'':74 ''m'':2 ''mayest'':100 ''medit'':93 ''midst'':40 ''mouth'':89 ''night'':97 ''nine'':57 ''observ'':101 ''oh'':62 ''one'':48 ''repetit'':44 ''river'':24 ''room'':9 ''saw'':52 ''say'':75 ''seven'':55 ''shall'':83 ''shalt'':92 ''six'':53 ''squeak'':46 ''therein'':94,110 ''thi'':88 ''thou'':91,99 ''three'':43 ''vers'':50 ''well'':58 ''written'':109'::tsvector, '{"text":"I''m filled with faith. There''s no room for lesser emotions. And to feel that, to know that, there''s no Jordan River we can''t cross. There''s no Canaan we can''t conquer. Now in the midst of those three repetitions, he squeaks in one other verse. We saw six and seven and nine. Well, what about eight? Oh, so glad you asked. Amazing counsel along the same lines. The Lord says to Joshua, this book of the law shall not depart out of thy mouth, but thou shalt meditate therein day and night that thou mayest observe to do according to all that is written therein.","seq_end":409,"t_end_s":1606.705,"seq_start":400,"t_start_s":1565.355,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#499', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''ahead'':104 ''apostl'':71 ''ask'':82,87 ''book'':18 ''courag'':56,112 ''encourag'':11,26,75 ''even'':78 ''faith'':90,114 ''follow'':99 ''give'':110 ''god'':33 ''good'':55 ''got'':29,35 ''honest'':61 ''hous'':13,23 ''israel'':15,25 ''joshua'':10,27,31 ''know'':58 ''lie'':103 ''live'':68 ''ll'':8 ''love'':2 ''need'':73 ''peopl'':5 ''prayer'':85 ''prophet'':69 ''see'':9,21 ''sens'':65 ''someth'':94 ''strong'':51 ''sure'':109 ''though'':79 ''throughout'':16 ''trust'':37,41,46 ''us'':77 ''whatev'':102 ''will'':97'::tsvector, '{"text":"I love that the people are we''ll see Joshua encouraging the house of Israel throughout this book, but to see the house of Israel encouraging Joshua, you got this, Joshua, because God''s got you. Trust in that. We trust in that, and we trust in you. So be strong. Be of a good courage. You know, to be honest, I don''t sense from our living prophets and apostles any need of encouragement from us, even though they do ask for our prayers and ask for our faith. But there''s something about being willing to follow them into whatever lies ahead that does, I am sure, give them courage and faith.","seq_end":508,"t_end_s":1975.195,"seq_start":499,"t_start_s":1933.715,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#538', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''10'':56 ''12'':15 ''caleb'':35 ''came'':89 ''d'':6 ''even'':47,51,83 ''faith'':32,66 ''fear'':57 ''funni'':4 ''generat'':22 ''give'':53 ''go'':69,79 ''gonna'':52 ''harlot'':92 ''heroin'':110 ''hous'':94 ''israel'':20 ''jericho'':84 ''joshua'':33 ''land'':74,82 ''like'':43 ''lodg'':98 ''m'':49 ''name'':95 ''need'':102 ''one'':58 ''option'':60 ''part'':12 ''paus'':107 ''promis'':73 ''rahab'':96,111 ''rememb'':25 ''said'':76 ''scope'':70 ''send'':8 ''spi'':16,67 ''stop'':104 ''two'':9,29,65 ''view'':80 ''want'':64 ''went'':18,87 ''wonder'':39 ''yeah'':44'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now it''s funny he''d only send two. He was part of the 12 spies that went into Israel a generation before. But remember there were only two that were faithful, Joshua and Caleb? So here I wonder if he''s like, yeah, don''t even I''m not even gonna give the the 10 fearful ones an option. So I just want two faithful spies to go scope out the promised land. He said to them, go view the land, even Jericho. And they went and came into an harlot''s house named Rahab and lodged there. Now we need to stop here and pause on this heroine, Rahab.","seq_end":546,"t_end_s":2108.375,"seq_start":538,"t_start_s":2072.84,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#824', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''armi'':61 ''blood'':15 ''care'':91 ''destroy'':60 ''even'':36,90 ''faith'':85 ''familiar'':73 ''greater'':37 ''guiltless'':4 ''hand'':23 ''harm'':69 ''head'':20 ''home'':79 ''hous'':13,48,50,107 ''ill'':109 ''live'':84 ''long'':42 ''longer'':100 ''mark'':53,77 ''one'':95,102 ''pass'':63 ''point'':96,103 ''re'':45 ''reput'':110 ''scarlet'':75 ''see'':40 ''shall'':7,16 ''someth'':74 ''sound'':72 ''symbol'':38 ''take'':34 ''thee'':10 ''token'':33,57 ''true'':32,56 ''upon'':25 ''whosoev'':6 ''within'':86'::tsvector, '{"text":"We will be guiltless, and whosoever shall be with thee in the house, his blood shall be on our head if any hand be upon him. Now this is where the true token takes on even greater symbolism. You see, as long as they''re in the house, the house that is marked by this true token, then our destroying armies will pass by and do them no harm. Is this sounding familiar? Something scarlet to mark the home of those who are living faithfully within. I don''t even care that this at one point, it is no longer. At one point, this was a house of ill repute.","seq_end":844,"t_end_s":3111.33,"seq_start":824,"t_start_s":3061.07,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1024', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''ankl'':79 ''chest'':88 ''discuss'':3 ''evid'':24 ''exodus'':26 ''faith'':55 ''final'':97 ''forward'':50 ''generat'':11 ''get'':76 ''jewish'':18,28 ''judah'':39 ''knee'':82 ''leader'':34 ''miracl'':13 ''mose'':47 ''move'':49 ''neck'':91 ''nostril'':94 ''one'':33 ''open'':98 ''part'':60 ''possibl'':7 ''prior'':10 ''red'':16 ''said'':40,48 ''sea'':17 ''start'':68 ''surf'':73 ''tradit'':19,29 ''tribe'':37 ''wade'':69 ''waist'':85 ''wait'':45 ''water'':58 ''way'':100 ''well'':41'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now we discussed this as a possibility in that prior generation''s miracle of the Red Sea. Jewish tradition, we don''t have evidence in Exodus, but Jewish tradition was that that one leader from the tribe of Judah said, well, what are we waiting for? Moses said, move forward, and he has the faith that the water will part, so so do I. And so he starts wading in through the surf, and it gets to his ankles and his knees and his waist and his chest and his neck and his nostrils before it finally opens the way.","seq_end":1032,"t_end_s":3803.465,"seq_start":1024,"t_start_s":3770.245,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1033', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''actual'':16,24 ''ahead'':88 ''beauti'':6 ''believ'':93 ''brim'':83 ''challeng'':86 ''dip'':78 ''faith'':37,42,56 ''feet'':75,80 ''first'':77 ''get'':73 ''gonna'':70 ''happen'':17 ''help'':94 ''histori'':25 ''know'':11 ''lie'':87 ''lord'':91 ''mine'':96 ''miracl'':40 ''need'':71 ''part'':66 ''preced'':38 ''principl'':28,33,35,44,58 ''probabl'':69 ''re'':68 ''receiv'':47 ''river'':64 ''taught'':30 ''thou'':95 ''tradit'':7 ''trial'':53 ''unbelief'':97 ''want'':62 ''wet'':76 ''whatev'':85 ''wit'':49'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now again, that''s a beautiful tradition. I don''t know if it if it actually happened, but here, now we have the actual history where the principle is taught, the same principle. The principle that faith precedes the miracle. The faith the principle that we receive no witness until after the trial of our faith. The principle that if you want the river to part, you''re probably gonna need to get your feet wet first. Dip your feet in the brim of whatever challenge lies ahead of you. Lord, I believe, help thou mine unbelief.","seq_end":1047,"t_end_s":3846.37,"seq_start":1033,"t_start_s":3804.105,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1048', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''17'':80 ''among'':76 ''ark'':86 ''bear'':84 ''begin'':57,61 ''believ'':59 ''coven'':89 ''faith'':47 ''fine'':1 ''firm'':94 ''forward'':7 ''god'':67 ''great'':98 ''inch'':6,63 ''initi'':18 ''ll'':55 ''lord'':92 ''miracl'':20 ''part'':15 ''pile'':33 ''power'':38 ''prepar'':71 ''priest'':82 ''principl'':41 ''promis'':69 ''put'':49 ''see'':73 ''someth'':37 ''start'':5,23,31 ''stood'':93 ''toe'':51 ''toward'':66 ''us'':77 ''verb'':99 ''vers'':79 ''wade'':25 ''wait'':11 ''water'':17,28 ''way'':65 ''wonder'':74 ''work'':75'::tsvector, '{"text":"Fine, I will, but start inching forward. And don''t wait for me to part the water. Initiate the miracle yourself by starting to wade into the water before it starts to pile up. There''s something powerful about that principle. And if we have the faith to put our toe in, if we''ll just begin to believe and begin to inch our way toward God''s promises, Then prepare to see wonders worked among us. In verse 17, the priests that bear the ark of the covenant of the Lord stood firm. That''s a great verb too.","seq_end":1071,"t_end_s":3906.725,"seq_start":1048,"t_start_s":3847.875,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1072', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''best'':121 ''better'':10 ''claim'':59 ''clean'':47 ''cross'':115 ''damn'':93 ''deiti'':95 ''dramat'':88 ''dri'':25,39 ''enter'':119 ''entir'':81 ''experi'':129,136 ''faith'':19 ''firm'':12,23 ''forth'':107 ''ground'':26,40 ''hold'':7,98 ''israelit'':35 ''jordan'':31,49 ''keep'':103 ''less'':87 ''let'':17 ''like'':51 ''littl'':73 ''midst'':29 ''mine'':69 ''miracl'':5,57 ''oh'':67,96 ''parent'':53,139 ''pass'':36,46 ''past'':135 ''path'':113 ''peopl'':44 ''person'':128 ''red'':82 ''reli'':131 ''river'':74,90 ''rush'':106 ''sea'':83 ''someon'':97 ''stand'':11 ''stood'':22 ''upon'':132 ''wall'':100 ''want'':3 ''water'':102 ''waver'':20 ''way'':117 ''whole'':78'::tsvector, '{"text":"If you want the miracle to hold, then you better stand firm in it. Don''t let the faith waver. They stood firm on dry ground in the midst of Jordan. And all the Israelites passed over on dry ground until all the people were passed clean over Jordan. Just like your parents, they had a miracle to claim as their own. Now you do too. Oh, but mine''s just a little river, theirs was the whole, was an entire Red Sea. Is it any less dramatic? A river that is damned by deity. Oh, someone holding that wall of water, keeping it from rushing forth so that you have a path to cross, a way to enter, and best of all, you now have a personal experience to rely upon, not just past experiences from your parents.","seq_end":1087,"t_end_s":3963.885,"seq_start":1072,"t_start_s":3906.965,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1221', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''abl'':79,97 ''behind'':15,25 ''come'':22 ''ear'':32 ''experi'':75 ''faith'':62 ''father'':65 ''give'':51 ''grow'':57 ''imag'':48 ''incred'':55 ''jordan'':110 ''know'':83,89 ''legaci'':14 ''live'':11 ''love'':42,45 ''matur'':3 ''mental'':47 ''mother'':67 ''parent'':91 ''re'':34 ''readi'':35,59 ''red'':105 ''religion'':29 ''river'':111 ''say'':81 ''sea'':106 ''see'':99 ''sneak'':23 ''spiritu'':74 ''testimoni'':93 ''us'':52 ''ve'':7,10 ''want'':60,69,76 ''whisper'':28 ''youth'':4,56'::tsvector, '{"text":"These are mature youth. They they''ve been they''ve lived with a legacy behind them. You don''t have to come sneak up behind them and whisper religion into their ears. They''re ready for more than that. But I love, I just love that mental image that he gives us of these incredible youth growing up ready, wanting the faith that their fathers and mothers have. Wanting to have their own spiritual experiences. Wanting to be able to say, I know for myself, not just, I know my parents have testimonies. And to be able to see that here, we had our Red Sea, you have your Jordan River.","seq_end":1235,"t_end_s":4510.555,"seq_start":1221,"t_start_s":4461.895,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1265', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''baptism'':49 ''children'':19,42 ''coven'':5,16,74 ''dnc'':23 ''done'':81 ''eight'':25,59 ''faith'':45 ''five'':27 ''ghost'':53 ''hadn'':8 ''haven'':79,85 ''head'':96 ''holi'':52 ''much'':30 ''old'':61 ''parent'':34,78,99 ''pass'':10,87 ''peopl'':1 ''readi'':70 ''rememb'':22 ''repent'':47 ''sin'':92 ''sixti'':24 ''take'':72 ''teach'':40 ''time'':56,67 ''token'':13 ''took'':3 ''twenti'':26 ''understand'':44 ''upon'':6,75 ''word'':64 ''year'':60 ''zion'':36'::tsvector, '{"text":"People who took the covenant upon themselves hadn''t passed on the token of that covenant to their children. Do you remember DNC sixty eight twenty five? In as much as there are parents in Zion that do not teach their children to understand faith and repentance and baptism in the Holy Ghost, by the time they are eight years old, in other words, by the time they are ready to take the covenant upon themselves, if parents haven''t done that, if they haven''t passed it on, then the sin be on the heads of the parents.","seq_end":1270,"t_end_s":4663.875,"seq_start":1265,"t_start_s":4633.525,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1281', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''actual'':107 ''also'':37 ''build'':75 ''circumcis'':98 ''coven'':9,47,66 ''cross'':30 ''dad'':57,64 ''day'':105 ''enough'':51 ''exact'':89 ''faith'':78 ''get'':67,71 ''god'':85 ''interest'':15,111 ''israel'':103 ''ll'':19 ''make'':80 ''men'':101 ''miracl'':33,59,70 ''mom'':55,62 ''one'':2 ''peopl'':92 ''promis'':83 ''put'':20 ''readi'':5,38 ''reli'':53 ''say'':108 ''symbol'':113 ''take'':7,40 ''testimoni'':74 ''thing'':112 ''token'':44 ''two'':109 ''upon'':10,41,54 ''ve'':25 ''water'':32 ''way'':23 ''well'':12,17'::tsvector, '{"text":"This one, are you ready to take the covenant upon yourself? Well, it''s interesting that, well, I''ll put it this way. You''ve now had your own crossing the water miracle. Are you now also ready to take upon yourself the token of the covenant? It''s not enough to rely upon mom and dad''s miracles nor on mom and dad''s covenants. Get your own miracles, get your own testimony, build your own faith, and make your own promises with God. And that''s exactly what these people will do. They are all circumcised, all the men of Israel that day, which actually says two other interesting things symbolically.","seq_end":1295,"t_end_s":4750.315,"seq_start":1281,"t_start_s":4702.53,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1348', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''arm'':106 ''armi'':80 ''behind'':7 ''complet'':76 ''cross'':51 ''cut'':11,56 ''easi'':14 ''enemi'':30,48,52 ''enter'':47 ''eye'':38 ''faith'':92 ''far'':35 ''final'':46 ''first'':66 ''flesh'':108 ''flow'':5 ''go'':74 ''god'':93 ''gonna'':70 ''incapacit'':77 ''incred'':89 ''intend'':25 ''land'':23 ''leap'':90 ''lie'':100 ''line'':53 ''militari'':84 ''path'':60 ''promis'':22 ''re'':19,69,73 ''retreat'':17,62 ''river'':2 ''see'':40 ''stay'':27 ''stretch'':32 ''tactic'':85 ''territori'':31 ''thing'':67 ''trust'':95 ''ve'':45,50,55 ''victori'':98 ''way'':15 ''wise'':83'::tsvector, '{"text":"The river is now flowing again behind them, which has cut off any easy way of retreat. We''re in the promised land, we intend to stay. But now enemy territory stretches off as far as the eye can see. So now that we''ve finally entered enemy we''ve crossed enemy lines, we''ve cut off our own path of retreat. What''s the first thing we''re gonna do? We''re going to completely incapacitate our own army. Not very wise military tactics. Then again, an incredible leap of faith. God, we trust that the victory will lie in you, not in the arm of flesh.","seq_end":1362,"t_end_s":4979.63,"seq_start":1348,"t_start_s":4933.135,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1522', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''around'':105 ''brick'':64 ''bring'':4,89 ''chapter'':20 ''citi'':13 ''close'':30 ''come'':53,113 ''conquer'':11 ''difficult'':77,87 ''doesn'':57 ''faith'':46 ''feel'':93 ''go'':109 ''god'':98 ''gospel'':81 ''ll'':15 ''loos'':63 ''love'':49 ''metaphor'':22 ''none'':108,112 ''re'':36 ''see'':16 ''seem'':29,59 ''share'':39,79 ''someon'':28 ''testimoni'':43 ''time'':78,88 ''tri'':37 ''truth'':96 ''us'':33,66 ''ve'':74,84 ''wall'':52,102 ''way'':70 ''work'':68'::tsvector, '{"text":"How do we bring them down so that we can conquer this city? We''ll see that in this chapter. But metaphorically, what do we do when someone seems closed off to us? When we''re trying to share with them our testimony or our faith or our love, and the walls come up and there doesn''t seem to be any loose bricks for us to work our way through. If you''ve had a difficult time sharing the gospel, if you''ve had a difficult time bringing up how you feel about the truths of God, because of the walls of those around you. If none go out and none come in.","seq_end":1531,"t_end_s":5548.77,"seq_start":1522,"t_start_s":5509.085,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1564', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''battl'':58 ''bless'':98 ''canaan'':46 ''citi'':32 ''complet'':14,29,37,44,69 ''confirm'':102 ''conquer'':45 ''creation'':7 ''destroy'':38 ''done'':19 ''exampl'':100 ''faith'':80 ''feel'':90 ''go'':27,35,42 ''god'':77 ''good'':23 ''gospel'':66 ''great'':10 ''kind'':56 ''love'':85,95 ''metaphor'':61 ''number'':12 ''peopl'':72 ''plan'':59 ''presenc'':75 ''priesthood'':97 ''re'':34,41 ''saw'':5 ''seven'':2,53 ''share'':64 ''surround'':30,71 ''symbol'':11 ''total'':16,70 ''well'':24 ''whole'':15'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now seven, as we saw in creation, is a great symbolic number for completeness, wholeness, totality. It''s done. It is very good. Well, we are going to completely surround this city. We''re going to completely destroy it. We''re going to completely conquer Canaan. This has to be a a seven all in kind of battle plan. Or metaphorically, as we share the gospel, can we completely, totally surround people with the presence of God, with our faith in him, with our love for them? Can they feel that''s what I love about priesthood blessings, for example, or confirmations.","seq_end":1582,"t_end_s":5716.16,"seq_start":1564,"t_start_s":5666.585,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1934', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''ago'':12 ''back'':103 ''better'':99 ''bring'':85 ''captain'':23 ''cucumb'':76 ''didn'':50 ''die'':102 ''drink'':63 ''eat'':58 ''egypt'':105 ''egyptian'':75 ''everi'':47 ''faith'':6 ''fear'':8 ''food'':56 ''forti'':10 ''happen'':31 ''host'':28 ''israel'':36 ''joshua'':2,13,29 ''kill'':92 ''leek'':78 ''like'':35,43,65 ''lord'':26 ''mister'':5 ''morsel'':54 ''murmur'':46 ''onion'':80 ''past'':73 ''peopl'':67 ''pine'':70 ''said'':3,14 ''shoe'':19 ''sound'':34,42,64 ''time'':48 ''took'':17 ''us'':86,93 ''wander'':40 ''water'':61 ''wilder'':39,90 ''would'':96 ''year'':11'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now Joshua said that? Mister faith over fear from forty years ago? Joshua said this who took his shoes off before the captain of the Lord''s hosts? Joshua, what happened here? This sounds like Israel from the wilderness wanderings. This sounds like those who murmured every time they didn''t have a morsel of food to eat or any water to drink. Sounds like the people that were pining over the past with Egyptian cucumbers and leeks and onions. And why did you bring us out into the wilderness to kill us here? It would have been better just to die back in Egypt.","seq_end":1944,"t_end_s":7003.325,"seq_start":1934,"t_start_s":6961.12,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#1945', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''annex'':29 ''assur'':90 ''best'':98 ''bring'':8 ''content'':15 ''crisi'':66 ''desper'':82 ''east'':21 ''even'':55 ''faith'':45,65,88 ''happen'':4,94 ''hope'':85 ''jordan'':23 ''joshua'':1,25,62 ''land'':33,40 ''level'':59 ''lose'':44 ''lost'':84,87 ''mighti'':61 ''moment'':80 ''peopl'':100 ''promis'':32,39 ''reassur'':52 ''rest'':89 ''someon'':56 ''stay'':18 ''struggl'':73 ''us'':9 ''way'':50 ''would'':6 ''wrestl'':75'::tsvector, '{"text":"Joshua, what''s happening? Why would you bring us here? We should have been content to just stay on the East Of Jordan. No, Joshua. That''s an annex to the promised land, but it''s not the promised land itself. Do not lose faith. In a in a way, it reassures me that even someone on the level of mighty Joshua had a faith crisis. And if any of you have struggled or wrestled with that, and in moments of desperation have lost hope and lost faith, rest assured that it can happen to the very best of people.","seq_end":1957,"t_end_s":7048.91,"seq_start":1945,"t_start_s":7004.045,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#2576', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''10'':63 ''afraid'':122,129 ''ahead'':27 ''better'':54 ''bring'':7 ''canaanit'':73,134 ''conglomer'':132 ''conquest'':60 ''continu'':61 ''faith'':14 ''famous'':65 ''feel'':32 ''fight'':78,107 ''first'':119 ''five'':72 ''freak'':115 ''friend'':38 ''gibeon'':80,109,111 ''gibeonit'':113 ''go'':26,106 ''god'':22,43 ''gonna'':105 ''good'':34,45 ''group'':70 ''hand'':50 ''israelit'':125 ''joshua'':62 ''king'':74 ''knee'':11 ''life'':6 ''like'':83 ''mayb'':137 ''minut'':86 ''miracl'':66 ''place'':55 ''re'':97,104,128 ''right'':36,41 ''say'':20 ''side'':94,100 ''submiss'':16 ''suppos'':89 ''truli'':19 ''trust'':24 ''unit'':76 ''us'':3,8 ''wait'':84 ''well'':58 ''whatev'':30 ''wherev'':5'::tsvector, '{"text":"This is us when wherever life brings us to our knees, and in faith and submission, we can truly say to God, I trust you. Go ahead and do whatever you feel is good and right. My friends, it is right because God is good. And being in his hands, there''s no better place to be. Well, the conquest continues. Joshua 10, a famous miracle. There''s a group of five Canaanite kings that unite to fight against Gibeon. It''s like, wait a minute, you were supposed to be on our side, now you''re on their side? And so they''re gonna go fight against Gibeon, and Gibeon, the Gibeonites are freaked out. We were, first we were afraid of the Israelites, now we''re afraid of these conglomeration of Canaanites, and but maybe more than just","seq_end":2591,"t_end_s":9459.426,"seq_start":2576,"t_start_s":9401.455,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#2908', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''back'':75 ''barnea'':45 ''book'':78 ''caleb'':15,55 ''came'':9 ''catch'':51 ''children'':6 ''concern'':39 ''didn'':65 ''die'':104,106 ''endur'':97 ''faith'':83 ''forti'':99 ''fourteen'':2 ''full'':81 ''get'':49 ''gilgal'':13 ''glad'':47 ''glimps'':53 ''god'':38 ''ignor'':91 ''jephunah'':19 ''joshua'':11,70 ''judah'':8 ''kadesh'':44 ''kenizzit'':21 ''kinda'':60 ''know'':107 ''knowest'':26 ''last'':57 ''lord'':31 ''lost'':61 ''man'':36 ''mose'':34 ''number'':80 ''one'':56 ''said'':22,32 ''sight'':62 ''six'':3 ''son'':17 ''spi'':74 ''thee'':42 ''thing'':28 ''thou'':25 ''time'':58 ''unfortun'':88 ''unto'':10,23,33 ''wonder'':102,103,105 ''year'':100 ''young'':73'::tsvector, '{"text":"In fourteen six, then the children of Judah came unto Joshua and Gilgal, and Caleb the son of Jephunah the Kenizzite said unto him, thou knowest the thing that the Lord said unto Moses, the man of God concerning me and thee and Kadesh barnea? So glad we get to catch a glimpse of Caleb one last time. We kinda lost sight of him, didn''t we? He and Joshua were the young spies back in the book of Numbers full of faith. We can do this. Unfortunately, they were ignored, and then they had to endure the forty years of wonder, wonder, die, wonder, die.","seq_end":2916,"t_end_s":10715.59,"seq_start":2908,"t_start_s":10678.585,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#2927', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''14'':2 ''40'':7 ''back'':47 ''barnea'':23 ''believ'':52 ''brethren'':59 ''brought'':31 ''caleb'':89 ''chapter'':1 ''deliv'':55 ''discipleship'':94 ''espi'':25 ''faith'':46,97 ''fake'':44 ''fledg'':96 ''follow'':75 ''full'':95 ''god'':53,79 ''heart'':40,67 ''kadesh'':22 ''land'':28 ''lord'':18,77 ''made'':65 ''melt'':71 ''mine'':39 ''mose'':13 ''nevertheless'':57 ''old'':9 ''one'':84 ''peopl'':70 ''realli'':50 ''rememb'':87 ''say'':6 ''sent'':19 ''servant'':15 ''seven'':4 ''thing'':85 ''us'':56 ''vers'':3 ''wasn'':42 ''went'':61 ''wholeheart'':93 ''wholli'':74 ''word'':33 ''worth'':86 ''would'':54 ''year'':8'::tsvector, '{"text":"Chapter 14 verse seven, he says, 40 years old was I when Moses, the servant of the Lord, sent me from Kadesh Barnea to espy out the land. And I brought him word again, as it was in mine heart. I wasn''t faking my faith back then. I really did believe God would deliver us. Nevertheless, my brethren that went up with me made the heart of the people melt, but I wholly followed the Lord my God. And if there''s one thing worth remembering about Caleb, it''s that. Wholehearted discipleship. Full fledged faith.","seq_end":2937,"t_end_s":10793.525,"seq_start":2927,"t_start_s":10755.01,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#2945', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''11'':50 ''40'':35 ''85'':4,30 ''age'':95 ''back'':8 ''come'':87 ''day'':58,64 ''didn'':101 ''even'':74 ''faith'':19,113 ''feel'':25,103 ''felt'':109 ''fire'':111 ''first'':38 ''forward'':120 ''go'':84 ''hadn'':90 ''land'':43 ''least'':99 ''lifetim'':11,17 ''like'':104 ''look'':7 ''m'':22,24 ''mose'':66 ''move'':119 ''old'':6 ''promis'':42 ''readi'':117 ''sacrific'':15 ''say'':48 ''sent'':67 ''servic'':13 ''slow'':92 ''spi'':39 ''still'':108,116 ''strength'':71,78 ''strong'':27,56 ''war'':81 ''year'':5 ''yet'':52'::tsvector, '{"text":"Here''s an 85 year old looking back on a lifetime of service and sacrifice, a lifetime of faith, and I''m I''m feeling as strong now at 85 as I did at 40 when I first spied out the promised land. It''s what he says in 11, as yet I am as strong this day as I was in the day that Moses sent me. As my strength was then, even so is my strength now. For war, both to go out, to come in. He hadn''t slowed down with age at all. At least he didn''t feel like he had. He still felt the fires of faith. He''s still ready to move forward.","seq_end":2954,"t_end_s":10868.66,"seq_start":2945,"t_start_s":10828.085,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3015', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''abl'':14 ''ago'':46 ''almost'':39 ''anakim'':112 ''back'':80 ''bit'':32 ''caleb'':23 ''chang'':30 ''cours'':69,106 ''d'':101 ''drive'':16,109 ''exact'':40 ''faith'':103 ''first'':49 ''five'':35 ''forti'':34 ''generat'':45 ''giant'':52 ''god'':71,86 ''haven'':28 ''long'':84 ''lord'':5,21 ''man'':58 ''old'':57 ''older'':75 ''re'':25,60 ''readi'':62 ''right'':26 ''said'':22,43 ''saw'':50 ''shall'':12 ''sound'':38 ''still'':61 ''take'':64 ''us'':97 ''well'':67 ''would'':93 ''year'':36'::tsvector, '{"text":"If so be the Lord will be with me, then I shall be able to drive them out as the Lord said. Caleb, you''re right. You haven''t changed a bit in forty five years. That sounds almost exactly what you said a generation ago when you first saw those giants. And now as an old man, you''re still ready to take them on? Well, of course, because God''s not any older now than he was back then. And as long as God''s with me now as he would have been with us then if we''d had faith, then of course I can drive out the Anakim.","seq_end":3021,"t_end_s":11127.75,"seq_start":3015,"t_start_s":11096.17,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3037', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''14'':34 ''1979'':8 ''ahead'':52 ''becom'':23 ''belov'':93 ''brother'':94 ''caleb'':14 ''call'':16 ''caus'':102 ''challeng'':51,80 ''channel'':11 ''chapter'':33 ''christ'':104 ''church'':21 ''confer'':9 ''excit'':63 ''faith'':30 ''feel'':41,66 ''fellow'':97 ''giant'':55 ''give'':73,77,83 ''great'':50 ''humbl'':72,81 ''inner'':13 ''joshua'':32 ''kimbal'':36 ''like'':25 ''lord'':71,88 ''man'':28 ''met'':59 ''mighti'':27 ''moment'':47 ''mountain'':76 ''octob'':7 ''opportun'':56 ''pledg'':85 ''presid'':35 ''prospect'':64 ''rest'':18 ''sacr'':101 ''said'':37 ''say'':68 ''sister'':96 ''unstopp'':3 ''us'':54 ''welcom'':61 ''work'':44 ''worker'':98'::tsvector, '{"text":"He was unstoppable. And in that October 1979 conference, he channeled his inner Caleb and called the rest of the church to become more like that mighty man of faith from Joshua chapter 14. President Kimball said, this is my feeling for the work at this moment. There are great challenges ahead of us, giant opportunities to be met. I welcome that exciting prospect and feel to say to the Lord humbly, give me this mountain. Give me these challenges. Humbly, I give this pledge to the Lord and to you, my beloved brothers and sisters, fellow workers in this sacred cause of Christ.","seq_end":3047,"t_end_s":11224.005,"seq_start":3037,"t_start_s":11176.325,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3048', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''accomplish'':26 ''ahead'':70 ''bless'':38 ''caleb'':60 ''climb'':81,101 ''direct'':18 ''discipl'':89 ''faith'':6,45,98 ''fear'':77 ''feel'':41 ''fellow'':88,90,94 ''final'':23 ''forward'':4 ''give'':62 ''go'':3 ''god'':9 ''guid'':16 ''hear'':59 ''holder'':95 ''israel'':11 ''kimbal'':43 ''know'':12 ''land'':34 ''lead'':21 ''like'':57 ''may'':92 ''mountain'':65,69 ''nelson'':75 ''pray'':83 ''presid'':42,74 ''promis'':33,37 ''purpos'':29 ''sens'':51,72 ''servant'':91 ''start'':100 ''still'':68 ''take'':79 ''thunder'':61 ''us'':19,22 ''word'':48 ''would'':54'::tsvector, '{"text":"I will go forward with faith in the God of Israel, knowing that he will guide and direct us and lead us finally to the accomplishment of his purposes, and to our promised land, and our promised blessings. Can you feel President Kimball''s faith In those words. Can you sense what it would have been like to hear Caleb thunder, give me this mountain. There are still mountains ahead. I sense in President Nelson no fear to take the climb. I pray that you and I, fellow disciples, fellow servants, may be fellow holders of that faith and start climbing ourselves.","seq_end":3064,"t_end_s":11272.07,"seq_start":3048,"t_start_s":11224.484,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3127', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''15'':106 ''16'':90,110 ''acknowledg'':8 ''actual'':75 ''around'':35 ''bell'':30 ''build'':39 ''canaanit'':49 ''chapter'':89,104 ''conquer'':15 ''conquest'':25,46 ''d'':116 ''david'':78 ''enough'':73 ''ephraim'':95,113,133 ''faith'':72 ''final'':59,61 ''first'':125 ''get'':76 ''go'':62 ''greatest'':24 ''ground'':20 ''harder'':13 ''hell'':32 ''inherit'':97 ''interest'':114 ''judah'':109,129 ''last'':57 ''leadership'':128,132 ''let'':92 ''ll'':81 ''might'':21,54 ''other'':17 ''place'':10 ''play'':101 ''polit'':127 ''pray'':65 ''re'':99 ''ring'':33 ''said'':6 ''see'':82,94,117 ''singl'':123 ''someth'':3 ''spiritu'':131 ''templ'':19 ''tribe'':122 ''two'':119,121 ''ultim'':45 ''valiant'':70 ''week'':87 ''well'':91 ''world'':50 ''zion'':37,41'::tsvector, '{"text":"There''s something to be said for acknowledging some places are just harder to conquer than others. And temple ground might be the greatest conquest of all. As the bells of hell ring all around it, Zion, the building of Zion will be the ultimate conquest in this Canaanite world of ours. It might be the last to finally to finally go, And I pray that we can be valiant and faithful enough to actually get there. David was. We''ll see that in a few weeks. Then chapter 16, well, let''s see Ephraim''s inheritance. We''re just playing through the chapters now. 15 was for Judah, 16 is for Ephraim. Interesting, we''d see those two those two tribes singled out first. The political leadership, Judah. The spiritual leadership, Ephraim.","seq_end":3141,"t_end_s":11567.885,"seq_start":3127,"t_start_s":11514.795,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3214', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''17'':55 ''art'':57 ''canaanit'':25,113 ''chariot'':30 ''chop'':16 ''countri'':9 ''cut'':96 ''drive'':110 ''even'':26,42 ''faith'':36 ''forest'':13 ''give'':1,5,10,19 ''god'':39,74 ''great'':59,63 ''hast'':62 ''hilli'':8 ''iron'':32 ''joshua'':50 ''land'':22 ''least'':66 ''ll'':71 ''lot'':80 ''mountain'':4,84 ''one'':79 ''outgo'':101 ''peopl'':60 ''power'':64 ''respond'':51 ''shall'':76,85,95,104,109 ''stronger'':43 ''thine'':87,106 ''thou'':56,75,94,108 ''trust'':72 ''vers'':54 ''wood'':92 ''would'':68'::tsvector, '{"text":"Give me this mountain. Give me this hilly country. Give me the forest. I can chop it down. Give me the land of these Canaanites even if they have chariots of iron because I have faith in a God that''s even stronger. That''s how that''s how Joshua responds to them. Verse 17, thou art a great people and hast great power. At least you would if you''ll trust in God. Thou shall not have one lot only, but the mountain shall be thine for it is a wood and thou shall cut it down. And the outgoings of it shall be thine for thou shall drive out the Canaanites.","seq_end":3221,"t_end_s":11910.811,"seq_start":3214,"t_start_s":11871.025,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb)
insert into lumen.search_index (kind, ref_id, collection_id, title, tsv, payload) values
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3374', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''45'':23 ''ahead'':19 ''beauti'':51 ''book'':55 ''came'':43,77 ''chapter'':61 ''could'':47 ''d'':12 ''end'':52 ''everyth'':5 ''fail'':25 ''faith'':100 ''figur'':85 ''give'':13 ''go'':18,84 ''god'':80 ''good'':30 ''hous'':39 ''israel'':41 ''kept'':81 ''land'':3 ''leav'':64 ''let'':96 ''lord'':34 ''moment'':74 ''ought'':27 ''pass'':45,79 ''place'':98 ''promis'':2,7 ''rest'':15,21,70 ''right'':66 ''sinc'':86 ''spoken'':36 ''still'':57 ''thing'':31 ''three'':59 ''told'':9 ''total'':95 ''trust'':93 ''unto'':37 ''us'':97 ''vers'':22 ''word'':83,90'::tsvector, '{"text":"The promised land is everything I promised. I told you I''d give you rest here, so go ahead and rest. Verse 45, there failed not ought of any good thing which the Lord had spoken unto the house of Israel. All came to pass. That could be such a beautiful ending of this book. We still have three more chapters, but to leave it right there and just rest there for a moment, it all came to pass. God kept his word. Go figure, since he is the word. Can we trust him? Totally. Let us place our faith in him.","seq_end":3388,"t_end_s":12613.53,"seq_start":3374,"t_start_s":12567.335,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3730', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''abl'':56 ''accord'':71 ''back'':63,91 ''bless'':67 ''blessed'':104 ''challeng'':98 ''come'':34 ''concern'':30 ''difficulti'':96 ''fail'':18,44 ''faith'':74 ''god'':28,79,114 ''good'':22 ''hath'':17,43 ''heart'':7 ''incred'':103 ''know'':3,108 ''life'':94,101 ''ll'':53,61,89,107 ''look'':62,90 ''lord'':26 ''love'':47 ''one'':15,41,81,111 ''pass'':36 ''patriarch'':66 ''phrase'':49 ''promis'':77 ''said'':116 ''see'':69 ''someday'':51,87 ''soul'':12 ''spake'':29 ''spoke'':122 ''thereof'':45 ''thing'':16,23,42,82,112 ''unto'':37 ''us'':86,121 ''utter'':58 ''withheld'':85,119'::tsvector, '{"text":"And you know in all your hearts and in all your souls that not one thing hath failed of all the good things which the Lord your God spake concerning you. All are come to pass unto you, and not one thing hath failed thereof. I love that phrase. And someday we''ll all be able to utter it. We''ll look back at our patriarchal blessing and see that according to our faithfulness and the promises of God, not one thing has been withheld us. Someday we''ll look back at a life of difficulty and challenge, but a life of incredible blessedness, and we''ll know that not one thing that God had said has he withheld from us.","seq_end":3741,"t_end_s":14021.345,"seq_start":3730,"t_start_s":13972.58,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3813', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''along'':15 ''alway'':111 ''amorit'':8 ''came'':101 ''chang'':55 ''choos'':44,69 ''church'':118,129 ''curious'':138 ''discipleship'':27 ''even'':122 ''ever'':21 ''experi'':41 ''faith'':98,114 ''feel'':131 ''go'':53 ''god'':5 ''hold'':88 ''household'':67 ''inconveni'':25 ''kind'':136 ''know'':108,123 ''life'':37,125 ''like'':132 ''likewis'':72 ''live'':35 ''lord'':61 ''m'':135 ''make'':46 ''member'':115 ''mind'':49 ''mine'':56 ''onto'':89 ''outsid'':126 ''pass'':11 ''plenti'':30 ''pray'':63 ''run'':39 ''said'':106 ''seen'':3,76 ''serv'':59 ''side'':82 ''struggl'':95 ''student'':93 ''tire'':22 ''ve'':2,10,75,110 ''way'':33 ''whole'':66 ''worth'':87 ''would'':130'::tsvector, '{"text":"I''ve seen the gods of the Amorites. We''ve passed through them all along with you. And if you ever tire of the inconveniences of discipleship, there are plenty of other ways to live your life. So run the experiment if you choose to. Make up your mind. It''s not going to change mine. I will serve the Lord. I pray that my whole household will choose to do likewise because I''ve seen what''s on the other side, and it''s not worth holding onto. I had a student once struggling in his faith, and he came to me and he said, you know, I''ve always been a faithful member of the church. I don''t even know what life outside of the church would feel like, but I''m kind of curious.","seq_end":3827,"t_end_s":14322.985,"seq_start":3813,"t_start_s":14271.2,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3915', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''12'':83 ''aliv'':16 ''altar'':92 ''ark'':106 ''confirm'':7 ''coven'':109,112 ''d'':42 ''decis'':9 ''ebal'':94 ''eye'':35 ''faith'':15 ''feel'':2,11 ''fire'':13 ''forgotten'':22 ''gerizim'':96 ''god'':6 ''hold'':45,51,54,60 ''jordan'':87 ''like'':43 ''look'':31 ''m'':50,59 ''may'':20 ''meantim'':25 ''mirror'':40 ''number'':74 ''one'':75 ''past'':77 ''pillar'':81 ''power'':4,66 ''revel'':76 ''river'':88 ''safe'':113 ''shelf'':73 ''shiloh'':102 ''someth'':65 ''stone'':84 ''tabernacl'':100 ''use'':38 ''within'':17,114'::tsvector, '{"text":"I feel the power of God confirming my decision. I feel the fire of faith alive within me. You may have forgotten in the meantime, but I have not. So look me in the eye. You can use any mirror you''d like, and hold on to what I''m holding on to. Hold on to what I''m holding you to. There''s something powerful about that''s again, that''s shelf number one, Revelation Past. That''s a pillar of 12 stones by the Jordan River. There''s an altar by Ebal and Gerizim. There''s a tabernacle at Shiloh. There''s an ark of the covenant with the covenant safe within.","seq_end":3925,"t_end_s":14693.936,"seq_start":3915,"t_start_s":14650.66,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3926', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''23'':36 ''24'':78 ''agre'':77 ''altern'':63 ''among'':48 ''anchor'':5 ''away'':40 ''crisi'':31 ''distract'':58 ''elimin'':56 ''even'':103 ''faith'':33 ''fall'':19 ''get'':59 ''god'':45,71,86 ''heart'':67 ''hold'':22 ''inclin'':65 ''invit'':107 ''israel'':73 ''joshua'':82,105 ''keep'':15 ''lord'':70,84 ''love'':97,102 ''mani'':4 ''may'':52 ''obey'':95 ''peopl'':76 ''point'':6 ''put'':39 ''respons'':99 ''rid'':60 ''rope'':17 ''said'':41 ''say'':80 ''serv'':89 ''sink'':10 ''still'':51 ''stone'':13 ''strang'':44 ''therefor'':38 ''thing'':28 ''unto'':68 ''vers'':35 ''voic'':92'::tsvector, '{"text":"We have so many anchor points that we can sink into the stone and keep our rope from falling. We can hold on to all of those things in any crisis of faith. In verse 23, now therefore put away, said he, the strange gods which are among you. There still may be a few. Eliminate those distractions, get rid of those alternatives, and incline your heart unto the Lord God of Israel. And the people agree. 24, they say to Joshua, the Lord our God will we serve, and his voice will we obey. I love their response, but I love even more Joshua''s invitation.","seq_end":3937,"t_end_s":14738.345,"seq_start":3926,"t_start_s":14694.335,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3947', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''backyard'':63 ''board'':118 ''brick'':79,94,133 ''california'':66 ''climb'':127 ''close'':123 ''confess'':55 ''could'':126,152 ''d'':137 ''day'':7 ''didn'':113 ''direct'':44 ''dive'':117 ''divers'':11 ''earthquak'':9 ''everybodi'':70 ''everywher'':17 ''faith'':16 ''fall'':39,41 ''feet'':100,145 ''go'':37 ''great'':110 ''ground'':148 ''grow'':67 ''hot'':74 ''hous'':83 ''jump'':153 ''know'':24,143 ''launch'':111 ''lean'':28,47 ''live'':4 ''look'':19 ''made'':106 ''mean'':98 ''neighbor'':88 ''occur'':33 ''place'':12 ''pool'':60,104 ''practic'':69 ''pretti'':122 ''re'':36,46 ''realli'':109 ''shake'':14,32 ''six'':144 ''southern'':65 ''swim'':59,103 ''thing'':22,26 ''time'':51 ''true'':54 ''walkway'':156 ''wall'':80,95,131,134 ''within'':99 ''yard'':85,90'::tsvector, '{"text":"Because we do live in a day of earthquakes in diverse places, of shaking of faith everywhere we look. But the thing I know about things that lean is that when shaking occurs, if they''re going to fall, they fall in the direction they''re leaning. Here''s a time for a true confession. We had a swimming pool in our backyard in Southern California growing up. Practically everybody did. It''s hot. And there was this brick wall between our house, our yard and our neighbor''s yard. And the the brick wall was, I mean, within feet of the swimming pool, which made it a really great launching. We didn''t have a diving board, but that was pretty close. And we could climb up on the wall, the brick wall and we''d be about, I don''t know, six feet off the ground and then you could jump over the walkway","seq_end":3957,"t_end_s":14824.825,"seq_start":3947,"t_start_s":14773.806,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3965', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''23'':65 ''ai'':105 ''anyon'':25 ''battl'':103 ''california'':16 ''came'':21 ''crisi'':93 ''day'':70 ''direct'':7,50 ''divers'':74 ''earthquak'':17,72 ''faith'':78,95 ''fell'':32,35 ''get'':60 ''gonna'':111 ''guess'':9,27 ''hit'':18 ''joshua'':79 ''lean'':4,47 ''m'':59 ''neighbor'':38,55 ''one'':12 ''place'':75 ''re'':86 ''right'':97 ''seem'':81 ''sens'':83 ''shake'':77 ''sorri'':54 ''southern'':15 ''struggl'':100 ''thank'':51 ''tumbl'':23 ''us'':53 ''vers'':64 ''wall'':20 ''wanna'':26 ''whose'':29 ''yard'':30,40 ''yeah'':33'::tsvector, '{"text":"But it was leaning in that direction. And guess what? When one of those Southern California earthquakes hit, the wall came a tumbling down. Anyone wanna guess into whose yard it fell? Yeah. It fell into the neighbor''s yard, not ours. Why? Because it was leaning in that direction. Thanks to us. Sorry, neighbors. Now what I''m getting at here in verse 23 is if in a day of earthquakes in diverse places and shaking faith, Joshua, he seems to sense what they''re up against. He had his own crisis of faith himself, right, when he struggled after the battle of Ai and what what are we gonna do?","seq_end":3977,"t_end_s":14915.905,"seq_start":3965,"t_start_s":14867.69,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#3978', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''altern'':44 ''arm'':92 ''best'':40 ''commit'':4 ''crown'':56 ''direct'':67 ''distract'':42 ''elimin'':41 ''faith'':31 ''fall'':85,88,95 ''fix'':51 ''gospel'':55 ''heart'':9,53,74 ''hold'':34 ''idea'':20 ''inclin'':61,72 ''know'':2 ''least'':60 ''life'':29 ''line'':101 ''ll'':87,94,104,110,116 ''long'':28 ''lord'':65,77 ''onto'':96 ''open'':91 ''place'':14 ''re'':23 ''right'':13 ''side'':98 ''struggl'':81,106 ''unto'':75 ''wonder'':111 ''worri'':113 ''yes'':33,102,108 ''yet'':50'::tsvector, '{"text":"I know your commitment is there and your heart''s in the right place, but do you have any idea what you''re up against in a long life of faith? So, yes, hold on to it. Do your best. Eliminate distractions and alternatives. But if you can''t yet fix your heart in gospel crown, can you at least incline it in the Lord''s direction? Because if you can incline your heart unto the Lord, then when you struggle and if you fall, you''ll fall into his open arms. You''ll fall onto his side of the line. Yes, you''ll be struggling, and yes, you''ll wonder and worry, but you''ll be with him.","seq_end":3992,"t_end_s":14967.575,"seq_start":3978,"t_start_s":14917.33,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A#4055', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Joshua: Choose You This Day', '''answer'':13 ''choos'':35 ''come'':68 ''constant'':46 ''day'':37,60 ''faith'':4 ''frequent'':72 ''god'':25,92 ''hand'':90,102 ''keep'':43 ''last'':18 ''live'':95 ''long'':2,6,20 ''lord'':41 ''make'':65 ''medit'':56 ''memori'':23 ''mouth'':71 ''night'':62 ''pillar'':77 ''power'':86 ''process'':106 ''rememb'':88 ''remembr'':47 ''serv'':39 ''set'':75 ''show'':99 ''stone'':79 ''sure'':66 ''take'':53 ''tend'':16 ''testimoni'':8 ''thing'':15,32 ''throughout'':103 ''upon'':57 ''us'':100 ''well'':9 ''whatev'':51 ''whole'':105 ''within'':84 ''word'':59'::tsvector, '{"text":"How long our faith? How long our testimony? Well, that''s the answer. Those things tend to last as long as our memory of God. And so will we do those things? Will we choose this day to serve the Lord? To keep him in constant remembrance? Will we do whatever it takes? Will we meditate upon his word day and night? Will we make sure it comes from our mouth frequently? Will we set up pillars of stones? Will we do all within our power to remember the hand of God in our lives? He''s been showing us that hand throughout the whole process.","seq_end":4067,"t_end_s":15227.751,"seq_start":4055,"t_start_s":15183.925,"episode_id":"unshaken-8SvK7L87o1A"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''back'':56 ''believ'':16 ''boy'':82 ''chapter'':72 ''come'':90 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cover'':66 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''eli'':85 ''faith'':10,44 ''find'':9 ''first'':70,74 ''friend'':53 ''halverson'':62 ''hannah'':79 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':61 ''last'':63 ''lord'':14 ''m'':60 ''man'':5 ''may'':21 ''met'':78 ''mine'':19 ''one'':38 ''ruth'':67 ''samuel'':75,83 ''seven'':71 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3,89 ''sought'':40 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':58 ''week'':64 ''welcom'':55 ''wick'':88'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends, and welcome back to Unshaken. I''m Jared Halverson. Last week, we covered Ruth and the first seven chapters of first Samuel where we met Hannah and the boy Samuel and Eli and his wicked sons.","seq_end":10,"t_end_s":48.245,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#490', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''21'':76 ''among'':48 ''continu'':15 ''cultur'':63 ''desper'':55 ''done'':7 ''driven'':45 ''ear'':90 ''els'':39 ''environ'':46 ''especi'':47 ''everyon'':38 ''faith'':28 ''fit'':57 ''futur'':22 ''generat'':51 ''god'':5 ''heard'':78 ''hearken'':100 ''king'':108 ''like'':37 ''lord'':93,96 ''make'':105 ''mani'':68 ''media'':44 ''obey'':73 ''past'':12 ''peopl'':84 ''re'':60 ''refus'':71 ''rehears'':86 ''rise'':50 ''said'':97 ''samuel'':77,99 ''social'':43 ''thing'':3 ''unto'':101 ''vers'':75 ''voic'':103 ''wanna'':35 ''want'':53 ''wonder'':67 ''word'':81 ''would'':14,25'::tsvector, '{"text":"All those things that God had done for them in the past and would continue to do for them in the future if they would only be faithful to him. But, no, we just wanna be like everyone else. And in this social media driven environment, especially among the rising generation that wants so desperately to fit in. We''re up against culture itself, and no wonder many of them refuse to obey. So verse 21, Samuel heard all the words of the people. He rehearsed them in the ears of the Lord, and the Lord said to Samuel, hearken unto their voice and make them a king.","seq_end":498,"t_end_s":2171.275,"seq_start":490,"t_start_s":2133.28,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#761', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''11'':61 ''alongsid'':42 ''amaz'':53 ''among'':79 ''anoth'':88 ''behold'':76 ''came'':64 ''come'':94 ''connect'':4 ''convert'':50 ''end'':9 ''experi'':47 ''faith'':20 ''find'':38 ''god'':6 ''good'':1 ''happen'':11 ''heart'':29 ''kish'':99 ''knew'':70 ''neighbor'':2 ''one'':86 ''pass'':66 ''peopl'':18,84 ''prophesi'':78 ''prophet'':81 ''right'':41 ''said'':85 ''saw'':74 ''son'':97 ''spirit'':26 ''surround'':16 ''testifi'':40 ''testimoni'':22 ''time'':73 ''touch'':27,33 ''unfold'':57 ''unto'':95 ''vers'':60 ''watch'':55 ''way'':31'::tsvector, '{"text":"Good neighbor''s connection with God. And what ends up happening, when when we are surrounded by people of faith and testimony, and when the spirit touches our hearts the way it touched theirs, then we will find ourselves testifying right alongside them. That''s the experience for you converts. It''s amazing to watch it unfold. Then in verse 11, and it came to pass when all that knew him before time saw that behold, he prophesied among the prophets. Then the people said one to another, what is this that has come unto the son of Kish?","seq_end":770,"t_end_s":3378.87,"seq_start":761,"t_start_s":3344.19,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1073', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''13'':50 ''ago'':96 ''ammonit'':92 ''apart'':59 ''armi'':110 ''attack'':88 ''back'':104 ''begin'':56,65 ''boast'':107 ''bright'':39 ''chapter'':49 ''choic'':3 ''doesn'':60 ''driver'':70 ''enemi'':87 ''everi'':31 ''faith'':45 ''fall'':58 ''first'':47 ''forward'':16 ''futur'':37 ''god'':25 ''help'':29 ''king'':79 ''littl'':94 ''live'':9 ''ll'':18,22 ''long'':41,63 ''look'':38 ''massiv'':109 ''move'':15 ''new'':86 ''philistin'':101 ''pray'':20 ''re'':103 ''reign'':76 ''samuel'':48 ''saul'':67 ''saw'':90 ''seat'':72 ''see'':54 ''sever'':81 ''start'':52 ''step'':32 ''take'':62 ''teach'':24 ''thing'':55 ''total'':11 ''way'':35 ''year'':82'::tsvector, '{"text":"But the choice is theirs, and how you live is totally up to you moving forward. I''ll be praying. I''ll be teaching. God will be there helping you every step of the way. The future looks bright as long as they are faithful, but first Samuel chapter 13, we start to see things begin to fall apart. Doesn''t take long. It begins with Saul in the driver''s seat. He''s been reigning now as king for several years. There''s a new enemy attacking. We saw the Ammonites a little while ago. Now it''s the Philistines. They''re back, and they boast a massive army.","seq_end":1083,"t_end_s":4759.14,"seq_start":1073,"t_start_s":4721.65,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1150', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''13'':63 ''come'':50 ''command'':77,85 ''could'':109 ''d'':49 ''done'':15,25,70 ''establish'':93 ''faith'':60 ''foolish'':71 ''forev'':98 ''god'':7,82,108 ''hast'':69,73 ''invit'':6 ''israel'':97 ''join'':9 ''kept'':75 ''kingdom'':95 ''lord'':80,91 ''need'':4,54 ''obedi'':61 ''offer'':17 ''patient'':59 ''problem'':37 ''sacrific'':18 ''samuel'':64 ''saul'':67 ''say'':65 ''thee'':86 ''thi'':81,94 ''thou'':68,72 ''told'':46 ''trust'':111 ''type'':106 ''upon'':96 ''us'':10 ''vers'':62 ''wait'':56 ''wasn'':39 ''well'':33 ''would'':89,101'::tsvector, '{"text":"And so I needed to invite God to join us And how is that done? Through offering sacrifice. And so it had to be done. And who to do it but me? Well, that''s the problem. It wasn''t you. It was me. I told you I''d come. I did. You needed to wait and be patient, faithful, obedient. Verse 13, Samuel says to Saul, thou hast done foolishly. Thou hast not kept the commandment of the Lord thy God which he commanded thee. For now would the Lord have established thy kingdom upon Israel forever if you would have been that the type that God could have trusted.","seq_end":1160,"t_end_s":5060.06,"seq_start":1150,"t_start_s":5023.325,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1171', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''19'':112 ''actual'':58 ''arm'':32 ''armi'':79 ''better'':29 ''closer'':7 ''consid'':103 ''continu'':21 ''could'':94 ''els'':52 ''equip'':30 ''fact'':102 ''faith'':13 ''fight'':88 ''fine'':53,60 ''get'':77 ''go'':83 ''god'':100 ''gonna'':37,48 ''got'':75 ''gotta'':87 ''heart'':3 ''help'':98 ''king'':42 ''littl'':6 ''m'':40 ''meantim'':57,65 ''much'':28 ''obedi'':15 ''pass'':49 ''patienc'':11 ''philistin'':25,90 ''say'':45 ''somebodi'':51 ''someon'':1 ''still'':18,95 ''suppos'':69 ''trust'':17 ''use'':96 ''ve'':74,86 ''vers'':111 ''war'':20 ''whose'':2 ''yes'':23'::tsvector, '{"text":"Someone whose heart is a little closer to his with patience and faith and obedience and trust. Still the war continued, and yes, the Philistines were so much better equipped and armed, so what are we gonna do? I''m the king now. You say it''s gonna pass to somebody else. Fine. But in the meantime actually, not fine. I but in the meantime, what am I supposed to do? And I''ve got to get my armies up and and going, and I''ve gotta fight the Philistines, and and I could still use the help of God. In fact, consider this what he''s up against in verse 19.","seq_end":1177,"t_end_s":5133.425,"seq_start":1171,"t_start_s":5099.175,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1212', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''12'':30 ''actual'':88 ''among'':82 ''arm'':8,68 ''auxiliari'':32 ''better'':75 ''church'':36 ''day'':97 ''faith'':46 ''follow'':4 ''hand'':60 ''haven'':66 ''insuffici'':63 ''iren'':21 ''joseph'':103 ''latter'':96 ''look'':12,24 ''lookout'':78 ''nelson'':15 ''oak'':18 ''play'':91 ''presid'':14,17,20,33 ''quorum'':27 ''saint'':98 ''see'':39 ''sharp'':51 ''shield'':44 ''similar'':7 ''smith'':81,104 ''spirit'':56 ''strong'':42 ''sword'':53 ''take'':2 ''testimoni'':101 ''us'':83 ''well'':71 ''wonder'':90 ''word'':94'::tsvector, '{"text":"It takes the followers to be similarly armed. So if we look at president Nelson or president Oaks or president Irene, if we look at the quorum of the 12 and auxiliary presidencies in the church and just see just how strong their shield of faith is and just how sharp the sword of the spirit is in their hands, that''s insufficient if we haven''t armed ourselves as well. And so we better have a lookout for the Smiths among us. Now here, there''s actually a wonderful play on that word for Latter day Saints who have testimonies of Joseph Smith.","seq_end":1220,"t_end_s":5321.185,"seq_start":1212,"t_start_s":5286.6,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1330', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''beat'':67 ''call'':39 ''care'':106 ''circumcis'':26 ''could'':64 ''coven'':33,49 ''david'':17 ''even'':111 ''faith'':72,76 ''garrison'':13,117 ''go'':9 ''god'':56,99 ''gonna'':8,19 ''israel'':58 ''jonathan'':74 ''languag'':22 ''lord'':87 ''may'':83 ''oh'':92 ''outsid'':47 ''philistin'':25,119 ''possibl'':66 ''re'':7,43,46,71 ''say'':5,44,80 ''side'':61 ''sign'':30 ''similar'':21 ''someon'':40 ''token'':35 ''troop'':120 ''trust'':97 ''uncircumcis'':16,24,41 ''us'':68,91,103,110 ''use'':20 ''way'':78 ''whole'':116 ''work'':89'::tsvector, '{"text":"And who does he say we''re gonna go up against? The garrison of those uncircumcised? David is gonna use similar language. The uncircumcised Philistines. Circumcision is the the sign of the covenant, the token. And so by calling someone uncircumcised, they''re saying, you''re outside the covenant. You don''t have the the God of Israel on your side. So how could you possibly beat us if we''re faithful? And Jonathan was faithful. The way he says it, it may be that the Lord will work for us. Oh, if we can just trust that God will be with us, then who cares who''s against us? Even if it''s a whole garrison of Philistine troops.","seq_end":1338,"t_end_s":5825.505,"seq_start":1330,"t_start_s":5788.46,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1382', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''20'':23 ''acr'':28 ''anoint'':84 ''away'':48 ''battl'':103 ''behind'':40 ''blown'':47 ''charg'':101 ''close'':31 ''combat'':20 ''could'':68 ''courag'':51 ''crown'':81 ''d'':97 ''david'':2,5 ''distanc'':8 ''faith'':54 ''famili'':73 ''fine'':77 ''front'':44 ''goliath'':4 ''half'':27 ''hand'':17,19 ''jonathan'':14,56,89 ''keep'':69 ''let'':79 ''like'':34 ''m'':46 ''maintain'':6 ''meanwhil'':13 ''pass'':87 ''person'':95 ''pick'':63 ''plus'':24 ''protect'':38 ''quarter'':32 ''safe'':7 ''said'':36 ''saul'':86 ''sling'':11 ''stone'':12 ''successor'':65 ''tri'':61 ''two'':21 ''type'':93 ''will'':99 ''within'':25'::tsvector, '{"text":"With David and Goliath, David maintains safe distance. He''s slinging stones. Meanwhile, Jonathan, this is hand to hand combat. Two on 20 plus within a half acre, this is close quarters. And like I said, his protection is behind him, not in front. I''m blown away by the courage and the faith of Jonathan. And if you were trying to pick a successor, how you could keep it in the family and do just fine, and let the crown or the anointing of Saul pass to Jonathan, He''s the type of person I''d be willing to charge into battle with.","seq_end":1395,"t_end_s":6103.1,"seq_start":1382,"t_start_s":6059.385,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1396', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''15'':3 ''21'':85 ''also'':32,111 ''among'':22,49,55,67 ''armi'':76 ''attack'':79 ''begin'':77 ''camp'':104 ''confid'':66 ''countri'':107 ''courag'':64 ''earth'':36 ''enemi'':51,57 ''even'':109 ''faith'':59 ''fear'':48,54 ''felt'':11 ''field'':21 ''friend'':69 ''garrison'':27 ''great'':43 ''hebrew'':88 ''host'':18 ''israelit'':117 ''jonathan'':123 ''least'':62 ''m'':5 ''massiv'':47 ''mean'':58 ''moreov'':86 ''one'':9 ''peopl'':25 ''philistin'':81,93 ''quak'':37 ''rank'':52 ''rest'':73 ''roundabout'':108 ''saul'':121 ''spoiler'':30 ''time'':96 ''trembl'':15,33,44 ''turn'':112 ''vers'':2,84 ''well'':83 ''went'':98'::tsvector, '{"text":"In verse 15, I''m not the only one who felt that. There was trembling in the host, in the field, among all the people, the garrison and the spoilers. They also trembled and the earth quaked, so it was a very great trembling. There is massive fear among the enemy ranks, and fear among the enemy means faith or at least some courage, some confidence among his friends. And so the rest of the army begins to attack the Philistines as well. Verse 21, moreover the Hebrews that were with the Philistines before that time, which went up with them into the camp from the country roundabout, even they also turned to be with the Israelites that were with Saul and Jonathan.","seq_end":1402,"t_end_s":6144.315,"seq_start":1396,"t_start_s":6104.14,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1418', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''back'':39 ''christ'':78 ''church'':57 ''come'':37 ''display'':88 ''either'':18 ''enough'':101 ''faith'':83 ''fortitud'':85 ''forward'':71 ''gospel'':75 ''halt'':21 ''happen'':35 ''hide'':10 ''hunker'':7 ''jesus'':77 ''jonathan'':87 ''kind'':5,81 ''live'':73 ''lord'':42,65 ''march'':70 ''mayb'':89,98 ''member'':54 ''opinion'':24 ''potenti'':52 ''power'':51 ''re'':3 ''run'':38 ''see'':32 ''show'':58,62 ''side'':19,44 ''start'':97 ''strength'':60 ''take'':92 ''think'':48 ''two'':23,93 ''us'':68,95 ''wanna'':15 ''well'':46'::tsvector, '{"text":"And they''re just kind of hunkering down and hiding out and don''t wanna be on either side. They halt between two opinions. And what do they do? When they see what''s happening, they come running back to the Lord''s side as well. I think there''s powerful potential if members of the church showed our strength and showed that the Lord was with us and marched forward and lived the gospel of Jesus Christ with the kind of faith and fortitude that Jonathan displayed. Maybe it only takes two of us to start. Maybe that''s enough.","seq_end":1427,"t_end_s":6246.59,"seq_start":1418,"t_start_s":6212.76,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#1428', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''allegi'':77 ''alreadi'':75 ''armi'':34 ''back'':84 ''battl'':68 ''chang'':76,83 ''come'':65 ''convict'':98 ''courag'':100 ''encourag'':47 ''exampl'':45 ''fact'':12 ''faith'':93 ''fight'':23,29 ''god'':105 ''group'':10 ''hide'':62 ''inact'':53 ''jonathan'':43 ''m'':37 ''mayb'':6 ''men'':18 ''need'':42,55 ''peopl'':2 ''place'':63 ''pop'':57 ''power'':96 ''quick'':81 ''quit'':26 ''re'':32 ''readi'':21,27 ''saul'':16 ''scare'':38 ''see'':89 ''side'':103 ''soon'':86 ''three'':9 ''worri'':5 ''would'':79 ''yeah'':13 ''yes'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"And people that are worried maybe there''s three groups in fact. Yeah. There''s Saul''s men that are ready to fight, but not quite ready to fight. Yes. We''re the army, but I''m scared. And they just need Jonathan''s example to encourage them. Then you have the inactive that needed to pop up out of their hiding places and come to the battle. Then you have those that have already changed allegiances, but would be quick to change back as soon as they see that there is faith and and power and conviction and courage on the side of God.","seq_end":1435,"t_end_s":6279.52,"seq_start":1428,"t_start_s":6247.07,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#2044', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''angri'':42 ''area'':78 ''book'':13 ''close'':93,111 ''david'':6,72 ''depress'':48 ''even'':38 ''evid'':17 ''express'':105 ''fact'':80 ''faith'':107 ''gift'':75 ''god'':95 ''heal'':65 ''heart'':36,68 ''help'':64 ''know'':4 ''lift'':60 ''lord'':29 ''mayb'':81,85 ''mean'':103 ''might'':52 ''music'':26,58,97 ''peopl'':39 ''power'':24,56 ''psalm'':10,15 ''rejoic'':30 ''revers'':84 ''see'':22 ''someth'':99 ''song'':33 ''soul'':62 ''struggl'':46 ''violent'':44 ''whatev'':50 ''wonder'':71,89 ''wound'':67 ''wrote'':7,19'::tsvector, '{"text":"We don''t know if David wrote all the psalms in the book of Psalms, but evidently he wrote some. We see the power of music. The the Lord rejoices in the song of the heart, and even people that are angry or violent or struggling or depressed or whatever it might be, there is power in music to lift the soul, to help heal the wounded heart. And no wonder David is so gifted in that area. In fact, maybe it''s reversed. Maybe it''s no wonder he''s so close to God because music is something that is a means of expressing that faith and that that closeness.","seq_end":2053,"t_end_s":8946.565,"seq_start":2044,"t_start_s":8905.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws#2054', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - 1 Samuel 8-16 - The Rise and Fall of Saul', '''analog'':25 ''bare'':86 ''bike'':42 ''build'':53 ''easiest'':49 ''energi'':91 ''exampl'':44 ''exert'':89 ''faith'':12 ''feel'':100 ''gear'':30,38,79 ''get'':64 ''ill'':16 ''lowest'':77 ''mental'':15 ''momentum'':55 ''mountain'':41 ''movement'':103 ''one'':50,83 ''peopl'':7,73 ''said'':71 ''see'':98 ''shift'':31,59 ''slowli'':52 ''sometim'':4 ''soul'':106 ''speed'':66 ''spiritu'':78 ''start'':46,96 ''struggl'':10 ''take'':35 ''talk'':5,19 ''use'':23 ''ve'':3,22,70'::tsvector, '{"text":"As I''ve sometimes talked to people that are struggling with faith or with mental illness and just talked about I''ve used this analogy before with you, the gear shift, that if you take all these gears on a mountain bike, for example, you start on the easiest one and slowly build some momentum and then you shift up to have to get some speed. And so I''ve said to people, what''s your lowest spiritual gear? What''s the one that you barely have to exert any energy at all, but you start to see or feel some some movement in the soul.","seq_end":2059,"t_end_s":8976.205,"seq_start":2054,"t_start_s":8946.646,"episode_id":"unshaken-ivzxaLpbZws"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''afterward'':142 ''amaz'':79 ''back'':58 ''bear'':115 ''believ'':16 ''book'':68,94 ''chapter'':75 ''come'':143 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cover'':66 ''cycl'':91 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''dizzi'':86,136 ''doctor'':106 ''earth'':13 ''especi'':81 ''exampl'':126 ''faith'':10,44 ''fall'':139 ''fast'':130 ''figur'':123 ''find'':9 ''first'':73 ''friend'':53 ''get'':113,135 ''go'':64 ''halverson'':55 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17,109 ''hope'':99 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':54 ''judg'':96 ''last'':83 ''lord'':14 ''m'':98 ''man'':5 ''materi'':80 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''one'':38 ''order'':107 ''pride'':90 ''re'':63 ''read'':120 ''recalibr'':111 ''right'':141 ''ruth'':70 ''samuel'':77 ''seven'':74 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''skater'':124 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''spin'':87,128 ''strong'':29 ''testimoni'':23 ''thou'':18 ''today'':61,101 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':60 ''ve'':119 ''week'':84 ''welcom'':57'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends. Jared Halverson here. Welcome back to Unshaken. Today, we''re going be covering the book of Ruth and the first seven chapters of Samuel. Some amazing material, especially after last week''s dizzying spin through the pride cycle in the book of Judges. I''m hoping that today is just what the doctor ordered to help you recalibrate and get your bearings once again. I''ve read that when figure skaters, for example, are spinning so fast, how do they not get dizzy and just fall down right afterwards?","seq_end":11,"t_end_s":66.04,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#83', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''among'':97 ''ancestri'':10 ''ask'':109 ''blame'':87 ''bottom'':133 ''challeng'':116 ''church'':98,101 ''common'':6,9 ''consid'':125 ''describ'':112 ''doctrin'':102 ''elsewher'':54 ''face'':96 ''faith'':75 ''food'':44 ''friction'':20 ''go'':53 ''gone'':121 ''heritag'':7 ''hold'':38 ''hope'':50 ''israelit'':26 ''leav'':92 ''member'':99 ''moabit'':23 ''noth'':32 ''often'':67,77,108 ''oh'':28 ''part'':15 ''peopl'':69 ''per'':103 ''problem'':114,130,135 ''se'':104 ''sometim'':58 ''stori'':83 ''struggl'':72 ''tell'':80 ''territori'':36 ''think'':61 ''top'':128 ''ve'':107,120 ''well'':29,63 ''work'':65 ''worri'':57'::tsvector, '{"text":"And so there is some common heritage, some common ancestry, but for the most part, there''s been some friction between the Moabites and the Israelites. But, oh well, there''s nothing in my own territory, to hold on to. There''s no food here, and and my only hope is to go elsewhere. I do worry sometimes when we think of well, I work so often with people who are struggling in their faith, and often when they tell me their stories, I can''t blame them at all for leaving because what they faced among church members, not church doctrine per se, not I''ve often asked when they describe their problems and challenges and what they''ve gone through, if they consider this a top down problem or a bottom up problem.","seq_end":96,"t_end_s":399.335,"seq_start":83,"t_start_s":350.365,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#378', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''abysm'':45 ''allow'':88 ''apart'':9 ''assuag'':77 ''blame'':27 ''coven'':96 ''done'':52 ''faith'':73 ''fall'':8 ''famin'':79 ''futur'':37 ''god'':75 ''greater'':72 ''hand'':55 ''hopeless'':33,34 ''isn'':18 ''israel'':67 ''left'':66 ''logic'':7 ''lord'':58 ''marri'':92,98 ''moabit'':99 ''naomi'':26 ''okay'':10 ''outsid'':93 ''part'':4,14 ''present'':42 ''quit'':20 ''rain'':83 ''realiti'':17 ''send'':82 ''someth'':48 ''son'':90 ''true'':21 ''ve'':51 ''wonder'':30 ''would'':76 ''wrong'':53'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s the part where the logic falls apart. Okay? That''s the part where the reality isn''t quite true. And so here''s Naomi blaming herself. No wonder she''s hopeless. Hopeless for a future for herself if my present is so abysmal because of something that I''ve done wrong. The hand of the Lord is against me. Was it because I left Israel? I should have had greater faith that God would assuage the famine there and send rain? Was it because I allowed my sons to marry outside of the covenant and marry Moabites?","seq_end":389,"t_end_s":1584.46,"seq_start":378,"t_start_s":1546.24,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#1183', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''accus'':42 ''affection'':80 ''believ'':38 ''better'':9,85 ''church'':100 ''didn'':36 ''differ'':25 ''els'':19 ''faith'':94 ''first'':48 ''friend'':61,104 ''job'':10 ''joseph'':31 ''left'':98 ''littl'':24 ''look'':22 ''love'':29 ''make'':45 ''manner'':81 ''much'':8 ''peopl'':35,88,95 ''proper'':78 ''rebuk'':13 ''reclaim'':74 ''reproach'':16 ''said'':33 ''say'':55 ''smith'':32 ''someon'':18 ''spiritu'':21 ''struggl'':91 ''thing'':53 ''think'':3 ''thought'':65 ''tri'':72 ''vision'':49 ''wrong'':68'::tsvector, '{"text":"And I think we can do a much better job of not rebuking and not reproaching when someone else''s spirituality looks a little different than ours. I love what Joseph Smith said when people didn''t believe him, and they accused him of making up the first vision and all these things. It says, They should have been my friends, and if I thought I was wrong, they should have tried to reclaim me in a proper and affectionate manner. We can do better at that. People that are struggling in their faith, people that have left the church, we can be friends.","seq_end":1190,"t_end_s":4457.45,"seq_start":1183,"t_start_s":4422.205,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#1406', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''begin'':84 ''care'':16,66 ''concern'':88 ''convers'':6,32,39,45 ''deriv'':93 ''determin'':51 ''els'':63 ''everyth'':62 ''faith'':81 ''field'':69 ''glean'':71 ''god'':34,60 ''good'':38 ''help'':50 ''hold'':10 ''horizont'':44 ''line'':27 ''meet'':74 ''often'':90 ''partner'':40,46 ''peopl'':75 ''rais'':86 ''side'':24 ''struggl'':78 ''thin'':3 ''thread'':4 ''vertic'':31 ''view'':54 ''whose'':68 ''world'':56 ''worldview'':13'::tsvector, '{"text":"And that thin thread of conversation is what is holding up your worldview. So be careful about who it is on the other side of the line. Are you having vertical conversations with God? That''s a good conversation partner. Who are your horizontal conversation partners? Because they will help determine how you view the world and yourself and God and everything else. So be careful in whose fields you glean. When I meet people that are struggling in their faith and they begin to raise their concerns, so often it''s derivative.","seq_end":1413,"t_end_s":5391.205,"seq_start":1406,"t_start_s":5357.405,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#1788', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''begin'':40 ''boaz'':82 ''case'':101 ''chapter'':28,33,57,58 ''citi'':106 ''come'':66 ''dead'':49 ''deborah'':98 ''end'':31,44,71 ''faith'':41 ''flip'':23 ''four'':59 ''gate'':86,103 ''glorious'':76 ''judgment'':92 ''like'':2,6 ''ll'':12 ''look'':1 ''mayb'':10 ''neither'':46 ''okay'':19,93 ''one'':47,77,79 ''palm'':96 ''place'':90 ''proactiv'':30 ''see'':13,62 ''side'':24 ''smell'':5 ''start'':26 ''stori'':65 ''submiss'':36 ''term'':18 ''total'':35 ''vers'':56,78 ''went'':81 ''wife'':4,8,17 ''work'':37'::tsvector, '{"text":"Look like a wife. Smell like a wife, and maybe he''ll see you in more wifely terms. Okay? But then the flip side, she starts the chapter with proactivity, ends the chapter with total submission. Works at the beginning, faith at the end, and neither one is dead because they both have the other. Verse chapter chapter four then, you see how the story comes to its to its end, and it''s a glorious one. Verse one, then went Boaz up to the gate. There''s the place of judgment. Okay? The the palm of Deborah. In this case, the gate of the city.","seq_end":1797,"t_end_s":6867.875,"seq_start":1788,"t_start_s":6829.09,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#1976', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''access'':54 ''account'':64 ''apart'':24 ''bibl'':30 ''citi'':46,98 ''consid'':67 ''coral'':108 ''discrep'':19 ''elkanah'':68 ''ephraim'':92 ''even'':75 ''everyon'':52 ''faith'':27 ''fall'':23 ''god'':14 ''gonna'':3 ''import'':5 ''inherit'':41,90 ''instead'':42 ''israel'':9,51 ''k'':99 ''land'':40,89 ''lead'':8 ''learn'':105 ''levit'':34,45,72,85,97 ''live'':86 ''mean'':107 ''name'':74,103 ''pearl'':110 ''penina'':106 ''person'':118 ''precious'':114,117 ''priesthood'':56,78 ''probabl'':93 ''problem'':60 ''prophet'':12 ''reconcil'':61 ''rememb'':32 ''scatter'':47 ''singular'':39 ''stone'':115 ''suggest'':76 ''thing'':79 ''throughout'':48 ''two'':63 ''within'':87'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s gonna be important as he leads Israel as a prophet of God. Now is this a discrepancy and are we falling apart with our faith in the Bible? No. Remember that Levites did not have a singular land inheritance. Instead, they were Levitical cities scattered throughout all of Israel, everyone had access to priesthood. There''s no problem reconciling these two accounts if we consider Elkanah as a a Levite. The name even suggests some priesthood things, but that he''s a Levite living within the land inheritance of Ephraim, probably in an a Levitical city. K? A few other names to learn. Penina means coral or pearl. This is a precious stone, a precious person.","seq_end":1980,"t_end_s":7671.18,"seq_start":1976,"t_start_s":7629.615,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2347', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''act'':8 ''ask'':62 ''but'':73 ''faith'':21,43,105 ''foot'':79 ''go'':85 ''god'':45,70,95 ''gonna'':66 ''good'':29 ''hand'':93 ''heart'':50 ''honor'':19 ''hope'':107 ''inspir'':17 ''knowledg'':11,25 ''leav'':67,89 ''lot'':6 ''m'':65,84 ''mouth'':82 ''pour'':48 ''put'':77 ''re'':38,61 ''recogn'':32 ''retreat'':87 ''see'':35,102 ''seem'':16 ''sorri'':71 ''submiss'':109,110 ''time'':14 ''total'':10 ''trust'':41,98 ''whatev'':56 ''without'':9 ''woman'':30'::tsvector, '{"text":"He''s he does a lot of acting without total knowledge, but this time he seems inspired. He honors her faith, not his own knowledge. This is a good woman. I recognize that. I see that you''re you have trust and faith in God and are pouring your heart out to him. And so whatever it is that you''re asking for, I''m gonna leave you with God. Sorry. I butted in here. I put my foot in my mouth. I''m going to retreat and leave you in the hands of God, and I trust that he will see the same faith and hope and submission submissiveness that I do.","seq_end":2352,"t_end_s":9256.945,"seq_start":2347,"t_start_s":9222.369,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2436', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''better'':23 ''bread'':58 ''children'':51 ''cross'':82 ''deliv'':101 ''faith'':77 ''feed'':54 ''finger'':83 ''get'':15,27 ''go'':11 ''god'':104 ''gonna'':3 ''heart'':85 ''hope'':79,86 ''life'':60 ''live'':19,31,63,91 ''lord'':34 ''m'':2,10 ''parent'':41 ''principl'':93 ''rais'':49 ''readi'':17,29,99 ''samuel'':8 ''stay'':4 ''tabernacl'':107 ''testimoni'':75 ''tri'':13,25 ''turn'':84 ''us'':21 ''water'':64 ''wean'':7,38,70 ''without'':20 ''yet'':24'::tsvector, '{"text":"I''m gonna stay here and wean Samuel. I''m going to try to get him ready to live without us, or better yet, try to get him ready to live with the Lord. Now that''s weaning for you. Parents out there, what are we doing to raise our children and to feed them on the bread of life and the living water so that we can then wean them off of our testimonies, our faith, and hope more than cross fingers, turn hearts. Hope that they will then live those principles on their own. Are we ready to deliver them to God at the Tabernacle?","seq_end":2450,"t_end_s":9645.835,"seq_start":2436,"t_start_s":9601.88,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2748', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''2021'':57 ''add'':20 ''advanc'':118 ''beauti'':46 ''begin'':111 ''bless'':60 ''bring'':33 ''coat'':27 ''continu'':47 ''eli'':59 ''elkanah'':61 ''entir'':104 ''faith'':38 ''give'':69,113 ''god'':93 ''gonna'':101 ''grown'':13 ''hannah'':52 ''inch'':24 ''interest'':116 ''kind'':43 ''know'':88 ''last'':102 ''lent'':80 ''let'':18 ''life'':105 ''loan'':77,98 ''lord'':68,83,110 ''love'':2,32 ''may'':108 ''much'':10 ''offer'':40,92 ''past'':16 ''relationship'':50 ''said'':66 ''samuel'':54 ''seed'':71 ''sew'':29 ''thought'':4 ''ve'':91 ''wife'':64 ''woman'':74 ''wonder'':8 ''word'':86 ''year'':17'::tsvector, '{"text":"I love the thought of this. I wonder how much he''s grown over the past year. Let me add a few more inches to his coat and sewing it with love, bringing it in in the faith, and offering it in kindness. Such a beautiful continuation of the relationship between Hannah and Samuel. And then 2021, and Eli blessed Elkanah and his wife and said, the Lord give the seed of this woman for the loan which is lent to the Lord. In other words, I know what you''ve offered God, and it''s a loan that''s gonna last his entire life. And so may the Lord begin to give you your interest in advance.","seq_end":2758,"t_end_s":10948.37,"seq_start":2748,"t_start_s":10906.694,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2903', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''35'':24 ''accord'':46 ''anoint'':78,119 ''appli'':83 ''branch'':11 ''broken'':21 ''build'':67 ''christ'':93 ''day'':3 ''die'':6 ''faith'':36 ''follow'':60 ''forev'':79 ''fulfil'':103 ''good'':27 ''grow'':15 ''heart'':53 ''hous'':71,113 ''instead'':58 ''jesus'':92 ''king'':94,96 ''lesser'':88 ''let'':14 ''lord'':97,99 ''mind'':57 ''mine'':52,77,118 ''news'':28 ''one'':2,42 ''priest'':37 ''propheci'':106 ''rais'':32 ''replac'':39 ''samuel'':85 ''scale'':89 ''shall'':5,44,74 ''sure'':70,112 ''talk'':109,116 ''ultim'':102 ''unfaith'':41 ''ve'':13 ''walk'':75 ''wanna'':108,115 ''way'':64 ''wild'':16 ''yes'':81'::tsvector, '{"text":"In one day, they shall die, both of them. Your branches you''ve let grow wild, and they will be broken off. Then 35, and the good news. And I will raise me up a faithful priest to replace the unfaithful ones that shall do according to that which is in mine heart and in my mind instead of following after their own ways. I will build him a sure house, and he shall walk before mine anointed forever. Now, yes, that applies to Samuel on a lesser scale. But again, Jesus Christ, king of kings, lord of lords, is the ultimate fulfillment of that prophecy. You wanna talk about a sure house. You wanna talk about mine anointed.","seq_end":2914,"t_end_s":11572.26,"seq_start":2903,"t_start_s":11528.24,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2915', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''anoth'':52 ''began'':110 ''begin'':17,73 ''boy'':36 ''came'':93 ''case'':34 ''chapter'':4,9 ''child'':41 ''could'':116 ''day'':85 ''demis'':55 ''dim'':113 ''eli'':48,57,100 ''end'':62 ''eye'':109 ''faith'':30 ''fulfil'':20 ''god'':26 ''hous'':59 ''immedi'':23 ''jesus'':3 ''juxtaposit'':53 ''laid'':102 ''lord'':46,80 ''minist'':43 ''one'':39 ''open'':89 ''pass'':95 ''place'':106 ''precious'':82 ''priest'':31 ''propheci'':16 ''rais'':27 ''rise'':68 ''samuel'':37,42,70 ''see'':13,118 ''shift'':7 ''term'':24 ''three'':10,75 ''time'':98 ''two'':5,64 ''unto'':44 ''vers'':38 ''vision'':90 ''wax'':112 ''word'':77'::tsvector, '{"text":"That''s Jesus. Chapter two then shifts to chapter three where you see that that prophecy begin to be fulfilled in the immediate term as God raises up a faithful priest. In this case, the boy Samuel. Verse one, the child Samuel ministered unto the Lord before Eli. So there''s another juxtaposition. The demise of Eli''s house at the end of two, and now the rise of Samuel at the beginning of three. The word of the Lord was precious in those days. There was no open vision. And it came to pass at that time when Eli was laid down in his place and his eyes began to wax dim that he could not see.","seq_end":2921,"t_end_s":11608.88,"seq_start":2915,"t_start_s":11572.5,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#2934', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''answer'':64 ''ark'':46 ''backdrop'':23 ''bed'':99 ''begin'':73 ''blind'':11 ''boy'':97 ''call'':60 ''creat'':75 ''eli'':1 ''els'':104 ''ere'':31 ''faith'':88 ''four'':29 ''god'':35,48,69,83 ''laid'':53 ''lamp'':33 ''littl'':96 ''look'':24 ''lord'':43,59 ''lost'':7 ''poster'':18 ''pride'':14 ''priest'':89 ''rais'':85,93 ''relationship'':77 ''samuel'':51,61,71 ''saw'':82 ''seer'':4 ''sight'':10 ''sleep'':56 ''someth'':103 ''spiritu'':9 ''templ'':40 ''three'':27 ''vers'':26 ''went'':36 ''yeah'':79'::tsvector, '{"text":"Eli was a seer who had lost his spiritual sight, blinded by the pride of his own posterity. So with that as backdrop, look at verse three and four. And ere the lamp of God went out in the temple of the Lord where the ark of God was. And Samuel was laid down to sleep, but the Lord called Samuel and he answered, here am I. So God and Samuel are beginning to create this relationship here. Yeah. We just saw God will raise up a faithful priest while he''s raising up this little boy from bed. Now there''s something else here.","seq_end":2941,"t_end_s":11687.74,"seq_start":2934,"t_start_s":11651.54,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-jMYk190JBys#3289', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - Ruth & 1 Samuel 1-7 - Women of Faith', '''28'':17 ''asap'':88 ''back'':13 ''bad'':61 ''botch'':47,107 ''canst'':76 ''chapter'':16 ''come'':28 ''d'':82 ''dermatologist'':87 ''describ'':21 ''deuteronomi'':15 ''earth'':9 ''egypt'':49 ''either'':56 ''emerod'':65 ''emirod'':6 ''faith'':33 ''god'':35 ''head'':84 ''heal'':79 ''itch'':73,111 ''know'':52,92 ''like'':22 ''lord'':41 ''man'':80 ''nasti'':106 ''plagu'':25 ''re'':31 ''realli'':94 ''scab'':69,109 ''smite'':43 ''smote'':3 ''sound'':59,60,105 ''sure'':104 ''thee'':44 ''thing'':99 ''thou'':75 ''warn'':39 ''whereof'':74'::tsvector, '{"text":"Now he smote them with emirods. What on earth is that? Now back in Deuteronomy chapter 28 when it''s describing like the the plagues that will come if you''re not faithful to God, here''s the warning. The Lord will smite thee with the botch of Egypt. Don''t know what that is either, but it sounds sounds bad. And with the emerods and with the scab and with the itch whereof thou canst not be healed. Man, I''d be heading for the dermatologist ASAP. I don''t know what really what any of these things are, but should they sure sound nasty? Botch and scab and itch?","seq_end":3295,"t_end_s":13161.235,"seq_start":3289,"t_start_s":13125.945,"episode_id":"unshaken-jMYk190JBys"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#0', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''back'':59 ''bank'':97 ''believ'':16 ''book'':76 ''come'':101 ''cometh'':6 ''confront'':36 ''could'':47 ''cover'':73 ''declar'':45 ''deep'':26 ''destroy'':42 ''earth'':13 ''either'':81 ''entir'':75 ''episod'':71 ''faith'':10,44 ''find'':9 ''five'':69 ''friend'':53 ''god'':94 ''halverson'':57 ''hello'':51 ''help'':17 ''hour'':70 ''insomniac'':83 ''jacob'':33 ''jare'':56 ''last'':65 ''leviticus'':78 ''lord'':14 ''lover'':89 ''m'':55,96 ''man'':5 ''masochist'':85 ''may'':21 ''mine'':19 ''near'':68 ''one'':38 ''shaken'':50 ''shall'':7 ''son'':3 ''sought'':40 ''strong'':29 ''surviv'':64 ''testimoni'':23 ''third'':100 ''thou'':18 ''true'':88 ''unbelief'':20 ''unshaken'':61 ''week'':66 ''welcom'':58 ''word'':92'::tsvector, '{"text":"When the son of man cometh, shall he find faith in the earth? Lord, I believe. Help thou mine unbelief. May our testimonies be as deep and as strong as that of Jacob, who, when confronted by one who sought to destroy his faith, declared, I could not be shaken. Hello, my friends. I''m Jared Halverson. Welcome back to Unshaken. If you survived last week, our near five hour episode that covered the entire book of Leviticus, you are either an insomniac, a masochist, or a true lover of the word of God. I''m banking on the third.","seq_end":13,"t_end_s":54.155,"seq_start":0,"t_start_s":0.64,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#57', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''abl'':72 ''book'':53 ''content'':94 ''decis'':82 ''disobedi'':96 ''distanc'':15 ''egypt'':17 ''enter'':74 ''entir'':66 ''even'':42 ''faith'':87 ''final'':71 ''forti'':8,23 ''generat'':67 ''get'':27 ''guilti'':108 ''half'':35 ''israel'':19 ''lack'':85 ''land'':76 ''leviticus'':55 ''look'':10 ''made'':62 ''map'':13 ''murmur'':90 ''often'':107 ''poor'':81 ''promis'':78 ''slow'':45 ''studi'':51 ''thing'':101 ''took'':7,40 ''wait'':64 ''walk'':25 ''well'':47 ''year'':9,24,32'::tsvector, '{"text":"It was on them that it took forty years. Look at the map. The distance from Egypt to Israel is not a forty year walk. They get there in about a year and a half. That''s all it took. And even that was slow because, well, they had to study the book of Leviticus too. But what was it that made them wait an entire generation before they were finally able to enter that land of promise? It was poor decisions. It was lack of faith. It was murmuring, and it was contention and disobedience and all the other things that you and I are often guilty of.","seq_end":62,"t_end_s":274.055,"seq_start":57,"t_start_s":242.505,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#82', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''abl'':84 ''around'':31 ''assum'':42 ''band'':52 ''battl'':23 ''blow'':27 ''book'':9 ''conquer'':18,32 ''cri'':54 ''cross'':14 ''die'':78,80 ''enemi'':34 ''enter'':86 ''fact'':20 ''faith'':89 ''full'':87 ''god'':65 ''hard'':38 ''jericho'':25 ''joshua'':11 ''ll'':4,82 ''loud'':56 ''march'':30,51 ''parent'':41 ''problem'':92 ''see'':5 ''still'':104 ''trumpet'':28 ''trust'':64 ''us'':101 ''wander'':76,77,79,105 ''wasn'':35,95 ''won'':48,72 ''would'':44 ''yes'':12,16'::tsvector, '{"text":"And as we''ll see in in the book of Joshua, yes, they cross, and yes, they conquer. In fact, with the battle of Jericho, they blow trumpets and march around. Conquering the enemy wasn''t as hard as their parents assumed it would be. They they won with the marching band, for crying out loud. Now if we can if we can trust God in all of this, then we won''t have to wander, wander, die, wander, die. We''ll be able to enter full of faith. And the problem is it wasn''t just them, it''s us that''s still wandering.","seq_end":90,"t_end_s":388.745,"seq_start":82,"t_start_s":355.235,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#222', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''arm'':18,43 ''bicep'':9 ''casualti'':129 ''census'':34 ''could'':22 ''david'':116 ''faith'':113 ''flesh'':20,45 ''god'':63,119 ''hous'':123 ''israel'':125 ''king'':115 ''know'':36 ''laps'':111 ''later'':102 ''level'':39 ''ll'':99 ''long'':79 ''m'':82 ''measur'':7 ''much'':5,14 ''number'':59,68,73 ''one'':67,74 ''part'':118 ''plagu'':121 ''problem'':31 ''punish'':108 ''put'':23 ''see'':11,27,100 ''side'':85 ''strength'':15 ''suffici'':58 ''trust'':25,52 ''worri'':3 ''yet'':61'::tsvector, '{"text":"and not worrying so much about measuring his biceps to see just how much strength in the arm of flesh he could put his trust in. See, that''s the problem with the census. I know the the level of of the arm of flesh that I have. I I can trust in that if I have sufficient numbers. And yet for God, there''s only one number, and it''s the number one. It''s him. As long as I''m on your side, then there are more that be with you than be with them. We''ll see that later. And so as a as punishment for that lapse of faith on King David''s part, God does plague the house of Israel, and there are casualties.","seq_end":230,"t_end_s":964.92,"seq_start":222,"t_start_s":924.1,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#231', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''16'':94 ''30'':92 ''also'':58 ''armor'':74 ''aton'':66,109 ''back'':26 ''census'':39 ''chapter'':91 ''command'':50,59 ''consider'':13 ''david'':8 ''even'':96 ''exodus'':28,90 ''faith'':17,22 ''go'':34,79 ''god'':24,76 ''gonna'':44 ''good'':115 ''import'':46 ''instead'':20 ''king'':7 ''m'':57 ''make'':37,64 ''money'':104,110 ''number'':4,19 ''okay'':119 ''pay'':67 ''place'':84 ''price'':69 ''put'':16 ''ransom'':62,122 ''re'':30,33,78 ''reach'':9 ''real'':86 ''shall'':106 ''someday'':36 ''take'':107 ''tell'':97 ''thou'':105 ''told'':31 ''trace'':83 ''trust'':87 ''vers'':93 ''went'':11 ''whatev'':2 ''word'':116 ''yes'':41'::tsvector, '{"text":"That whatever the number was that King David reached, it went down considerably because he put faith in numbers instead of faith in God. So back in Exodus, they''re told, you''re going to someday make a census, and yes, it''s gonna be important, and I will command you to do so, but I''m also commanding you to ransom yourselves. Make an atonement. Pay a price because it''s the armor of God you''re going to have to trace place your real trust in. In Exodus chapter 30 verse 16, he even tells them what to do with that money. Thou shall take the atonement money. How''s that a good word for it? Okay. This is ransom.","seq_end":241,"t_end_s":1006.805,"seq_start":231,"t_start_s":965.32,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#884', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''barley'':36 ''bitter'':95 ''call'':69 ''cannot'':9 ''caus'':114 ''causeth'':98 ''curs'':100 ''dust'':109 ''faith'':84 ''floor'':113 ''frankincens'':42 ''god'':14,78 ''hand'':31,93 ''head'':7 ''hide'':10 ''hold'':46 ''holi'':104 ''jealous'':77 ''jealousi'':60 ''judg'':74 ''memori'':28,51 ''mix'':107 ''offer'':26,34,61 ''oil'':39 ''priest'':88 ''put'':24 ''re'':44,72 ''rememb'':54 ''repent'':23 ''shall'':89 ''sin'':12,56 ''tabernacl'':112 ''thing'':67 ''unaton'':19 ''uncov'':3,18 ''unless'':21 ''us'':81 ''want'':80 ''water'':96,105 ''whole'':66 ''woman'':5'::tsvector, '{"text":"He will uncover the woman''s head. You cannot hide your sins from God. You are now uncovered, unatoned for unless you repent. Put the offering of memorial in her hands. So that offering of barley with no oil and no frankincense. You''re now holding it. It''s a memorial. Do you remember your sins? Which is the jealousy offering. That''s what this whole thing is called. And they''re being judged by a jealous God that wants us to be faithful to him. The priest shall have in his hand the bitter water that causeth the curse. That''s the holy water now mixed with dust from the Tabernacle floor.","seq_end":894,"t_end_s":3441.9,"seq_start":884,"t_start_s":3401.565,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#955', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''accept'':29 ''amen'':26,27 ''babi'':46 ''belli'':96 ''belong'':11,47 ''chapter'':62 ''child'':10 ''conceiv'':2,42 ''faith'':24 ''first'':73 ''go'':88 ''god'':86 ''guilti'':99 ''head'':66 ''hide'':106 ''husband'':16 ''investig'':33 ''jealous'':15 ''know'':7 ''look'':59 ''odd'':72 ''oh'':1 ''okay'':35 ''parti'':100 ''realli'':71,87 ''result'':31 ''rot'':90 ''said'':68 ''scratch'':64 ''second'':77 ''seed'':3,43 ''show'':34 ''sin'':108 ''swell'':94 ''thigh'':92 ''tri'':104 ''true'':25 ''trust'':38 ''unfaith'':55 ''well'':19 ''whatev'':30 ''wife'':51 ''work'':84 ''worri'':18 ''would'':17'::tsvector, '{"text":"Oh, conceiving seed. How do I know if this child belongs to me? A jealous husband would worry. Well, if she has been faithful. True. Amen. Amen. I accept whatever results this investigation shows. Okay. You can trust now as she conceives seed that that baby belongs to you. Your wife has not been unfaithful. Now some have looked at this chapter and scratched their head and said, this is really odd, first of all. But second of all, does it does it work? Is God really going to rot the thigh and swell the belly of this guilty party if she''s trying to hide her sin?","seq_end":965,"t_end_s":3680.175,"seq_start":955,"t_start_s":3641.08,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1207', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''also'':3 ''amaz'':78 ''bless'':52 ''choos'':41 ''continu'':45 ''courag'':94 ''death'':14,70 ''differ'':11 ''etern'':37 ''faith'':96 ''field'':21 ''forward'':99 ''help'':54 ''know'':4,22,57 ''lift'':50 ''lost'':28,33 ''love'':29 ''make'':85 ''missionari'':6 ''move'':98 ''nobl'':75 ''occur'':65 ''one'':30 ''overcom'':61 ''peopl'':56 ''perspect'':12 ''power'':92 ''preach'':46 ''re'':17 ''see'':26 ''sens'':86 ''separ'':63 ''serv'':48 ''sin'':67 ''stay'':43 ''would'':89'::tsvector, '{"text":"But I also know of missionaries that have such a different perspective on death when they''re out in the field, knowing that they will see that lost loved one again, not lost to them, not eternally. And so they choose to stay and continue preaching and serving and lifting and blessing and helping other people know how they can overcome the separation that occurs through sin or through death. It''s it''s noble. It''s amazing to them, to me, but it makes sense how they would have the power and courage and faith to move forward.","seq_end":1214,"t_end_s":4658.89,"seq_start":1207,"t_start_s":4623.16,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1361', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''accord'':12,53 ''also'':6 ''altar'':35 ''ashon'':38 ''come'':10 ''dedic'':33 ''deep'':97 ''deeper'':67,69 ''enter'':61 ''faith'':108 ''first'':59,116 ''forward'':111 ''give'':120 ''go'':80 ''god'':102 ''got'':72 ''jewish'':8,55 ''judah'':23 ''kept'':65 ''later'':85 ''lead'':118 ''move'':110 ''na'':37 ''nostril'':76,82 ''offer'':30,90,123 ''one'':43,117 ''part'':48 ''princ'':18 ''process'':27 ''re'':79 ''red'':50 ''sacrific'':31,125 ''sea'':51 ''see'':81 ''servic'':100 ''start'':25 ''talk'':46 ''text'':15 ''today'':84 ''tradit'':9,56 ''tribe'':21 ''wade'':66 ''water'':63 ''way'':3 ''well'':77'::tsvector, '{"text":"By the way, this is also where Jewish tradition comes in. According to the text here, the prince of the tribe of Judah who started the process of of offering sacrifice to dedicate the altar was Na''ashon. And he''s the one when we talked about parting the Red Sea, that according to Jewish tradition was the first to enter the water and kept wading deeper and deeper until it got up to the nostrils. Well, we''re going see nostrils again today later. But here he''s offering he''s he''s just as deep in his service of God as he was in his faith to move forward. And he''s the first one leading out, giving these these offerings and sacrifices.","seq_end":1368,"t_end_s":5289.215,"seq_start":1361,"t_start_s":5249.185,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1515', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''14'':94 ''also'':30 ''among'':116 ''apart'':9,83 ''appli'':108 ''author'':17,24,68 ''bless'':86 ''call'':53 ''children'':118 ''come'':33 ''communiti'':36 ''direct'':91 ''faith'':73 ''give'':20 ''god'':3,26 ''guess'':106 ''hand'':5,59 ''israel'':120 ''keyword'':102 ''lay'':57 ''levit'':110,114,123 ''meet'':72 ''middleman'':78 ''middlewoman'':80 ''mine'':126 ''nazarit'':104 ''power'':22,31 ''priesthood'':16 ''receiv'':85 ''right'':12 ''saint'':38 ''separ'':98,112 ''servant'':11 ''set'':8,82 ''shall'':124 ''shalt'':96 ''strength'':88 ''support'':43 ''sustain'':49 ''thou'':97 ''thus'':95 ''ultim'':6 ''upon'':60 ''us'':21 ''vers'':93 ''well'':63'::tsvector, '{"text":"It''s God''s hand ultimately that sets apart his servants. Right? It''s that priesthood authority that that gives us power and authority from God. But there is also power that comes from the community of saints that is there to support them. I am here to sustain you in your calling, so I am laying my hands upon you as well. It''s as if authority from above is meeting faith from below, and this middleman or middlewoman being set apart is receiving blessings and strength from both directions. In verse 14, thus shalt thou separate, there''s our keyword for Nazarites. I guess it applies to Levites too. Separate the Levites from among the children of Israel, and the Levites shall be mine.","seq_end":1523,"t_end_s":5875.955,"seq_start":1515,"t_start_s":5828.89,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1832', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''11'':93 ''along'':88 ''amaz'':40 ''apart'':31 ''book'':22 ''camp'':65 ''chapter'':92 ''complain'':99 ''day'':48,50,77 ''drag'':51 ''eat'':74 ''everi'':76 ''experi'':38 ''faith'':17 ''fall'':30 ''far'':19 ''food'':71 ''gather'':70 ''go'':6 ''got'':54,61 ''great'':36 ''keep'':73 ''kind'':46 ''laman'':105 ''lemuel'':107 ''manna'':75 ''much'':16 ''number'':24 ''oh'':100 ''one'':95 ''outpour'':41 ''peopl'':3,98 ''pitch'':56 ''question'':10 ''see'':83 ''seem'':12 ''set'':63 ''spiritu'':37 ''start'':29,81 ''tent'':57 ''thus'':18 ''trek'':90 ''trial'':85 ''troubl'':87 ''ve'':33,53,60,68 ''vers'':94'::tsvector, '{"text":"To the people, that''s going to be the question. There seems to be so much faith thus far in the book of Numbers. Now is when it starts falling apart. We''ve had our great spiritual experience, these amazing outpourings, but now it''s kind of day to day drag. I''ve got to pitch tents, and I''ve got to set up camp, and I''ve to gather food and keep eating manna every day. And now you start to see some trials and troubles along the trek in chapter 11. Verse one, when the people complained oh, there they are again, Laman and Lemuels all.","seq_end":1839,"t_end_s":7191.635,"seq_start":1832,"t_start_s":7156.555,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1840', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''among'':24 ''anger'':14 ''author'':113 ''away'':47,65,109 ''burnt'':23 ''camp'':37,77 ''catch'':38 ''central'':112 ''consum'':27 ''deal'':88 ''displeas'':2 ''faith'':101 ''far'':108 ''figur'':6 ''fire'':19 ''fring'':98 ''furthest'':46 ''go'':5 ''god'':67,115 ''head'':70 ''heard'':10 ''israel'':86 ''kindl'':16 ''like'':54 ''liter'':55 ''lord'':4,9,22 ''m'':83 ''mean'':79 ''okay'':87 ''part'':34,74 ''possibl'':117 ''speak'':61 ''spiritu'':60 ''still'':84 ''tabernacl'':50 ''technic'':80 ''think'':58 ''uttermost'':33,73 ''victim'':42 ''wander'':64 ''yeah'':81'::tsvector, '{"text":"It displeased the Lord. Go figure. And the Lord heard it, and his anger was kindled, and the fire of the Lord burnt among them and consumed them that were in the uttermost parts of the camp. Catch who were the victims? Those that were furthest away from the Tabernacle? That is most likely literal there. But think of, spiritually speaking, as we wander away from God, as we head to the uttermost parts of the camp. I mean, technically, yeah, I''m still in Israel. Okay? Deal with it. But can''t I be on the fringe of the faith? Can''t I just be as far away from the central authority of God as possible?","seq_end":1848,"t_end_s":7233.23,"seq_start":1840,"t_start_s":7192.35,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#1956', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''alon'':66 ''best'':120 ''biggest'':52 ''catch'':19 ''dirt'':27 ''eye'':32 ''faith'':106 ''get'':29 ''heavi'':77 ''know'':4 ''let'':80 ''look'':102,109 ''love'':115 ''lower'':9 ''merci'':113 ''mose'':12,88 ''need'':99 ''never'':91 ''okay'':96 ''one'':15 ''packer'':41 ''point'':10 ''presid'':40 ''problem'':38,53 ''pronoun'':23,48 ''say'':44 ''see'':83 ''use'':42 ''would'':68 ''wretched'':85'::tsvector, '{"text":"I don''t know if there''s a lower point for Moses than this one, but did you catch all of his pronouns? Some of this dirt was getting in his eyes because it was an I problem, as president Packer used to say. But the I pronoun, that''s the biggest problem of all. I can''t do it. I can''t do it alone. Why would you do this to me? It''s too heavy for me. Let me not see my wretchedness. It''s Moses. This was never about you. It''s okay. I just need you to look to me in faith and then look to them in mercy and love and do the very best that you can.","seq_end":1967,"t_end_s":7656.7,"seq_start":1956,"t_start_s":7617.02,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2205', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''angri'':22,31 ''anyon'':75 ''assum'':9 ''back'':77 ''care'':66 ''carri'':37 ''confirm'':41 ''danger'':7 ''els'':76 ''envi'':70 ''everyon'':87,95 ''faith'':43 ''god'':11,34,100 ''help'':14 ''isn'':12 ''less'':26 ''lift'':110 ''ll'':62 ''lowercas'':91 ''man'':116 ''mose'':80 ''natur'':115 ''next'':83 ''offend'':73 ''p'':92 ''perhap'':29 ''phrase'':69 ''prophet'':90 ''said'':81 ''sentenc'':84 ''spirit'':98 ''strengthen'':45 ''testimoni'':47 ''thing'':107 ''think'':3 ''trial'':18 ''turn'':63 ''upon'':101 ''us'':20 ''will'':53 ''wish'':86,94'::tsvector, '{"text":"But I think there''s a danger in assuming that God isn''t helping them through their trials and us being angry when they are less so and perhaps not angry at all. God has been carrying me through this, confirming my faith and strengthening my testimony through it all. He''s willing to do the same for you if you''ll turn to him. Careful with that phrase, envying or being offended for anyone else. Back to what Moses said the next sentence, I wish everyone was a prophet. Lowercase p. I wish everyone had the spirit of God upon them. It''s the only thing that''s lifted me up above my natural man.","seq_end":2217,"t_end_s":8655.585,"seq_start":2205,"t_start_s":8608.855,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2297', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''aaron'':109 ''abraham'':59 ''along'':79 ''assyria'':42 ''come'':67 ''connect'':63 ''convert'':9,43 ''could'':2,35 ''descend'':57 ''equival'':38 ''ethiopian'':8 ''fact'':91 ''faith'':46 ''fulli'':68 ''go'':24 ''god'':12 ''hous'':71 ''interest'':94 ''israel'':14,21,26,73 ''issu'':106,112 ''join'':17 ''joseph'':40 ''land'':30 ''line'':81 ''mention'':119 ''midianit'':54 ''miriam'':102 ''mose'':48,76 ''noth'':85 ''peopl'':19 ''promis'':29 ''realli'':66 ''remarri'':78 ''second'':120 ''spiritu'':89 ''want'':15 ''way'':33 ''well'':4 ''wonder'':97 ''would'':99,101 ''wrong'':86 ''zipporah'':50'::tsvector, '{"text":"It could very well have been an Ethiopian convert to the God of Israel, wanting to join the people of Israel off to go to Israel as a promised land. In some ways this could be the equivalent of Joseph and Assyria, convert to the faith. Or Moses and Zipporah, who''s a Midianite, that''s descended from Abraham, there''s some connection, but to really come fully into the house of Israel. And if Moses is remarried along those lines, then there''s nothing wrong with this spiritually. In fact, what''s interesting is I wonder why would why would Miriam have such an issue with this? Aaron has an issue with it too, but he is mentioned second.","seq_end":2306,"t_end_s":9040.431,"seq_start":2297,"t_start_s":8997.035,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2357', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''admit'':20 ''anyth'':66 ''aren'':116 ''bring'':112 ''command'':15 ''concern'':90 ''doctrin'':83 ''done'':46 ''even'':42 ''fact'':9 ''faith'':58 ''feel'':123 ''find'':36 ''first'':13 ''found'':50 ''frustrat'':5 ''histor'':77 ''implic'':94 ''insecur'':132 ''instead'':18 ''interest'':102 ''issu'':78,84,114,120 ''justifi'':127 ''like'':124 ''look'':30 ''m'':92 ''mayb'':1 ''noth'':47 ''often'':59 ''peopl'':53 ''pick'':40,108 ''project'':128 ''re'':11,29 ''realiz'':23 ''realli'':4,118 ''see'':104 ''social'':89 ''someth'':37 ''sometim'':106 ''struggl'':55 ''thing'':110 ''though'':43 ''tri'':34 ''ve'':45 ''want'':63 ''weak'':25 ''wrong'':48'::tsvector, '{"text":"Maybe what''s really frustrating you is the fact you''re not first in command. And so instead of admitting that and realizing that weakness in yourself, you''re looking at me and trying to find something you can pick at, even though I''ve done nothing wrong. I found that when people are struggling in their faith, often they don''t want to have anything to do with them, and so it''s just a historical issue. It''s just a doctrinal issue. It''s just some social concern. I''m not implicated in any of this. But it is interesting to see that sometimes we pick at things or bring up issues that aren''t really the issue because it feels like a more justifiable projection for our own insecurities.","seq_end":2367,"t_end_s":9278.766,"seq_start":2357,"t_start_s":9233.03,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2413', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''among'':12,29 ''anyon'':61 ''appar'':112 ''bless'':81 ''dark'':115 ''dream'':50,75 ''even'':111 ''everywher'':19 ''faith'':98 ''god'':51 ''hear'':3 ''hous'':102 ''impress'':78 ''known'':37 ''lord'':33 ''make'':35 ''might'':85 ''mine'':101 ''mose'':16,92 ''mouth'':108,110 ''much'':60 ''open'':64 ''pretti'':59 ''priesthood'':80 ''prompt'':67 ''prophet'':11,28 ''reveal'':55 ''said'':2 ''servant'':91 ''seven'':89 ''speak'':45,107 ''speech'':116 ''spiritu'':77 ''thing'':71 ''unto'':38,46 ''vers'':88 ''vision'':42,73 ''want'':17 ''whatev'':83 ''word'':6'::tsvector, '{"text":"He said, hear now my words. If there be a prophet among you, and again, Moses wants them everywhere, so do I. But if there be a prophet among you, I, the Lord, will make myself known unto him in a vision. I will speak unto him in a dream. God can and does reveal his will to pretty much anyone who''s open to his promptings. And there''s things from visions to dreams to spiritual impressions to priesthood blessings to whatever it might be. But verse seven, my servant Moses is not so, who is faithful in all mine house. With him will I speak mouth to mouth, even apparently, not in dark speeches.","seq_end":2424,"t_end_s":9535.71,"seq_start":2413,"t_start_s":9494.76,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2551', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''12'':42 ''anyon'':28,49,54 ''ask'':39 ''birthright'':8 ''caleb'':71 ''east'':15 ''exodus'':109 ''faith'':73,75 ''fear'':84,86 ''forget'':91 ''give'':32,44 ''god'':24 ''happen'':95 ''hous'':22 ''interest'':1 ''joshua'':69 ''leader'':12,16 ''m'':37 ''magnific'':100 ''met'':53 ''never'':52 ''nine'':82 ''other'':60 ''part'':101 ''pleas'':48 ''polit'':10 ''power'':11 ''reason'':65 ''rememb'':56,79 ''someth'':89 ''stori'':106 ''surround'':20 ''tabernacl'':26 ''third'':35,47 ''tri'':30 ''tribe'':7 ''two'':6 ''understand'':93 ''ve'':51 ''wanna'':29 ''west'':19 ''would'':3'::tsvector, '{"text":"Interesting. It would be those two tribes. Birthright and political power. Leader on the East, leader on the West, surrounding the house of God, the Tabernacle. But anyone wanna try to give me a third? I''m not asking for all 12. Just give me a third, please, anyone. I''ve never met anyone that remembers any of the others, and there''s a reason for that. Because Joshua and Caleb had faith, and faith is to be remembered. The other nine had fear, and fearfulness That''s something to forget. To understand what happens here is such a magnificent part of the of the story of the Exodus.","seq_end":2569,"t_end_s":10129.64,"seq_start":2551,"t_start_s":10081.046,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
  ('moment', 'unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo#2577', 'unshaken', 'Come Follow Me - The Book of Numbers: Look and Live', '''20'':44 ''back'':109,119 ''bring'':51,118 ''build'':28 ''cannot'':104 ''come'':71 ''counsel'':41 ''courag'':50 ''cowardic'':92 ''crop'':16 ''cross'':111 ''faith'':99 ''fear'':106 ''forward'':102 ''fruit'':54,62,121 ''good'':49 ''hold'':107 ''ignor'':82 ''import'':40 ''isn'':93 ''kind'':26 ''know'':65 ''labor'':126 ''land'':8,57,76,117 ''live'':5 ''long'':2 ''materi'':29 ''move'':101 ''never'':79 ''okay'':84 ''overcom'':89 ''pioneer'':73 ''plant'':13 ''river'':113 ''scope'':74,114 ''see'':17,68 ''shall'':64 ''therein'':22 ''think'':34 ''ve'':78 ''vers'':43 ''way'':59 ''whether'':18 ''wood'':21 ''ye'':47,63'::tsvector, '{"text":"How long can we live off the land before we have to plant our own crops? See whether there be wood therein or not. What kind of building materials are we are we thinking about? And then the all important counsel in verse 20, and be ye of good courage, bring of the fruit of the land, that way by their fruits ye shall know them. You see, when it comes to pioneering, scoping out land you''ve never been to, ignorance is okay. This is how you overcome it. But cowardice isn''t. There has to be faith to move forward. There cannot be fear holding you back. So cross the river, scope out the land, bring back the fruits of your of your labors.","seq_end":2587,"t_end_s":10209.431,"seq_start":2577,"t_start_s":10165.665,"episode_id":"unshaken-ki0bTvQsaCo"}'::jsonb),
